# CraftLeveTalk
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Language: ru\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"X-Game-Version: 2026.09.15.0000.0000\n"
"X-Source-Language: en\n"

#. ja: あれ持ってきてくれた？
#. de: Hast du die Ware?
#. fr: Vous m'avez amené ce dont j'ai besoin<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Thanks!
#. column 38: Oh...
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:1:0:36"
msgid "Did ya bring it?"
msgstr "Принёс?"

#. ja: ありがとう！
#. de: Danke sehr!
#. fr: Merci<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Did ya bring it?
#. column 38: Oh...
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:1:0:37"
msgid "Thanks!"
msgstr "Спасибо!"

#. ja: 残念だよ・・
#. de: Hm ...
#. fr: Dommage...
#. column 36: Did ya bring it?
#. column 37: Thanks!
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:1:0:38"
msgid "Oh..."
msgstr "Эх..."

#. ja: あれちょーだい
#. de: Hallihallo! Hast du die Lieferung fertig? Immer her mit dem Zeug.
#. fr: Ah, voilà ce que je voulais<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Excellent!
#. column 38: Then get to it!
#. column 39: Would you like to make more?
#. column 40: If you change your mind, let me know!
#. column 41: Thank you for everything!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:2:0:36"
msgid "Have you completed the order?"
msgstr "Заказ готов?"

#. ja: さんきゅー！
#. de: Besten Dank!
#. fr: Super, merci<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed the order?
#. column 38: Then get to it!
#. column 39: Would you like to make more?
#. column 40: If you change your mind, let me know!
#. column 41: Thank you for everything!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:2:0:37"
msgid "Excellent!"
msgstr "Отлично!"

#. ja: そっか・・
#. de: Dann mal los!
#. fr: Je vois...
#. column 36: Have you completed the order?
#. column 37: Excellent!
#. column 39: Would you like to make more?
#. column 40: If you change your mind, let me know!
#. column 41: Thank you for everything!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:2:0:38"
msgid "Then get to it!"
msgstr "Тогда за работу!"

#. ja: お、まだくれるの？
#. de: Könnte ich noch mehr davon bekommen?
#. fr: Oh, vous m'en ramenez encore<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Have you completed the order?
#. column 37: Excellent!
#. column 38: Then get to it!
#. column 40: If you change your mind, let me know!
#. column 41: Thank you for everything!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:2:0:39"
msgid "Would you like to make more?"
msgstr "Сделаешь ещё?"

#. ja: じゃあ、もう一度こえかけてくれよ！
#. de: Na gut. Aber sag Bescheid, wenn du es dir anders überlegst.
#. fr: Bon, alors parlez-moi de nouveau si vous changez d'avis<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed the order?
#. column 37: Excellent!
#. column 38: Then get to it!
#. column 39: Would you like to make more?
#. column 41: Thank you for everything!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:2:0:40"
msgid "If you change your mind, let me know!"
msgstr "Передумаешь — дай знать!"

#. ja: もう十分、ほんとうにありがとう！
#. de: Vielen Dank für alles!
#. fr: Ça suffira. Merci<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed the order?
#. column 37: Excellent!
#. column 38: Then get to it!
#. column 39: Would you like to make more?
#. column 40: If you change your mind, let me know!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:2:0:41"
msgid "Thank you for everything!"
msgstr "Спасибо за всё!"

#. ja: リーヴを受けてくださった職人さんだね？<br>依頼の品は、用意してきてくれた？
#. de: Bist du nicht das Handwerker-Genie, dem ich letzthin einen Freibrief übertragen habe? Dann gib mal her, was du fabriziert hast.
#. fr: C'est vous l'artisan<if $gn4>e</if> qui a pris en charge le mandat<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Let me see here...<br>Hm... I believe this will do. Here is the payment promised.
#. column 38: I have nothing more to say until you've completed my order.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:3:0:36"
msgid "Here for the job, are you? Then there's no need for pleasantries. Show me your work."
msgstr "Ты по заказу? Тогда без церемоний. Показывай, что сделал."

#. ja: ありがとう！<br>あなたが信頼できる人でよかった。<br>さあ、報酬だよ。
#. de: Huh, erstaunlich. Auf dich ist ja Verlass. Dann nimm, was du dir verdient hast. Hier, bitte.
#. fr: Merci<nbsp>! J'ai eu de la chance de tomber sur une personne fiable comme vous. Voici votre récompense.
#. column 36: Here for the job, are you? Then there's no need for pleasantries. Show me your work.
#. column 38: I have nothing more to say until you've completed my order.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:3:0:37"
msgid "Let me see here...<br>Hm... I believe this will do. Here is the payment promised."
msgstr "Так, посмотрим...<br>Хм... Думаю, сойдёт. Вот обещанная плата."

#. ja: 弱ったな……必要な品物だから、<br>リーヴの依頼を出しておいたんだけれど。
#. de: Kann man sich auf gar nichts mehr verlassen? Ich habe geduldig auf deine Lieferung gewartet, und was hab ich davon?
#. fr: Mince, voilà qui ne m'arrange pas... J'ai pourtant émis un mandat pour ce travail...
#. column 36: Here for the job, are you? Then there's no need for pleasantries. Show me your work.
#. column 37: Let me see here...<br>Hm... I believe this will do. Here is the payment promised.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:3:0:38"
msgid "I have nothing more to say until you've completed my order."
msgstr "Пока не выполнишь заказ, нам не о чем говорить."

#. ja: あなたがリーヴを受注してくれた職人さん？<br>待っていたわ。品物の準備はできてるかしら？
#. de: Ah, da kommt ja meine Lieferung! Ein Glück! Hast du auch alles dabei?
#. fr: C'est vous l'artisan<if $gn4>e</if> qui a accepté le mandat<nbsp>? Vous avez préparé ce qui était demandé<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Excellent. You are to be commended, good <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if>. I believe this should be sufficient remuneration for your services.
#. column 38: Well, then. Take your time. I do not wish to see you sacrifice quality if it only means I save a few bells. You know where I will be.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:4:0:36"
msgid "Ah, you must be the adventurer the guild said they would send. I have been ever so eagerly awaiting your arrival. Might you have the delivery on your person?"
msgstr "А, ты, должно быть, тот самый искатель приключений, которого обещала прислать гильдия. Я так ждала твоего прихода! Заказ при тебе?"

#. ja: 品物をお届けくださり、感謝します。<br>今、報酬をお出ししますわ。
#. de: Vielen Dank. Du hast mir einen großen Gefallen getan. Hier, dein Lohn.
#. fr: Merci de m'avoir fourni ce dont j'avais besoin. Je vais vous donner votre récompense.
#. column 36: Ah, you must be the adventurer the guild said they would send. I have been ever so eagerly awaiting your arrival. Might you have the delivery on your person?
#. column 38: Well, then. Take your time. I do not wish to see you sacrifice quality if it only means I save a few bells. You know where I will be.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
#. macro: <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:4:0:37"
msgid "Excellent. You are to be commended, good <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if>. I believe this should be sufficient remuneration for your services."
msgstr "Прекрасно. Тебя стоит похвалить, <if $gn4>миледи<else>сударь</if>. Думаю, это достойная плата за твои труды."

#. ja: あら、残念。<br>依頼の品ができるのを、お待ちしておりますわ。
#. de: Noch nicht? Bitte beeil dich, es ist wirklich dringend.
#. fr: Ah, dommage... Je n'ai qu'à prendre mon mal en patience, alors.
#. column 36: Ah, you must be the adventurer the guild said they would send. I have been ever so eagerly awaiting your arrival. Might you have the delivery on your person?
#. column 37: Excellent. You are to be commended, good <if $gn4>lady<else>sir</if>. I believe this should be sufficient remuneration for your services.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:4:0:38"
msgid "Well, then. Take your time. I do not wish to see you sacrifice quality if it only means I save a few bells. You know where I will be."
msgstr "Ну что ж, не торопись. Не хочу, чтобы ты жертвовал качеством ради пары лишних монет. Ты знаешь, где меня найти."

#. ja: 連絡のあった匠の先生ですね？<br>お品の準備はよろしいでしょうか？
#. de: Ah, dein Kommen wurde mir schon angekündigt. Hast du mitgebracht, was ich benötige?
#. fr: Vous êtes l'artisan<if $gn4>e</if> que la guilde m'envoie, n'est-ce pas<nbsp>? Vous avez pu préparer ce que j'ai demandé<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Ah, yes, your success was never in question. The universe is pleased and grants you your reward.
#. column 38: Shhh. Hush, now. The Spinner has decreed your path. Craft away, my child. Craft away.
#. column 39: But wait... What is this I sense? A desire to craft more?
#. column 40: Could it be that the stars were wrong? Bah! I have a feeling you will be back, my child, and I shall be here waiting when you do.
#. column 41: A thousand thanks, my child! Until our paths cross again!
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 12 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 4 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 17 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:5:0:36"
msgid "Your arrival here this <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> was foretold in the stars. You have something to...deliver, don't you?"
msgstr "Звёзды предсказали, что ты придёшь сюда этой <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>ночью<else>утром</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>днём<else>ночью</if></if>. Ты что-то... принёс, верно?"

#. ja: すばらしい品です。確かに拝領いたしました。
#. de: Hervorragende Arbeit. Wirklich hervorragend.
#. fr: Quelle qualité<nbsp>! Merci, j'accuse réception de la commande.
#. column 36: Your arrival here this <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> was foretold in the stars. You have something to...deliver, don't you?
#. column 38: Shhh. Hush, now. The Spinner has decreed your path. Craft away, my child. Craft away.
#. column 39: But wait... What is this I sense? A desire to craft more?
#. column 40: Could it be that the stars were wrong? Bah! I have a feeling you will be back, my child, and I shall be here waiting when you do.
#. column 41: A thousand thanks, my child! Until our paths cross again!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:5:0:37"
msgid "Ah, yes, your success was never in question. The universe is pleased and grants you your reward."
msgstr "Да, успех твой был предрешён. Вселенная довольна и награждает тебя."

#. ja: ……お察し致します。<br>何か事情がおありなのですね？<br>我々は先生を信じます。
#. de: Sicher haben dich dringliche An<shy>ge<shy>legen<shy>heiten von der Ausführung des Auftrags abgehalten. Wenn du Zeit findest, bitte denk an uns.
#. fr: Je comprends, j'imagine que vous avez vos raisons. Une personne comme vous n'agirait pas de manière irresponsable.
#. column 36: Your arrival here this <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> was foretold in the stars. You have something to...deliver, don't you?
#. column 37: Ah, yes, your success was never in question. The universe is pleased and grants you your reward.
#. column 39: But wait... What is this I sense? A desire to craft more?
#. column 40: Could it be that the stars were wrong? Bah! I have a feeling you will be back, my child, and I shall be here waiting when you do.
#. column 41: A thousand thanks, my child! Until our paths cross again!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:5:0:38"
msgid "Shhh. Hush, now. The Spinner has decreed your path. Craft away, my child. Craft away."
msgstr "Тс-с, тише. Прядильщица предначертала тебе этот путь. Твори, дитя моё. Твори."

#. ja: ところで先生、まだお時間はありますか？<br>追加で依頼したい品があるのですが……<br>いかがでしょう？
#. de: Könntest du womöglich noch etwas Zeit für uns erübrigen? Ich würde ja gerne noch etwas in Auftrag geben ...
#. fr: Si vous avez encore un peu de temps à m'accorder, accepteriez-vous de me fournir une nouvelle fois<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Your arrival here this <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> was foretold in the stars. You have something to...deliver, don't you?
#. column 37: Ah, yes, your success was never in question. The universe is pleased and grants you your reward.
#. column 38: Shhh. Hush, now. The Spinner has decreed your path. Craft away, my child. Craft away.
#. column 40: Could it be that the stars were wrong? Bah! I have a feeling you will be back, my child, and I shall be here waiting when you do.
#. column 41: A thousand thanks, my child! Until our paths cross again!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:5:0:39"
msgid "But wait... What is this I sense? A desire to craft more?"
msgstr "Постой... Что это я чувствую? Тебе хочется сделать ещё?"

#. ja: 先生にも事情というものがありましょう。<br>お手すきのときに、また声をおかけください。
#. de: Es gibt Abenteuer, die auf dich warten? Dann komm bitte wieder, wenn du mehr Zeit hast, ja?
#. fr: Il est normal qu'une personne de votre talent ne soit pas toujours disponible, bien sûr... Si jamais vous vous libériez, cependant, revenez me voir.
#. column 36: Your arrival here this <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> was foretold in the stars. You have something to...deliver, don't you?
#. column 37: Ah, yes, your success was never in question. The universe is pleased and grants you your reward.
#. column 38: Shhh. Hush, now. The Spinner has decreed your path. Craft away, my child. Craft away.
#. column 39: But wait... What is this I sense? A desire to craft more?
#. column 41: A thousand thanks, my child! Until our paths cross again!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:5:0:40"
msgid "Could it be that the stars were wrong? Bah! I have a feeling you will be back, my child, and I shall be here waiting when you do."
msgstr "Неужели звёзды ошиблись? Ха! Чую, ты ещё вернёшься, дитя моё. А я буду ждать."

#. ja: この度は、誠にありがとうございました。
#. de: Ich danke dir von ganzem Herzen. Hoffentlich kreuzen sich unsere Pfade bald wieder.
#. fr: Merci beaucoup<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Your arrival here this <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>morn</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> was foretold in the stars. You have something to...deliver, don't you?
#. column 37: Ah, yes, your success was never in question. The universe is pleased and grants you your reward.
#. column 38: Shhh. Hush, now. The Spinner has decreed your path. Craft away, my child. Craft away.
#. column 39: But wait... What is this I sense? A desire to craft more?
#. column 40: Could it be that the stars were wrong? Bah! I have a feeling you will be back, my child, and I shall be here waiting when you do.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:5:0:41"
msgid "A thousand thanks, my child! Until our paths cross again!"
msgstr "Тысячу благодарностей, дитя моё! До новой встречи!"

#. ja: 首を長くして、待っていました。<br>依頼の品はできていますね？
#. de: Du bist wegen des Auftrags hier? Gut. Dann zeig mir die Ware.
#. fr: Ah, vous voilà enfin<nbsp>! Je n'en pouvais plus d'attendre<nbsp>! Vous avez ce que j'ai demandé<nbsp>?
#. column 37: A fine display of synthesis. I must extend to you my admiration and gratitude...in the form of a reward, of course.
#. column 38: Well, may the Builder watch over your endeavors. But remember, Black Rabbit Traders <i>also</i> appreciate promptness.
#. column 39: Now, if it is further employment that you seek, I would be willing to make you a similar offer for more of the same item. What say you?
#. column 40: Very well. You know where to find me, should you come to your senses.
#. column 41: My thanks, adventurer. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if>.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:6:0:36"
msgid "Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet."
msgstr "Мой заказ готов? Знаю, у вас, искателей приключений, дел невпроворот, но и у меня сроки поджимают."

#. ja: ああ、よくできましたね。びっくりしました。<br>では、これが報酬となります。<br>また、何かありましたら頼みますよ。
#. de: Lass mal sehen ...<br>Hmm ... Ja, das wird wohl genügen. Hier hast du deine Bezahlung.
#. fr: Oh, quel beau travail<nbsp>! Très bien, voici la récompense.
#. column 36: Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet.
#. column 38: Well, may the Builder watch over your endeavors. But remember, Black Rabbit Traders <i>also</i> appreciate promptness.
#. column 39: Now, if it is further employment that you seek, I would be willing to make you a similar offer for more of the same item. What say you?
#. column 40: Very well. You know where to find me, should you come to your senses.
#. column 41: My thanks, adventurer. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if>.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:6:0:37"
msgid "A fine display of synthesis. I must extend to you my admiration and gratitude...in the form of a reward, of course."
msgstr "Отличная работа. Позволь выразить восхищение и благодарность... разумеется, в виде награды."

#. ja: 早く、作ってください。<br>急ぎではない用件を、わざわざリーヴで<br>頼むようなことはしません。
#. de: Solange du hier nicht mit der bestellten Ware aufkreuzt, haben wir nichts zu besprechen.
#. fr: Que quelqu'un vienne m'aider, et vite<nbsp>! Si ce n'était pas urgent, je n'aurais pas émis un mandat exprès<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet.
#. column 37: A fine display of synthesis. I must extend to you my admiration and gratitude...in the form of a reward, of course.
#. column 39: Now, if it is further employment that you seek, I would be willing to make you a similar offer for more of the same item. What say you?
#. column 40: Very well. You know where to find me, should you come to your senses.
#. column 41: My thanks, adventurer. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if>.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:6:0:38"
msgid "Well, may the Builder watch over your endeavors. But remember, Black Rabbit Traders <i>also</i> appreciate promptness."
msgstr "Да пребудет с тобой благословение Строителя. Но помни: в «Чёрном Кролике» <i>тоже</i> ценят расторопность."

#. ja: 追加注文をお願いしたいのだけど、いかがかしら。<br><split " " 1><string $gs1></split>さんでしたら、<br>お茶の子さいさいでしょう？
#. de: Wenn du nach mehr Arbeit suchst, könntest du noch mehr für mich herstellen. Interesse?
#. fr: J'ai demandé une nouvelle livraison, est-ce que vous voudriez bien m'aider à nouveau<nbsp>? Je vois que vous savez travailler vite et bien...
#. column 36: Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet.
#. column 37: A fine display of synthesis. I must extend to you my admiration and gratitude...in the form of a reward, of course.
#. column 38: Well, may the Builder watch over your endeavors. But remember, Black Rabbit Traders <i>also</i> appreciate promptness.
#. column 40: Very well. You know where to find me, should you come to your senses.
#. column 41: My thanks, adventurer. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if>.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:6:0:39"
msgid "Now, if it is further employment that you seek, I would be willing to make you a similar offer for more of the same item. What say you?"
msgstr "Если ищешь ещё работу, могу заказать у тебя побольше того же товара. Что скажешь?"

#. ja: では、また声をかけてください。<br>個人的なお誘いでしたらお断りですけれど。
#. de: Also gut. Du weißt ja, wo du mich finden kannst.
#. fr: Bien, n'hésitez pas à revenir une autre fois. Enfin, si c'est pour m'inviter, c'est à voir.
#. column 36: Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet.
#. column 37: A fine display of synthesis. I must extend to you my admiration and gratitude...in the form of a reward, of course.
#. column 38: Well, may the Builder watch over your endeavors. But remember, Black Rabbit Traders <i>also</i> appreciate promptness.
#. column 39: Now, if it is further employment that you seek, I would be willing to make you a similar offer for more of the same item. What say you?
#. column 41: My thanks, adventurer. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if>.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:6:0:40"
msgid "Very well. You know where to find me, should you come to your senses."
msgstr "Что ж, как знаешь. Если одумаешься, ты знаешь, где меня искать."

#. ja: まいどどうも。<br>私の役に立つ冒険者は、いつでも歓迎です。
#. de: Ich habe zu danken. Du warst mir tatsächlich eine große Hilfe.
#. fr: Merci<nbsp>! Les aventuriers qui me rendent service comme vous sont toujours les bienvenus ici<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet.
#. column 37: A fine display of synthesis. I must extend to you my admiration and gratitude...in the form of a reward, of course.
#. column 38: Well, may the Builder watch over your endeavors. But remember, Black Rabbit Traders <i>also</i> appreciate promptness.
#. column 39: Now, if it is further employment that you seek, I would be willing to make you a similar offer for more of the same item. What say you?
#. column 40: Very well. You know where to find me, should you come to your senses.
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 12 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 4 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 17 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:6:0:41"
msgid "My thanks, adventurer. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>evening</if></if>."
msgstr "Спасибо, искатель приключений. Хорошего <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>вечера<else>дня</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>дня<else>вечера</if></if>."

#. ja: ほう、我が隊が依頼したギルドリーヴを<br>受注してくれたようだな。君の協力に感謝する。<br>さっそく依頼の品を調達してきてくれ。
#. de: Du hast also einen Freibrief angenommen, den wir ausgeschrieben haben, ja? Worauf wartest du dann noch? Bring mir die Waren, die wir brauchen.
#. fr: Ah, c'est vous qui avez accepté la requête de mon unité. Très bien, voyons un peu ce que vous nous avez apporté.
#. column 37: Yes, yes... This appears to meet Wood Wailer standards. You have my unit's thanks, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Let me prepare your reward forthwith.
#. column 38: My men and I require those supplies immediately. Every moment you tarry puts us in danger of being unprepared for an attack.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:7:0:36"
msgid "So it is you that accepted my unit's request. Very well, then. Let us see what you have brought us."
msgstr "Так это ты принял заказ моего отряда. Хорошо. Посмотрим, что ты нам принёс."

#. ja: うむ、まさしくこれは我が隊が発注した品だ。<br>その手並み……なかなかのものだな。<br>君の尽力に対し、我が隊を代表して礼を言わせてくれ。
#. de: Na, geht doch! Genau, was wir wollten, und nicht mal schlechte Qualität. Dann danke ich dir im Namen von uns allen.
#. fr: Je n'ai rien à redire sur la qualité, c'est de l'excellent travail. Vous avez toute ma recon<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ce.
#. column 36: So it is you that accepted my unit's request. Very well, then. Let us see what you have brought us.
#. column 38: My men and I require those supplies immediately. Every moment you tarry puts us in danger of being unprepared for an attack.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:7:0:37"
msgid "Yes, yes... This appears to meet Wood Wailer standards. You have my unit's thanks, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Let me prepare your reward forthwith."
msgstr "Да-да... Похоже, качество достойное Древесных стражей. От всего отряда спасибо, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Сейчас приготовлю тебе награду."

#. ja: ところで依頼の品はどこかな？<br>……な、なんと用意できなかったと？<br>次こそは、しっかりと頼むぞ……。
#. de: Wo sind die bestellten Waren? Na? Ich sehe hier nichts, was auch nur annähernd so aussieht. Jetzt mach dich aber mal ernsthaft auf die Suche!
#. fr: Moi et mes hommes avons besoin de la marchandise dans les plus brefs délais. Tout retard est susceptible de nous coûter la vie si nous subissons une attaque.
#. column 36: So it is you that accepted my unit's request. Very well, then. Let us see what you have brought us.
#. column 37: Yes, yes... This appears to meet Wood Wailer standards. You have my unit's thanks, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Let me prepare your reward forthwith.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:7:0:38"
msgid "My men and I require those supplies immediately. Every moment you tarry puts us in danger of being unprepared for an attack."
msgstr "Мне и моим людям припасы нужны немедленно. Каждая минута промедления может застать нас врасплох, если нападут."

#. ja: <string $gs1>だな。<br>話は聞いている、さっそくだが用件に入ろう。
#. de: Dich schickt die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde? Na ja, mal sehen, was du drauf hast.
#. fr: Ah<nbsp>! Vous devez être l'aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if> dont on m'a parlé... <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>, c'est ça<nbsp>? Bien, montrez-moi la marchandise...
#. column 37: Finished, are we? Let me take a look.<br>Yes... Yes... Very good. Very good, indeed. You have done a fine job today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. My superiors at the Consortium will be pleased, to say the least.
#. column 38: The Brugaire Consortium is known for the expediency with which it fills its orders. If you refuse to complete the items I have requested, I will simply hire another adventurer to do my bidding. Gods know there are more than enough of you running around this city to choose from.
#. column 39: And, I believe they would be even <i>more</i> pleased if I were to return to the warehouses with a healthy surplus of the requested goods. You seem competent enough in your chosen trade. Would you consider contributing a few more whacks of the proverbial hammer in service of Brugaire?
#. column 40: I see. Off with you then. I am a busy man, and my clients are waiting.
#. column 41: You have served the Consortium well. I shall duly note your contributions in my log. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if>, then.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:8:0:36"
msgid "From the Adventurers' Guild, are you? Very good, very good."
msgstr "Из гильдии искателей приключений? Прекрасно, прекрасно."

#. ja: よろしい、依頼どおりだ。<br>気に入ったぞ、<string $gs1>。<br>我が商会は信用を重んじる、約束の報酬を渡そう。
#. de: Fertig? Dann lass mich mal sehen ... Hm ... Ja ... Sieht gar nicht so schlecht aus, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. So kommst du mit dem Konsortium ins Geschäft.
#. fr: Hmm... C'est du bon travail. Oui, j'aime beaucoup ce que vous avez fait. Je ne manquerai pas de faire à nouveau appel à vos services dans le futur. Tenez, voici votre récompense.
#. column 36: From the Adventurers' Guild, are you? Very good, very good.
#. column 38: The Brugaire Consortium is known for the expediency with which it fills its orders. If you refuse to complete the items I have requested, I will simply hire another adventurer to do my bidding. Gods know there are more than enough of you running around this city to choose from.
#. column 39: And, I believe they would be even <i>more</i> pleased if I were to return to the warehouses with a healthy surplus of the requested goods. You seem competent enough in your chosen trade. Would you consider contributing a few more whacks of the proverbial hammer in service of Brugaire?
#. column 40: I see. Off with you then. I am a busy man, and my clients are waiting.
#. column 41: You have served the Consortium well. I shall duly note your contributions in my log. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if>, then.
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:8:0:37"
msgid "Finished, are we? Let me take a look.<br>Yes... Yes... Very good. Very good, indeed. You have done a fine job today, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. My superiors at the Consortium will be pleased, to say the least."
msgstr "Готово? Дай-ка взглянуть.<br>Да... Да... Очень хорошо. Действительно хорошо. Отличная работа, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Начальство в консорциуме будет довольно."

#. ja: 手段は問わん。<br>なるたけ急いで、ブツを用意してくれたまえ。
#. de: Das Konsortium lässt keine Aufträge unerledigt. Wenn du nicht liefern kannst, frage ich jemand anders, der mir die gewünschte Waren im Hand<shy>umdrehen herstellt. Arbeitswillige Handwerker gibt es genug. Also?
#. fr: Pressez-vous, le Consortium de Brugaire est réputé pour la rapidité avec laquelle il honore ses commandes. Si vous ne pouvez pas fabriquer les objets que j'ai demandés, dites-le-moi et j'embaucherai quelqu'un d'autre. Comme vous pouvez le voir, les aventuriers ne manquent pas par ici.
#. column 36: From the Adventurers' Guild, are you? Very good, very good.
#. column 37: Finished, are we? Let me take a look.<br>Yes... Yes... Very good. Very good, indeed. You have done a fine job today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. My superiors at the Consortium will be pleased, to say the least.
#. column 39: And, I believe they would be even <i>more</i> pleased if I were to return to the warehouses with a healthy surplus of the requested goods. You seem competent enough in your chosen trade. Would you consider contributing a few more whacks of the proverbial hammer in service of Brugaire?
#. column 40: I see. Off with you then. I am a busy man, and my clients are waiting.
#. column 41: You have served the Consortium well. I shall duly note your contributions in my log. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if>, then.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:8:0:38"
msgid "The Brugaire Consortium is known for the expediency with which it fills its orders. If you refuse to complete the items I have requested, I will simply hire another adventurer to do my bidding. Gods know there are more than enough of you running around this city to choose from."
msgstr "Консорциум Брюгера славится тем, что быстро выполняет заказы. Не хочешь сделать то, о чём я попросил, — найму другого искателя приключений. Богов ради, в городе их полно."

#. ja: なるほど、確かな腕を持っているようだな。<br>その腕を見込んで追加注文をしよう。<br>むろん、やってくれるのだろう？
#. de: Ich sehe, dass du dein Handwerk verstehst. Ich würde dir noch mehr davon abnehmen. Wie wär's?
#. fr: Ho, ho... Beau travail... Excellent travail, dirais-je même. Que diriez-vous de m'en livrer un peu plus<nbsp>?
#. column 36: From the Adventurers' Guild, are you? Very good, very good.
#. column 37: Finished, are we? Let me take a look.<br>Yes... Yes... Very good. Very good, indeed. You have done a fine job today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. My superiors at the Consortium will be pleased, to say the least.
#. column 38: The Brugaire Consortium is known for the expediency with which it fills its orders. If you refuse to complete the items I have requested, I will simply hire another adventurer to do my bidding. Gods know there are more than enough of you running around this city to choose from.
#. column 40: I see. Off with you then. I am a busy man, and my clients are waiting.
#. column 41: You have served the Consortium well. I shall duly note your contributions in my log. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if>, then.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:8:0:39"
msgid "And, I believe they would be even <i>more</i> pleased if I were to return to the warehouses with a healthy surplus of the requested goods. You seem competent enough in your chosen trade. Would you consider contributing a few more whacks of the proverbial hammer in service of Brugaire?"
msgstr "Думаю, начальство будет <i>ещё</i> довольнее, если я вернусь на склады с хорошим запасом товара. Ты, похоже, знаешь своё ремесло. Не хочешь ещё немного потрудиться на Брюгера?"

#. ja: ……まあ、よい。<br>最低限の数は、確保できたのだからな。
#. de: Na gut, dann lass mal gut sein. Ich habe ja, was ich brauche.
#. fr: Non<nbsp>? Bon, tant pis... Je ferai avec ce que j'ai.
#. column 36: From the Adventurers' Guild, are you? Very good, very good.
#. column 37: Finished, are we? Let me take a look.<br>Yes... Yes... Very good. Very good, indeed. You have done a fine job today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. My superiors at the Consortium will be pleased, to say the least.
#. column 38: The Brugaire Consortium is known for the expediency with which it fills its orders. If you refuse to complete the items I have requested, I will simply hire another adventurer to do my bidding. Gods know there are more than enough of you running around this city to choose from.
#. column 39: And, I believe they would be even <i>more</i> pleased if I were to return to the warehouses with a healthy surplus of the requested goods. You seem competent enough in your chosen trade. Would you consider contributing a few more whacks of the proverbial hammer in service of Brugaire?
#. column 41: You have served the Consortium well. I shall duly note your contributions in my log. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if>, then.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:8:0:40"
msgid "I see. Off with you then. I am a busy man, and my clients are waiting."
msgstr "Понятно. Тогда ступай. Я занятой человек, клиенты ждут."

#. ja: 気に入ったぞ、<string $gs1>。<br>我が商会は、信用を重んじる。<br>この働きぶりは覚えておこう……。
#. de: Deine Arbeit gefällt mir, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Ich werde mir deinen Namen merken. Bis zum nächsten Mal!
#. fr: Merci, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Vous avez rendu un grand service au Consortium de Brugaire. J'espère que nous aurons l'occasion de travailler ensemble à nouveau.
#. column 36: From the Adventurers' Guild, are you? Very good, very good.
#. column 37: Finished, are we? Let me take a look.<br>Yes... Yes... Very good. Very good, indeed. You have done a fine job today, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. My superiors at the Consortium will be pleased, to say the least.
#. column 38: The Brugaire Consortium is known for the expediency with which it fills its orders. If you refuse to complete the items I have requested, I will simply hire another adventurer to do my bidding. Gods know there are more than enough of you running around this city to choose from.
#. column 39: And, I believe they would be even <i>more</i> pleased if I were to return to the warehouses with a healthy surplus of the requested goods. You seem competent enough in your chosen trade. Would you consider contributing a few more whacks of the proverbial hammer in service of Brugaire?
#. column 40: I see. Off with you then. I am a busy man, and my clients are waiting.
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 12 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 4 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 17 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:8:0:41"
msgid "You have served the Consortium well. I shall duly note your contributions in my log. Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>night<else>day</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>day<else>night</if></if>, then."
msgstr "Ты хорошо послужил консорциуму. Я отмечу твой вклад в журнале. Что ж, доброй <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>ночи<else>доброго дня</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>доброго дня<else>ночи</if></if>."

#. ja: アンタが、冒険者ギルドから来た人だね？<br>さっそくだが、依頼品を出してもらおうか。
#. de: Danke, dass du gekommen bist. Ich bin ja selbst keine ungeschickte Handwerkerin, aber manchmal ist es einfach rentabler, jemanden anzustellen.
#. fr: C'est très aimable à vous d'avoir accepté ma requête. Je suis moi-même initiée à plusieurs disciplines de la main, mais il y a encore des domaines pour lesquels je préfère faire appel à des artisans plus ex<shy>pé<shy>ri<shy>men<shy>tés.
#. column 37: Wonderful! Your reputation for quality precedes you. I shall remember you if I happen to require assistance again.
#. column 38: Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:9:0:36"
msgid "I thank you very much for accepting my request. I fancy myself a decent craftswoman, yet there are some fields in which I have found employing the services of another can often prove most fortuitous for both parties."
msgstr "Спасибо, что согласился выполнить мой заказ. Сама я вроде неплохо управляюсь с ремеслом, но в некоторых делах нанять другого мастера бывает выгоднее для всех."

#. ja: ふむ、確かに依頼したとおりの品だ。<br>これなら問題ない、約束通りの報酬を渡そう。<br>また依頼を見つけたら、請け負ってくれ。
#. de: Wirklich solide Arbeit. Heutzutage wird viel zu viel für die Müllhalden produziert ... Ich werde dich wieder beauftragen, wenn du Zeit und Lust hast.
#. fr: Magnifique<nbsp>! C'est exactement ce que je voulais. Tenez, c'est votre récompense.
#. column 36: I thank you very much for accepting my request. I fancy myself a decent craftswoman, yet there are some fields in which I have found employing the services of another can often prove most fortuitous for both parties.
#. column 38: Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:9:0:37"
msgid "Wonderful! Your reputation for quality precedes you. I shall remember you if I happen to require assistance again."
msgstr "Чудесно! О твоём качестве работы я уже наслышана. Если мне снова понадобится помощь, я тебя найду."

#. ja: どうした、依頼品を忘れでもしたのか？<br>だったら取りに戻るんだね。
#. de: Hast du etwa vergessen, um was ich dich gebeten hatte? Vielleicht hätte ich lieber einen anderen Handwerker beauftragen sollen ...
#. fr: Et ma commande, alors<nbsp>? Ne me dites pas que vous l'avez perdue en cours de route<nbsp>!?
#. column 36: I thank you very much for accepting my request. I fancy myself a decent craftswoman, yet there are some fields in which I have found employing the services of another can often prove most fortuitous for both parties.
#. column 37: Wonderful! Your reputation for quality precedes you. I shall remember you if I happen to require assistance again.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:9:0:38"
msgid "Have you completed my request? I know you adventurers are the busy sort, but I, too, have deadlines to meet."
msgstr "Мой заказ готов? Знаю, у вас, искателей приключений, дел невпроворот, но и у меня сроки поджимают."

#. ja: 俺のギルドリーヴを受けたのか。<br>なら、ちゃんとできているんだろうな？
#. de: Besonders geschickt siehst du mir ja nicht aus, aber ich bezahl dich ja auch nicht fürs Aussehen. Hauptsache ist, du lieferst, was ich bestelle, dann können wir alle in Frieden unseren Geschäften nachgehen.
#. fr: Aaah, enfin une livraison<nbsp>! Alors, voyons voir ce que nous avons là...
#. column 37: I find your work more than satisfactory. Let me thank you. May our paths cross again.
#. column 38: I await your completion of the task I requested.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:10:0:36"
msgid "Hmph. You don't have the look of a crafts<if $gn4>woman<else>man</if>. Then again, I am not paying for looks. Make me what I have requested and all parties shall be satisfied."
msgstr "Хм. На ремесленника ты не похож<if $gn4>а<else></if>. Впрочем, я плачу не за внешность. Сделай, что я заказал, и все останутся довольны."

#. ja: いいね、いいね。<br>これでまた、ひと商売ができそうだ。<br>俺の依頼を見かけたら、また頼むぜ、相棒。
#. de: Ja, das entspricht meinen Vorstellungen. Wenn du weiter so gute Arbeit lieferst, werden wir gut zu<shy>sammen<shy>arbeiten.
#. fr: Ooh... Pas mal<nbsp>! Pas mal du tout<nbsp>! Oui, je devrais pouvoir en tirer un bon prix. Tiens, c'est ta récompense. N'hésite pas à accomplir d'autres mandats pour moi, j'aime beaucoup ce que tu fais.
#. column 36: Hmph. You don't have the look of a crafts<if $gn4>woman<else>man</if>. Then again, I am not paying for looks. Make me what I have requested and all parties shall be satisfied.
#. column 38: I await your completion of the task I requested.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:10:0:37"
msgid "I find your work more than satisfactory. Let me thank you. May our paths cross again."
msgstr "Работа меня более чем устраивает. Спасибо тебе. Надеюсь, ещё встретимся."

#. ja: おいおい、まだできてないのか？<br>こんなしみったれた入植地で油を売ってる<br>ヒマがあったら、とっとと働いてくれよ。
#. de: Bist du immer noch nicht fertig? Dann spute dich mal ein bisschen!
#. fr: T'es pas sympa de me faire des fausses joies, comme ça<nbsp>! J'ai besoin de cette marchandise le plus rapidement possible. Au cas où tu l'aurais pas remarqué, je roule pas sur l'or et chaque minute qui passe me rapproche un peu plus de la famine. Fais vite<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Hmph. You don't have the look of a crafts<if $gn4>woman<else>man</if>. Then again, I am not paying for looks. Make me what I have requested and all parties shall be satisfied.
#. column 37: I find your work more than satisfactory. Let me thank you. May our paths cross again.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:10:0:38"
msgid "I await your completion of the task I requested."
msgstr "Жду, когда ты выполнишь мой заказ."

#. ja: おや、ひょっとして<string $gs1>かい？<br>あたしは「アイスプリンセス号」のハ・ランボロ船長だ。<br>あんたを待ってたんだよ！
#. de: Bist du <if $gn4>die Handwerkerin<else>der Handwerker</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>den</if> die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde schickt? Ich bin H'rhanbolo, Kapitänin der <i>Eisprinzessin</i>, dem drittschnellsten Handelsschiff in ganz Limsa Lominsa.
#. fr: Salut, mousaillon<nbsp>! Alors, qu'est-ce que tu m'apporrrtes de beau, aujourd'hui<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Everything seems to be in order; a fine job, if I do say so myself. You ever think about hanging up your adventurer's britches, let me know. There might be a place for you on the <i>Princess</i>.
#. column 38: The Navigator did well to guide you here, but don't think she'll save you if my order isn't ready soon.
#. column 39: But before you trade in your land legs, could a lady ask one last favor? Those items I requested...might you be able to craft a few more? There's coin to be had, don't you worry.
#. column 40: That's unfortunate. My crew and I set sail soon, and I've never been one for waiting. Perhaps next time, then.
#. column 41: Such fine work! You are either a master at your craft, or a master at finding someone who's a master at their craft to make you look like a master at your craft. Either way, the Princess gets her supplies, and you get your reward. Everyone wins!
#. macro: <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:11:0:36"
msgid "You the <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> the Adventurers' Guild sent to do my synthesis? I'm H'rhanbolo, captain of the <i>Ice Princess</i>─third fastest trading ship in all of Limsa."
msgstr "Ты тот <if $gn4>парнишка<else>парень</if>, которого прислала гильдия, чтобы изготовить заказ? Я Х'ранболо, капитан <i>«Ледяной принцессы»</i> — третьего по скорости торгового судна во всей Лимсе."

#. ja: ばっちりじゃないか、<string $gs1>！<br>ねぇ、しみったれた冒険者なんか辞めて、<br>あたしの船に乗らないかい？　可愛がってやるけどねぇ。
#. de: Das nenne ich mal gute Arbeit! Willst du das karge Abenteurerleben nicht aufgeben und mit mir die Meere besegeln? Leute wie dich könnte ich gebrauchen.
#. fr: Parrrfait, c'est exactement ce que je voulais. Si jamais tu te lasses du métier d'aventurier et que tu veux devenir marin, sache que tu es l<if $gn4>a<else>e</if> bienvenu<if $gn4>e</if> sur la Prrrincesse de glace.
#. column 36: You the <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> the Adventurers' Guild sent to do my synthesis? I'm H'rhanbolo, captain of the <i>Ice Princess</i>─third fastest trading ship in all of Limsa.
#. column 38: The Navigator did well to guide you here, but don't think she'll save you if my order isn't ready soon.
#. column 39: But before you trade in your land legs, could a lady ask one last favor? Those items I requested...might you be able to craft a few more? There's coin to be had, don't you worry.
#. column 40: That's unfortunate. My crew and I set sail soon, and I've never been one for waiting. Perhaps next time, then.
#. column 41: Such fine work! You are either a master at your craft, or a master at finding someone who's a master at their craft to make you look like a master at your craft. Either way, the Princess gets her supplies, and you get your reward. Everyone wins!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:11:0:37"
msgid "Everything seems to be in order; a fine job, if I do say so myself. You ever think about hanging up your adventurer's britches, let me know. There might be a place for you on the <i>Princess</i>."
msgstr "Всё в порядке, работа на славу — уж я-то знаю. Если когда-нибудь решишь завязать с приключениями, дай знать. На <i>«Принцессе»</i> для тебя найдётся место."

#. ja: 依頼内容は復唱したかい？<br>それじゃあ、しっかり頼んだよ。<br>賃金なら心配無用。海の女は約束を守るからね。
#. de: Hast du Fragen zu dem Auftrag? Nicht? Dann brauche ich bestimmt nicht mehr lang auf die Lieferung zu warten. Oder etwa doch?
#. fr: Ça y est, tu te rappelles de ce que tu devais m'apporrrter<nbsp>? Bien, dans ce cas, dépêche-toi de me livrer<nbsp>! Plus tu me fais attendrrre, plus ta récompense diminue<nbsp>! Hé hé hé<nbsp>!
#. column 36: You the <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> the Adventurers' Guild sent to do my synthesis? I'm H'rhanbolo, captain of the <i>Ice Princess</i>─third fastest trading ship in all of Limsa.
#. column 37: Everything seems to be in order; a fine job, if I do say so myself. You ever think about hanging up your adventurer's britches, let me know. There might be a place for you on the <i>Princess</i>.
#. column 39: But before you trade in your land legs, could a lady ask one last favor? Those items I requested...might you be able to craft a few more? There's coin to be had, don't you worry.
#. column 40: That's unfortunate. My crew and I set sail soon, and I've never been one for waiting. Perhaps next time, then.
#. column 41: Such fine work! You are either a master at your craft, or a master at finding someone who's a master at their craft to make you look like a master at your craft. Either way, the Princess gets her supplies, and you get your reward. Everyone wins!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:11:0:38"
msgid "The Navigator did well to guide you here, but don't think she'll save you if my order isn't ready soon."
msgstr "Навигатор хорошо постаралась, приведя тебя сюда, но не думай, что она тебя спасёт, если заказ скоро не будет готов."

#. ja: やるじゃないか、<string $gs1>！<br>ねぇ、追加で仕事を依頼したいんだけどどうだい？<br>賃金なら心配無用。海の女は約束を守るからね。
#. de: Potzblitz, das kann sich sehen lassen! Würdest du mir noch mehr davon herstellen?
#. fr: Par Llymlaen<nbsp>! Tu te débrouilles sacrément bien, dis donc<nbsp>! Dis, tu voudrrrais pas m'en livrer un peu plus<nbsp>? Je te paierai, bien sûr...
#. column 36: You the <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> the Adventurers' Guild sent to do my synthesis? I'm H'rhanbolo, captain of the <i>Ice Princess</i>─third fastest trading ship in all of Limsa.
#. column 37: Everything seems to be in order; a fine job, if I do say so myself. You ever think about hanging up your adventurer's britches, let me know. There might be a place for you on the <i>Princess</i>.
#. column 38: The Navigator did well to guide you here, but don't think she'll save you if my order isn't ready soon.
#. column 40: That's unfortunate. My crew and I set sail soon, and I've never been one for waiting. Perhaps next time, then.
#. column 41: Such fine work! You are either a master at your craft, or a master at finding someone who's a master at their craft to make you look like a master at your craft. Either way, the Princess gets her supplies, and you get your reward. Everyone wins!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:11:0:39"
msgid "But before you trade in your land legs, could a lady ask one last favor? Those items I requested...might you be able to craft a few more? There's coin to be had, don't you worry."
msgstr "Но прежде чем променять сушу на море, окажи капитанше последнюю услугу. Сделаешь ещё немного того, что я заказала? Заплачу щедро, не сомневайся."

#. ja: なんだい、何か用でもあるってのかい？<br>まぁ、こっちの都合で頼んだ仕事ではあるんだけどさ。
#. de: Verstehe, du bist vielbeschäftigt. Ich kann leider nicht warten, weil ich bald ablege. Vielleicht ein anderes Mal!
#. fr: Comment ça “non”<nbsp>!? Tu sais à qui tu parrrles, petit<if $gn4>e</if><nbsp>? Bon, tant pis... Je vais me contenter de ce que j'ai sous la main.
#. column 36: You the <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> the Adventurers' Guild sent to do my synthesis? I'm H'rhanbolo, captain of the <i>Ice Princess</i>─third fastest trading ship in all of Limsa.
#. column 37: Everything seems to be in order; a fine job, if I do say so myself. You ever think about hanging up your adventurer's britches, let me know. There might be a place for you on the <i>Princess</i>.
#. column 38: The Navigator did well to guide you here, but don't think she'll save you if my order isn't ready soon.
#. column 39: But before you trade in your land legs, could a lady ask one last favor? Those items I requested...might you be able to craft a few more? There's coin to be had, don't you worry.
#. column 41: Such fine work! You are either a master at your craft, or a master at finding someone who's a master at their craft to make you look like a master at your craft. Either way, the Princess gets her supplies, and you get your reward. Everyone wins!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:11:0:40"
msgid "That's unfortunate. My crew and I set sail soon, and I've never been one for waiting. Perhaps next time, then."
msgstr "Жаль. Мы с командой скоро отплываем, а ждать я не люблю. Может, в другой раз."

#. ja: ばっちりじゃないか、<string $gs1>！<br>本気で、あたしの船の一員に迎えたいくらいだよ。<br>冒険に飽きたら、声をかけてくんな！
#. de: Das lobe ich mir! Das ist genau der Arbeitsgeist, den ich auch von meinen Seeleuten erwarte. Du würdest dich auf der <i>Eisprinzessin</i> wirklich gut machen.
#. fr: Alors là, chapeau... c'est de l'excellent boulot<nbsp>! Avec un<if $gn4>e</if> artisan<if $gn4>e</if> de ton calibrrre dans mon équipage, je suis sûr que la Princesse de glace deviendrait le navire de commerce numéro un dans la région<nbsp>! Penses-y et reviens me voir si le cœurrr t'en dit.
#. column 36: You the <if $gn4>lass<else>lad</if> the Adventurers' Guild sent to do my synthesis? I'm H'rhanbolo, captain of the <i>Ice Princess</i>─third fastest trading ship in all of Limsa.
#. column 37: Everything seems to be in order; a fine job, if I do say so myself. You ever think about hanging up your adventurer's britches, let me know. There might be a place for you on the <i>Princess</i>.
#. column 38: The Navigator did well to guide you here, but don't think she'll save you if my order isn't ready soon.
#. column 39: But before you trade in your land legs, could a lady ask one last favor? Those items I requested...might you be able to craft a few more? There's coin to be had, don't you worry.
#. column 40: That's unfortunate. My crew and I set sail soon, and I've never been one for waiting. Perhaps next time, then.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:11:0:41"
msgid "Such fine work! You are either a master at your craft, or a master at finding someone who's a master at their craft to make you look like a master at your craft. Either way, the Princess gets her supplies, and you get your reward. Everyone wins!"
msgstr "Отличная работа! Ты либо мастер своего дела, либо мастер находить мастеров, чтобы самому выглядеть мастером. В любом случае «Принцесса» получила припасы, а ты — награду. Все довольны!"

#. ja: ギルドリーヴの仕事を受けていただいた方ですね？<br>よろしい、それでは早速、仕事の話を致しましょう。
#. de: Wo bleibst du denn? Ich warte schon eine Ewigkeit auf dich! Es gibt viel zu tun und Meister Gegeruju ist ein vielbeschäftigter Lalafell.
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. Avez-vous les mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses que messire Gegeruju a commandées<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Finally done, are we? Couldn't remember if you were quenching or cross-stitching, is that it? Hand it over, then! Pleasure doing business and all that!
#. column 38: Are you getting to it, or do I have to get on you!?
#. column 39: Oh, wait. Where are you going? I wasn't finished. Would a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your means be interested in whipping up a few more of those fine items? The master likes to see that he's always prepared.
#. column 40: No get-up-and-go in your blood? Pity... Then again, the master has <i>other</i> means of getting what he needs.
#. column 41: Excellent. Master Gegeruju always says, “Why have one of anything when you can have a dozen?”
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:12:0:36"
msgid "Where in Thal's bowels have you been? There's work to be done. Come on, come on, get to it! Commerce and industry wait for no Lalafell! Especially when that Lalafell is Master Gegeruju."
msgstr "Где тебя носило, у Таловых кишок?! Дел полно! Давай, давай, за работу! Торговля не ждёт, особенно когда за ней стоит сам мастер Гегеруджу!"

#. ja: 確かに頂戴いたしました。<br>これだけの品でしたら、問題はないでしょう。<br>今後ともよろしくお願い致します。
#. de: Bist du endlich fertig? Ich dachte schon, du hättest den Auftrag vergessen. Dann schieb mal rüber, was du hast.
#. fr: Merci. C'est un beau produit que vous m'avez livré. Je suis sûr que le seigneur en sera fort satisfait. Prenez soin de vous, et à bientôt j'espère.
#. column 36: Where in Thal's bowels have you been? There's work to be done. Come on, come on, get to it! Commerce and industry wait for no Lalafell! Especially when that Lalafell is Master Gegeruju.
#. column 38: Are you getting to it, or do I have to get on you!?
#. column 39: Oh, wait. Where are you going? I wasn't finished. Would a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your means be interested in whipping up a few more of those fine items? The master likes to see that he's always prepared.
#. column 40: No get-up-and-go in your blood? Pity... Then again, the master has <i>other</i> means of getting what he needs.
#. column 41: Excellent. Master Gegeruju always says, “Why have one of anything when you can have a dozen?”
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:12:0:37"
msgid "Finally done, are we? Couldn't remember if you were quenching or cross-stitching, is that it? Hand it over, then! Pleasure doing business and all that!"
msgstr "Наконец-то! Не помню уже, что ты там делал — ковал или вышивал. Давай сюда! Приятно иметь с тобой дело и всё такое!"

#. ja: ……ところで、依頼品はどちらに？<br>まさか、まだ手を付けていないなどということは、<br>ありません……よね？
#. de: Gut Ding will Weile haben, aber die Weile ist nun langsam rum ... Wird das noch was?
#. fr: Eh bien, n'avez-vous rien à me montrer<nbsp>? Ne me dites pas que vous n'avez pas encore commencé<nbsp>!? Je vous conseille de faire vite, le seigneur Gegeruju a <i>horreur</i> d'attendre<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Where in Thal's bowels have you been? There's work to be done. Come on, come on, get to it! Commerce and industry wait for no Lalafell! Especially when that Lalafell is Master Gegeruju.
#. column 37: Finally done, are we? Couldn't remember if you were quenching or cross-stitching, is that it? Hand it over, then! Pleasure doing business and all that!
#. column 39: Oh, wait. Where are you going? I wasn't finished. Would a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your means be interested in whipping up a few more of those fine items? The master likes to see that he's always prepared.
#. column 40: No get-up-and-go in your blood? Pity... Then again, the master has <i>other</i> means of getting what he needs.
#. column 41: Excellent. Master Gegeruju always says, “Why have one of anything when you can have a dozen?”
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:12:0:38"
msgid "Are you getting to it, or do I have to get on you!?"
msgstr "Ты за работу возьмёшься или мне тебя подгонять?!"

#. ja: 確かな腕をお持ちとお見受けしました。<br>追加したい注文があるのですが、いかがでしょう？<br>もちろん相応の対価は用意してありますよ。
#. de: Moment, wohin des Wegs? Ich bin noch nicht fertig. Könntest du noch ein paar davon herstellen? Meister Gegeruju ist ein vorausschauender Lalafell, der einen soliden Vorrat zu schätzen weiß.
#. fr: Quel travail remarquable... Connaissant le seigneur, je suis persuadé qu'il apprécierait d'en avoir quelques exemplaires sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>res. Que diriez-vous d'effectuer une nouvelle livraison<nbsp>? Bien sûr, vous serez généreusement récompensé<if $gn4>e</if>. Vous le savez, l'argent n'est pas un problème chez nous. Ho ho ho<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Where in Thal's bowels have you been? There's work to be done. Come on, come on, get to it! Commerce and industry wait for no Lalafell! Especially when that Lalafell is Master Gegeruju.
#. column 37: Finally done, are we? Couldn't remember if you were quenching or cross-stitching, is that it? Hand it over, then! Pleasure doing business and all that!
#. column 38: Are you getting to it, or do I have to get on you!?
#. column 40: No get-up-and-go in your blood? Pity... Then again, the master has <i>other</i> means of getting what he needs.
#. column 41: Excellent. Master Gegeruju always says, “Why have one of anything when you can have a dozen?”
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:12:0:39"
msgid "Oh, wait. Where are you going? I wasn't finished. Would a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your means be interested in whipping up a few more of those fine items? The master likes to see that he's always prepared."
msgstr "Постой, куда собрался? Я ещё не закончил. Не хочешь сделать ещё несколько таких замечательных вещей? Мастеру важно быть готовым ко всему."

#. ja: なるほど、冒険者は冒険者なりに<br>都合というものがあるのでしょうね。
#. de: Nein? Ich weiß nicht, wie der Meister darauf reagieren wird ... Aber gut, es ist deine Entscheidung.
#. fr: Quel dommage... Enfin, j'imagine que vous avez d'autres coeurls à fouetter.
#. column 36: Where in Thal's bowels have you been? There's work to be done. Come on, come on, get to it! Commerce and industry wait for no Lalafell! Especially when that Lalafell is Master Gegeruju.
#. column 37: Finally done, are we? Couldn't remember if you were quenching or cross-stitching, is that it? Hand it over, then! Pleasure doing business and all that!
#. column 38: Are you getting to it, or do I have to get on you!?
#. column 39: Oh, wait. Where are you going? I wasn't finished. Would a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your means be interested in whipping up a few more of those fine items? The master likes to see that he's always prepared.
#. column 41: Excellent. Master Gegeruju always says, “Why have one of anything when you can have a dozen?”
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:12:0:40"
msgid "No get-up-and-go in your blood? Pity... Then again, the master has <i>other</i> means of getting what he needs."
msgstr "Нет задора? Жаль... Хотя у мастера есть <i>другие</i> способы получить нужное."

#. ja: 確かに頂戴いたしました。<br>これだけの量があれば、我が主ゲゲルジュ様も<br>満足なさることでしょう。
#. de: Sehr gut. Meister Gegeruju wird hocherfreut sein.
#. fr: Parfait<nbsp>! Messire Gegeruju sera aux anges. Après tout, c'est un homme dont la devise est<nbsp>: “Pourquoi se contenter d'un arbre quand on peut avoir toute une forêt<nbsp>?”. Continuez à mettre votre talent au service du seigneur et, bientôt, vous serez aussi riche que lui<nbsp>! Enfin... presque. Ho ho ho<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Where in Thal's bowels have you been? There's work to be done. Come on, come on, get to it! Commerce and industry wait for no Lalafell! Especially when that Lalafell is Master Gegeruju.
#. column 37: Finally done, are we? Couldn't remember if you were quenching or cross-stitching, is that it? Hand it over, then! Pleasure doing business and all that!
#. column 38: Are you getting to it, or do I have to get on you!?
#. column 39: Oh, wait. Where are you going? I wasn't finished. Would a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> of your means be interested in whipping up a few more of those fine items? The master likes to see that he's always prepared.
#. column 40: No get-up-and-go in your blood? Pity... Then again, the master has <i>other</i> means of getting what he needs.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:12:0:41"
msgid "Excellent. Master Gegeruju always says, “Why have one of anything when you can have a dozen?”"
msgstr "Прекрасно. Мастер Гегеруджу всегда говорит: «Зачем брать одну вещь, если можно взять дюжину?»"

#. ja: <string $gs1>君だね？<br>待っていたよ。早速だが、<br>ビジネスの話を始めるとしよう。
#. de: Einen schönen guten <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Abend<else>Morgen</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Tag<else>Abend</if></if>! Bist du hier, um etwas anzuliefern oder abzuholen?
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. C'est pour une livraison ou un enlèvement<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Handing in? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a nice day. Next!
#. column 38: I cannot sign off on your contract until you complete the order. Next!
#. column 39: If your business is not pressing, might Ashgana Exports persuade you to extend your contract? You will be rightly recompensed.
#. column 40: Not willing, eh? Very good. Sign here, please. Next!
#. column 41: Handing in surplus? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a wonderful day. Next!
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if></if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 12 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 4 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 11 < 17 (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:13:0:36"
msgid "Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if></if>, adventurer. Handing in or picking up? One moment, please."
msgstr "Добрый <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>вечер<else>утро</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>день<else>вечер</if></if>, искатель приключений. Сдаёшь заказ или забираешь? Одну минуту, пожалуйста."

#. ja: すばらしい、<string $gs1>君！<br>期待以上の成果だよ。我がアシュガナ貿易の<br>ビジネスパートナーとして、これからもよろしく頼むよ。
#. de: Eine Lieferung? Lad die Waren hier ab. Danke sehr und einen schönen Tag noch. Nächster!
#. fr: Une livraison<nbsp>? Signez ici, je vous prie. Merci, et bonne journée. Au suivant<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if></if>, adventurer. Handing in or picking up? One moment, please.
#. column 38: I cannot sign off on your contract until you complete the order. Next!
#. column 39: If your business is not pressing, might Ashgana Exports persuade you to extend your contract? You will be rightly recompensed.
#. column 40: Not willing, eh? Very good. Sign here, please. Next!
#. column 41: Handing in surplus? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a wonderful day. Next!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:13:0:37"
msgid "Handing in? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a nice day. Next!"
msgstr "Сдаёшь заказ? Подпиши здесь, пожалуйста. Спасибо, хорошего дня. Следующий!"

#. ja: わざわざ冒険者ギルドに手数料を支払って、<br>君を呼んだのだ。期待に応えてもらいたいものだね。
#. de: Komm wieder, wenn du die bestellte Ware fertiggestellt hast. Nächster!
#. fr: Je suis désolé, mais je ne peux pas signer votre contrat tant que vous n'avez pas livré les mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses. Au suivant<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if></if>, adventurer. Handing in or picking up? One moment, please.
#. column 37: Handing in? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a nice day. Next!
#. column 39: If your business is not pressing, might Ashgana Exports persuade you to extend your contract? You will be rightly recompensed.
#. column 40: Not willing, eh? Very good. Sign here, please. Next!
#. column 41: Handing in surplus? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a wonderful day. Next!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:13:0:38"
msgid "I cannot sign off on your contract until you complete the order. Next!"
msgstr "Не смогу закрыть твой заказ, пока ты его не выполнишь. Следующий!"

#. ja: 君には、ぜひ注文を追加したい。<br>どうだろう、難しい話ではないだろう？
#. de: Das Ashgana-Überseedepartment würde den Auftrag gerne erweitern. Für ein entsprechendes Entgelt, versteht sich.
#. fr: Les affaires marchent fort en ce moment et j'aimerais en profiter pour renflouer nos stocks. Que diriez-vous de prolonger votre contrat avec nous<nbsp>? Bien sûr, vous serez récompensé<if $gn4>e</if> comme il se doit.
#. column 36: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if></if>, adventurer. Handing in or picking up? One moment, please.
#. column 37: Handing in? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a nice day. Next!
#. column 38: I cannot sign off on your contract until you complete the order. Next!
#. column 40: Not willing, eh? Very good. Sign here, please. Next!
#. column 41: Handing in surplus? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a wonderful day. Next!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:13:0:39"
msgid "If your business is not pressing, might Ashgana Exports persuade you to extend your contract? You will be rightly recompensed."
msgstr "Если у тебя нет срочных дел, не согласишься продлить контракт с «Экспортом Ашганы»? Мы хорошо заплатим."

#. ja: そうか……ならば仕方はあるまい。<br>今日のところは、これにて商談を終えるとしよう。<br>次の機会に、よろしく頼むよ。
#. de: Vielleicht später? Wie du meinst. Nächster!
#. fr: Vous n'êtes pas intéressé<if $gn4>e</if><nbsp>? Tant pis, alors... Au suivant<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if></if>, adventurer. Handing in or picking up? One moment, please.
#. column 37: Handing in? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a nice day. Next!
#. column 38: I cannot sign off on your contract until you complete the order. Next!
#. column 39: If your business is not pressing, might Ashgana Exports persuade you to extend your contract? You will be rightly recompensed.
#. column 41: Handing in surplus? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a wonderful day. Next!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:13:0:40"
msgid "Not willing, eh? Very good. Sign here, please. Next!"
msgstr "Не хочешь? Что ж. Подпиши здесь, пожалуйста. Следующий!"

#. ja: まさに期待以上の成果と言わざるを得ない！<br>報酬は、弾ませてもらうよ！
#. de: Das können wir gut gebrauchen. Danke sehr und einen schönen Tag noch.
#. fr: C'est pour...<nbsp>? Ah, je vous reconnais. Une livraison, donc. Signez ici, je vous prie. Merci, et bonne journée<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Good <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>evening<else>morning</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>afternoon<else>evening</if></if>, adventurer. Handing in or picking up? One moment, please.
#. column 37: Handing in? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a nice day. Next!
#. column 38: I cannot sign off on your contract until you complete the order. Next!
#. column 39: If your business is not pressing, might Ashgana Exports persuade you to extend your contract? You will be rightly recompensed.
#. column 40: Not willing, eh? Very good. Sign here, please. Next!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:13:0:41"
msgid "Handing in surplus? Sign here, please. Thank you, and have a wonderful day. Next!"
msgstr "Сдаёшь излишки? Подпиши здесь, пожалуйста. Спасибо, хорошего дня. Следующий!"

#. ja: どうもどうも、依頼品は仕上がりましたか？<br>当然、持ってきているんですよね。
#. de: Ich hoffe, du kennst dich aus in deinem Metier. Die Karawane stellt höchste Ansprüche.
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir, bonsoir<else>Bonjour, bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour, bonjour<else>Bonsoir, bonsoir</if></if><nbsp>! C'est pour une livraison, j'imagine<nbsp>? Montrez-moi ce que vous avez.
#. column 37: Well, I suppose this is <i>adequate</i>. You may return to your so<hyphen>called <i>adventuring</i>.
#. column 38: Let us not <i>mince</i> words here. The Seventy-Seven Caravans require <i>perfection</i>. Pure and simple. Your <i>reputation</i> is at stake here, as is <i>mine</i>. You are to begin <i>at once</i>.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:14:0:36"
msgid "This <i>stripling</i> is who they send in answer to my summons? I trust you understand the <i>importance</i> of this work?"
msgstr "Это <i>несмышлёное дитя</i> прислали по моему вызову? Надеюсь, ты понимаешь, насколько <i>важна</i> эта работа."

#. ja: どうもどうも、確かに依頼した品のようですね。<br>それでは、報酬を支払いましょう。
#. de: Hm, kein Meisterstück, aber gut, es soll reichen. Hier, dein Lohn.
#. fr: Hmm... Oui, je pense que ça fera l'affaire. Tenez, c'est pour vous. Au plaisir de vous revoir<nbsp>!
#. column 36: This <i>stripling</i> is who they send in answer to my summons? I trust you understand the <i>importance</i> of this work?
#. column 38: Let us not <i>mince</i> words here. The Seventy-Seven Caravans require <i>perfection</i>. Pure and simple. Your <i>reputation</i> is at stake here, as is <i>mine</i>. You are to begin <i>at once</i>.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:14:0:37"
msgid "Well, I suppose this is <i>adequate</i>. You may return to your so<hyphen>called <i>adventuring</i>."
msgstr "Что ж, сойдёт. Можете возвращаться к своим <i>так называемым</i> <i>приключениям</i>."

#. ja: おやおや、一体どうしたというんです？<br>もしかして何を依頼されたのか、<br>忘れちゃったんですか？
#. de: Was macht meine Bestellung? Die Handelskarawane kann es sich nicht leisten, auf tranige Handwerker Rücksicht zu nehmen. Leg dich ins Zeug!
#. fr: Comment voulez-vous que je procède au contrôle des mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses si vous venez les mains vides<nbsp>!? Si vous n'êtes pas capable de fabriquer les produits que j'ai commandés, dites-le tout de suite et ne me faites pas perdre mon temps.
#. column 36: This <i>stripling</i> is who they send in answer to my summons? I trust you understand the <i>importance</i> of this work?
#. column 37: Well, I suppose this is <i>adequate</i>. You may return to your so<hyphen>called <i>adventuring</i>.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:14:0:38"
msgid "Let us not <i>mince</i> words here. The Seventy-Seven Caravans require <i>perfection</i>. Pure and simple. Your <i>reputation</i> is at stake here, as is <i>mine</i>. You are to begin <i>at once</i>."
msgstr "Не будем <i>ходить вокруг да около</i>. Караванам Семидесяти Семерых нужно <i>совершенство</i>. И точка. На кону твоя <i>репутация</i> — и <i>моя</i>. Приступай <i>немедленно</i>."

#. ja: あら、どうしたの？<br>何か届け物でもあるのかしら？
#. de: Und? Hast du mir etwas mitgebracht oder bist du nur hier, um mich anzuglotzen?
#. fr: Une livraison, vous dites<nbsp>? Montrez-moi la marchandise, que je l'inspecte.
#. column 37: Hmph. I s'pose this'll hafta do. You done what you came for. Off you trot.
#. column 38: You waltzed in here empty-handed? I oughta box your ears, you cheeky git. Now start craftin' or start bleedin'. Your choice.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:15:0:36"
msgid "Well? You gonna hand it over, or just stand there gawpin'?"
msgstr "Ну? Отдашь заказ или так и будешь глазеть?"

#. ja: 確かに受け取ったわ。<br>はいこれ、報酬。ごくろうさん！
#. de: Hm, sieht ja ganz ordentlich aus. Hier ist dein Geld.
#. fr: Oui, c'est bien ce que j'avais commandé. Merci, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>.
#. column 36: Well? You gonna hand it over, or just stand there gawpin'?
#. column 38: You waltzed in here empty-handed? I oughta box your ears, you cheeky git. Now start craftin' or start bleedin'. Your choice.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:15:0:37"
msgid "Hmph. I s'pose this'll hafta do. You done what you came for. Off you trot."
msgstr "Хм. Сойдёт. Ты сделал, за чем пришёл. А теперь ступай."

#. ja: あのさ……まさか、道中荷物を捨てて、<br>ここに逃げ込んだんじゃないでしょうね？<br>とにもかくにも、さっさと用意して頂戴！
#. de: Was macht meine Bestellung? Ich will ja nicht, dass du in der Eile irgendeinen Schund produzierst, aber so langsam solltest du fertig werden.
#. fr: Il faudrait savoir<nbsp>: vous avez quelque chose pour moi, oui ou non<nbsp>? Si vous cherchez juste à enquiquiner quelqu'un, allez voir mon collègue Gigiyon, au rond-point des Scorpions<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Well? You gonna hand it over, or just stand there gawpin'?
#. column 37: Hmph. I s'pose this'll hafta do. You done what you came for. Off you trot.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:15:0:38"
msgid "You waltzed in here empty-handed? I oughta box your ears, you cheeky git. Now start craftin' or start bleedin'. Your choice."
msgstr "Ты явился с пустыми руками? Я бы надавала тебе по ушам, наглец! А ну, принимайся за дело, а не то получишь. Выбирай."

#. ja: ……あんた、本当に職人？<br>アマルジャのスパイじゃないでしょうね？
#. de: Wer bist du? Was machst du hier? Ach, du bist <if $gn4>die Handwerkerin<else>der Handwerker</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>den</if> diese Gilde geschickt hat. Wie hieß sie noch? Ich weiß, die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde. Worum ging es noch mal? Ach ja, der Auftrag!
#. fr: Une livraison, tu dis<nbsp>? Ha<nbsp>! On ne me la fait pas, à moi<nbsp>! C'est les Amalj'aa qui t'envoient, c'est ça<nbsp>!?
#. column 37: Er... Are you sure this is what I asked for? Whatever was I thinki─ Ah? Oh, no matter, I'm sure it will come to me! My thanks!
#. column 38: Don't tell me you've forgotten to bring the order! My memory is like a steel trap, you see. Can't abide forgetfulness. Hm? Oh yes, the order! Did you bring it? No? Well then, craft away!
#. column 39: Oh, but before you go off to wherever it is you adventurers go, might I ask that you make me some more? I have this sinking feeling I might just...er, misplace the ones you've already submitted.
#. column 40: No? Oh... Well, I'm certain you have your reasons... Whatever they might be.
#. column 41: Wonderful... I think. This <i>is</i> what I ordered, right?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:16:0:36"
msgid "Yes, and how may I help you? ...Oh! Oh, an adventurer! From that guild! Which one was it now? Ah, yes! The Adventurers' Guild! And why were you here again? Ah, the order!"
msgstr "Да, чем могу помочь? ...О! Искатель приключений! Из той гильдии! Как же она называлась? А, точно! Гильдия искателей приключений! И зачем ты пришёл? Ах да, заказ!"

#. ja: これは！　助かったわ。<br>商人に鞍替えしてから、何人もの男に欺されてきたの……。<br>疑ったりしてごめんなさい。ありがとう。
#. de: Was ist das? Das habe ich bei dir bestellt? Na gut, wenn du es sagst, wird es schon seine Richtigkeit haben. Danke!
#. fr: Oups<nbsp>! C'est bien le produit que j'avais commandé. Je me sens un peu idiote maintenant... Enfin, avec tous ces escrocs qui traînent, on n'est jamais trop prudent. Merci encore et... désolée pour la méprise.
#. column 36: Yes, and how may I help you? ...Oh! Oh, an adventurer! From that guild! Which one was it now? Ah, yes! The Adventurers' Guild! And why were you here again? Ah, the order!
#. column 38: Don't tell me you've forgotten to bring the order! My memory is like a steel trap, you see. Can't abide forgetfulness. Hm? Oh yes, the order! Did you bring it? No? Well then, craft away!
#. column 39: Oh, but before you go off to wherever it is you adventurers go, might I ask that you make me some more? I have this sinking feeling I might just...er, misplace the ones you've already submitted.
#. column 40: No? Oh... Well, I'm certain you have your reasons... Whatever they might be.
#. column 41: Wonderful... I think. This <i>is</i> what I ordered, right?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:16:0:37"
msgid "Er... Are you sure this is what I asked for? Whatever was I thinki─ Ah? Oh, no matter, I'm sure it will come to me! My thanks!"
msgstr "Э... Ты уверен, что это я просила? О чём я только думала... А? Да ладно, может, ещё вспомню! Спасибо!"

#. ja: ふぅん、なかなか完成に漕ぎ着けなくて、せめて<br>誠意だけでも見せようと、このキャンプまで来ました、と……<br>どこまで信じていいのかしら？
#. de: Du bist noch nicht fertig? Du wirst ja wohl meine Bestellung nicht vergessen haben? Ein gutes Gedächtnis ist unentbehrlich für jeden Geschäftsmann. Also, gib mir die bestellte Ware. Ach, du bist noch nicht fertig? Du hast doch wohl meine Bestellung nicht vergessen? Ein gutes Gedächtnis ... Hm, ich glaube, ich hatte gerade ein Déjà vu. Seltsames Gefühl. Wovon hatten wir gesprochen?
#. fr: Ha<nbsp>! J'en étais sûre<nbsp>! Tu ne manques pas de toupet pour t'aventurer dans ce camp. Je vais être gentille et te laisser la vie sauve... pour cette fois. Mais ne t'avise pas de remettre les pieds ici, sinon je te dénoncerai aux autorités<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Yes, and how may I help you? ...Oh! Oh, an adventurer! From that guild! Which one was it now? Ah, yes! The Adventurers' Guild! And why were you here again? Ah, the order!
#. column 37: Er... Are you sure this is what I asked for? Whatever was I thinki─ Ah? Oh, no matter, I'm sure it will come to me! My thanks!
#. column 39: Oh, but before you go off to wherever it is you adventurers go, might I ask that you make me some more? I have this sinking feeling I might just...er, misplace the ones you've already submitted.
#. column 40: No? Oh... Well, I'm certain you have your reasons... Whatever they might be.
#. column 41: Wonderful... I think. This <i>is</i> what I ordered, right?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:16:0:38"
msgid "Don't tell me you've forgotten to bring the order! My memory is like a steel trap, you see. Can't abide forgetfulness. Hm? Oh yes, the order! Did you bring it? No? Well then, craft away!"
msgstr "Только не говори, что забыл заказ! У меня-то память что стальной капкан — терпеть не могу, когда забывают. А? Заказ! Ты его принёс? Нет? Тогда за работу!"

#. ja: あの……もしよかったら、追加注文を……<br>お願い、信じられるのは、あなただけなの！
#. de: Würdest du mir noch mehr davon herstellen? Nur für den Fall, dass ich etwas verlegen sollte. Das kommt aber nie vor. So gut wie nie. Eigentlich nur selten. Manchmal, wenn ich viel zu tun habe. Oder müde werde, am Nachmittag.
#. fr: Maintenant que je sais que tu es un<if $gn4>e</if> artisan<if $gn4>e</if> digne de confiance, j'aimerais te demander un petit service... Rien de compliqué, rassure-toi. Je voudrais juste que tu me fabriques quelques objets en plus, histoire de réapprovisionner mes stocks de mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses.
#. column 36: Yes, and how may I help you? ...Oh! Oh, an adventurer! From that guild! Which one was it now? Ah, yes! The Adventurers' Guild! And why were you here again? Ah, the order!
#. column 37: Er... Are you sure this is what I asked for? Whatever was I thinki─ Ah? Oh, no matter, I'm sure it will come to me! My thanks!
#. column 38: Don't tell me you've forgotten to bring the order! My memory is like a steel trap, you see. Can't abide forgetfulness. Hm? Oh yes, the order! Did you bring it? No? Well then, craft away!
#. column 40: No? Oh... Well, I'm certain you have your reasons... Whatever they might be.
#. column 41: Wonderful... I think. This <i>is</i> what I ordered, right?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:16:0:39"
msgid "Oh, but before you go off to wherever it is you adventurers go, might I ask that you make me some more? I have this sinking feeling I might just...er, misplace the ones you've already submitted."
msgstr "Постой, прежде чем уходить... Не мог бы ты сделать мне ещё немного? Боюсь, я... э-э... куда-нибудь задевала то, что ты уже принёс."

#. ja: 追加注文くらい、応えられないの？<br>あんた、職人なんでしょ、一応？
#. de: Nicht? Dann passe ich eben besonders gut auf. Auf den ... die ... Was war es noch gleich?
#. fr: Tu refuses<nbsp>? C'est juste une petite commande de rien du tout. Un<if $gn4>e</if> artisan<if $gn4>e</if> digne de ce nom ne laisserait jamais un client dans l'embarras. Hmm... Je commence à douter de ton honnêteté, tout à coup.
#. column 36: Yes, and how may I help you? ...Oh! Oh, an adventurer! From that guild! Which one was it now? Ah, yes! The Adventurers' Guild! And why were you here again? Ah, the order!
#. column 37: Er... Are you sure this is what I asked for? Whatever was I thinki─ Ah? Oh, no matter, I'm sure it will come to me! My thanks!
#. column 38: Don't tell me you've forgotten to bring the order! My memory is like a steel trap, you see. Can't abide forgetfulness. Hm? Oh yes, the order! Did you bring it? No? Well then, craft away!
#. column 39: Oh, but before you go off to wherever it is you adventurers go, might I ask that you make me some more? I have this sinking feeling I might just...er, misplace the ones you've already submitted.
#. column 41: Wonderful... I think. This <i>is</i> what I ordered, right?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:16:0:40"
msgid "No? Oh... Well, I'm certain you have your reasons... Whatever they might be."
msgstr "Нет? Ох... Наверное, у тебя есть причины. Какие бы они ни были."

#. ja: 本当に助かったわ！<br>やっぱり、あなたを信じて良かった……<br>世の中には、信頼できる人もいるのね！
#. de: Sehr schön! Dann bestelle ich noch mehr von den ... die ... Du weißt schon!
#. fr: Merci<nbsp>! Merci mille fois<nbsp>! C'est tellement rassurant de savoir qu'il existe des gens honnêtes dans ce bas monde.
#. column 36: Yes, and how may I help you? ...Oh! Oh, an adventurer! From that guild! Which one was it now? Ah, yes! The Adventurers' Guild! And why were you here again? Ah, the order!
#. column 37: Er... Are you sure this is what I asked for? Whatever was I thinki─ Ah? Oh, no matter, I'm sure it will come to me! My thanks!
#. column 38: Don't tell me you've forgotten to bring the order! My memory is like a steel trap, you see. Can't abide forgetfulness. Hm? Oh yes, the order! Did you bring it? No? Well then, craft away!
#. column 39: Oh, but before you go off to wherever it is you adventurers go, might I ask that you make me some more? I have this sinking feeling I might just...er, misplace the ones you've already submitted.
#. column 40: No? Oh... Well, I'm certain you have your reasons... Whatever they might be.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:16:0:41"
msgid "Wonderful... I think. This <i>is</i> what I ordered, right?"
msgstr "Чудесно... Кажется. Это <i>точно</i> то, что я заказывала?"

