#. ja: ギルドから派遣された冒険者だね？<br>私の仕事を請け負ってくれたんだろう？<br>寒いところに、よく来てくれたよ。
#. de: Die Gilde schickt dich?<br>Ah, du hast meinen Auftrag angenommen? Der Weg durch die Kälte bis hierher muss dich ziemlich mitgenommen haben.
#. fr: Voilà donc le fameux envoyé de la guilde des aventuriers que j'attendais... Tu as du courage de venir travailler dans un endroit aussi froid.
#. column 37: Splendid! Working as a sutler for the Ishgardians can be both a curse and a blessing. While the seemingly endless conflict with the dragons makes for good business, the extreme location of this conflict makes it difficult to maintain my stock. You adventurers are a Twelvesend!
#. column 38: I believe someone once said good things come to those who wait. Obviously that person did not have orders to fill.
#. column 39: You adventurers are a Twelvesend! But do you know what I appreciate most of your lot? That you are always willing to do more work, should there be extra coin in it for you. Oh, and look here. I have extra coin! Might you be willing to procure more items?
#. column 40: Did I mention I had coin? Well, no matter, then. I have what I need for the time being. If I require more, I suppose I can simply find myself another adventurer.
#. column 41: Yes, yes. This is exactly what I needed. Perhaps with the profits made from this surplus I can finally purchase that snow wolf jacket I've had my eye on. Any extra layer is welcome in this cold.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:18:0:36"
msgid "From the guild, are we? They told me someone would be along to deliver my order...but from the description provided, I imagined you'd be <i>taller</i>."
msgstr "Ты из гильдии? Сказали, кто-то принесёт мой заказ... но по описанию я представлял тебя <i>выше</i>."

#. ja: うん、確かに必要な品がそろってる。<br>これでどうにか、商売が続けられそうだ。<br>しっかし、寒いねぇ……。
#. de: Das habe ich wirklich dringend gebraucht, um meine Geschäfte fortführen zu können. Wenn es nur nicht so kalt wäre ...
#. fr: Voyons voir ça... Oui, il y a bien tout ce que j'ai commandé. Brrr, décidément, qu'est-ce qu'il fait froid par ici...
#. column 36: From the guild, are we? They told me someone would be along to deliver my order...but from the description provided, I imagined you'd be <i>taller</i>.
#. column 38: I believe someone once said good things come to those who wait. Obviously that person did not have orders to fill.
#. column 39: You adventurers are a Twelvesend! But do you know what I appreciate most of your lot? That you are always willing to do more work, should there be extra coin in it for you. Oh, and look here. I have extra coin! Might you be willing to procure more items?
#. column 40: Did I mention I had coin? Well, no matter, then. I have what I need for the time being. If I require more, I suppose I can simply find myself another adventurer.
#. column 41: Yes, yes. This is exactly what I needed. Perhaps with the profits made from this surplus I can finally purchase that snow wolf jacket I've had my eye on. Any extra layer is welcome in this cold.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:18:0:37"
msgid "Splendid! Working as a sutler for the Ishgardians can be both a curse and a blessing. While the seemingly endless conflict with the dragons makes for good business, the extreme location of this conflict makes it difficult to maintain my stock. You adventurers are a Twelvesend!"
msgstr "Прекрасно! Быть торговцем при ишгардцах — и проклятие, и благословение. Бесконечная, кажется, война с драконами приносит прибыль, но из-за того, что идёт она на отшибе, пополнять запасы непросто. Вы, искатели приключений, прямо посланы Двенадцатью!"

#. ja: 依頼した品を、そろえてきておくれ。<br>こうやって寒い場所で待っているのも、<br>かなり堪えるんだよ……。うぅ、寒い……。
#. de: Bitte erledige meinen Auftrag so schnell du kannst. Sonst erfriere ich hier noch, während ich auf dich warte.
#. fr: Non, ça ne va pas. Tu dois m'apporter ce que j'ai demandé, c'est pourtant simple<nbsp>! Tu as de la chance que j'ai l'habitude d'attendre dans le froid. Brrr...
#. column 36: From the guild, are we? They told me someone would be along to deliver my order...but from the description provided, I imagined you'd be <i>taller</i>.
#. column 37: Splendid! Working as a sutler for the Ishgardians can be both a curse and a blessing. While the seemingly endless conflict with the dragons makes for good business, the extreme location of this conflict makes it difficult to maintain my stock. You adventurers are a Twelvesend!
#. column 39: You adventurers are a Twelvesend! But do you know what I appreciate most of your lot? That you are always willing to do more work, should there be extra coin in it for you. Oh, and look here. I have extra coin! Might you be willing to procure more items?
#. column 40: Did I mention I had coin? Well, no matter, then. I have what I need for the time being. If I require more, I suppose I can simply find myself another adventurer.
#. column 41: Yes, yes. This is exactly what I needed. Perhaps with the profits made from this surplus I can finally purchase that snow wolf jacket I've had my eye on. Any extra layer is welcome in this cold.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:18:0:38"
msgid "I believe someone once said good things come to those who wait. Obviously that person did not have orders to fill."
msgstr "Говорят, терпение приносит награду. Видать, тот, кто это сказал, не занимался заказами."

#. ja: うん、確かに必要な品がそろってる。<br>とはいえ、もっと数があれば嬉しいんだけど……<br>もう一働きしていく気はないかい？
#. de: Eigentlich brauche ich eine noch größere Menge. Könntest du das über<shy>nehmen?
#. fr: Pas de doute, tout y est. En fait, ça serait encore mieux s'il y en avait un peu plus<nbsp>! Tu crois que tu peux faire ça pour me rendre service<nbsp>?
#. column 36: From the guild, are we? They told me someone would be along to deliver my order...but from the description provided, I imagined you'd be <i>taller</i>.
#. column 37: Splendid! Working as a sutler for the Ishgardians can be both a curse and a blessing. While the seemingly endless conflict with the dragons makes for good business, the extreme location of this conflict makes it difficult to maintain my stock. You adventurers are a Twelvesend!
#. column 38: I believe someone once said good things come to those who wait. Obviously that person did not have orders to fill.
#. column 40: Did I mention I had coin? Well, no matter, then. I have what I need for the time being. If I require more, I suppose I can simply find myself another adventurer.
#. column 41: Yes, yes. This is exactly what I needed. Perhaps with the profits made from this surplus I can finally purchase that snow wolf jacket I've had my eye on. Any extra layer is welcome in this cold.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:18:0:39"
msgid "You adventurers are a Twelvesend! But do you know what I appreciate most of your lot? That you are always willing to do more work, should there be extra coin in it for you. Oh, and look here. I have extra coin! Might you be willing to procure more items?"
msgstr "Вы, искатели приключений, прямо посланы Двенадцатью! А знаешь, что мне в вас нравится больше всего? Всегда готовы поработать ещё, если за это доплатят. И гляди-ка, у меня как раз есть лишние монеты! Принесёшь ещё товара?"

#. ja: それなら仕方ないね。<br>規定の数は既に受け取っているわけだし、<br>何より、これだけ寒いとね……無理強いできないよ。
#. de: Da kann man erst mal nichts machen. Hauptsache, du hast den Auftrag wie gewünscht erledigt. In dieser Kälte kann man natürlich niemanden zu Überstunden zwingen.
#. fr: Pas de problème, je comprends très bien. Qui aurait envie de faire du zèle avec une température pareille, après tout<nbsp>?
#. column 36: From the guild, are we? They told me someone would be along to deliver my order...but from the description provided, I imagined you'd be <i>taller</i>.
#. column 37: Splendid! Working as a sutler for the Ishgardians can be both a curse and a blessing. While the seemingly endless conflict with the dragons makes for good business, the extreme location of this conflict makes it difficult to maintain my stock. You adventurers are a Twelvesend!
#. column 38: I believe someone once said good things come to those who wait. Obviously that person did not have orders to fill.
#. column 39: You adventurers are a Twelvesend! But do you know what I appreciate most of your lot? That you are always willing to do more work, should there be extra coin in it for you. Oh, and look here. I have extra coin! Might you be willing to procure more items?
#. column 41: Yes, yes. This is exactly what I needed. Perhaps with the profits made from this surplus I can finally purchase that snow wolf jacket I've had my eye on. Any extra layer is welcome in this cold.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:18:0:40"
msgid "Did I mention I had coin? Well, no matter, then. I have what I need for the time being. If I require more, I suppose I can simply find myself another adventurer."
msgstr "Говорил, что у меня есть монеты? Ладно, неважно. Пока мне хватит. Если понадобится ещё, найду другого искателя приключений."

#. ja: これは助かったよ。<br>寒いところで、待ってた甲斐があったってものさ。<br>あぁ、これで分厚い毛皮の外套が買えるかも……。
#. de: Du hast mir sehr geholfen. Jetzt kann ich mir bald einen dicken Pelzmantel leisten. In dieser Kälte unverzichtbar.
#. fr: Ça alors, merci beaucoup<nbsp>! Ça valait le coup d'attendre ici, sous cette neige glaciale... Je crois que je vais m'acheter une épaisseur de fourrure sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>re pour la prochaine fois.
#. column 36: From the guild, are we? They told me someone would be along to deliver my order...but from the description provided, I imagined you'd be <i>taller</i>.
#. column 37: Splendid! Working as a sutler for the Ishgardians can be both a curse and a blessing. While the seemingly endless conflict with the dragons makes for good business, the extreme location of this conflict makes it difficult to maintain my stock. You adventurers are a Twelvesend!
#. column 38: I believe someone once said good things come to those who wait. Obviously that person did not have orders to fill.
#. column 39: You adventurers are a Twelvesend! But do you know what I appreciate most of your lot? That you are always willing to do more work, should there be extra coin in it for you. Oh, and look here. I have extra coin! Might you be willing to procure more items?
#. column 40: Did I mention I had coin? Well, no matter, then. I have what I need for the time being. If I require more, I suppose I can simply find myself another adventurer.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:18:0:41"
msgid "Yes, yes. This is exactly what I needed. Perhaps with the profits made from this surplus I can finally purchase that snow wolf jacket I've had my eye on. Any extra layer is welcome in this cold."
msgstr "Да-да, именно это мне и было нужно. Может, на выручку с излишков наконец куплю себе ту куртку из шкуры снежного волка. В такой холод лишний слой не помешает."

#. ja: 私の依頼を引き受けた冒険者だな？<br>……それでは、よろしく頼む。
#. de: Du bist also <if $gn4>die Abenteurerin<else>der Abenteurer</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>der</if> meinen Auftrag angenommen hat? Nun denn, so sei es ...
#. fr: C'est bien toi l'aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if> qu'on envoie pour ma requête<nbsp>?
#. column 37: The craftsmanship is excellent. The knights I serve will be beyond pleased... Now, whether they can live long enough to appreciate it, is another matter. But such are the ways of war.
#. column 38: The very lives of the men and women of this place ride on whether or not I can provide them with quality materiel in a timely manner. If you are incapable of fulfilling my request, then might I suggest finding someone who can?
#. column 39: The most ill-stricken of the knights may not be fortunate enough to find me before my stock is depleted once more. You see, no matter how much I procure, the demand is always greater than the supply. Now, if there were some way to increase my stock...
#. column 40: Oh, I understand. There is more to life as an adventurer than seeing knights are properly equipped so that they might return to their families alive, rather than in several pieces.
#. column 41: Thank you for the extra effort, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>. Knowing that the work we do might save even a single life... It makes this all worthwhile.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:19:0:36"
msgid "Here with the delivery? Good, then let us be quick. One can never tell when the dragon horde will strike next, and I would like to have my stock secure when it does."
msgstr "Ты с доставкой? Хорошо, не будем терять времени. Никогда не знаешь, когда нагрянет драконья орда, а я хочу, чтобы запасы были в порядке к её приходу."

#. ja: ……ふむ、見事なもんだ。<br>この商品があれば、一稼ぎできるだろう。<br>冒険者ギルドに頼んで正解だったようだな。
#. de: Eine beachtliche Leistung, <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if>! Damit lässt es sich arbeiten. Meine Entscheidung, die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde damit zu beauftragen, war die richtige!
#. fr: Hum, oui, c'est vraiment pas mal du tout. J'ai bien fait de m'adresser à la guilde des aventuriers, finalement.
#. column 36: Here with the delivery? Good, then let us be quick. One can never tell when the dragon horde will strike next, and I would like to have my stock secure when it does.
#. column 38: The very lives of the men and women of this place ride on whether or not I can provide them with quality materiel in a timely manner. If you are incapable of fulfilling my request, then might I suggest finding someone who can?
#. column 39: The most ill-stricken of the knights may not be fortunate enough to find me before my stock is depleted once more. You see, no matter how much I procure, the demand is always greater than the supply. Now, if there were some way to increase my stock...
#. column 40: Oh, I understand. There is more to life as an adventurer than seeing knights are properly equipped so that they might return to their families alive, rather than in several pieces.
#. column 41: Thank you for the extra effort, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>. Knowing that the work we do might save even a single life... It makes this all worthwhile.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:19:0:37"
msgid "The craftsmanship is excellent. The knights I serve will be beyond pleased... Now, whether they can live long enough to appreciate it, is another matter. But such are the ways of war."
msgstr "Работа превосходная. Рыцари, которым я служу, будут в восторге... если, конечно, доживут до того, чтобы оценить её. Такова уж война."

#. ja: 冒険者ギルドには手数料を支払い済みだ。<br>しっかり、依頼した品をそろえてほしい。<br>……それでは、よろしく頼む。
#. de: Über deinen Lohn habe ich mich bereits mit der Gilde geeinigt. Lass mich nicht zu lange auf die Gegenleistung warten.
#. fr: Avec tous les frais que j'ai payés à la guilde, j'espérais qu'on me fasse parvenir mon dû aussitôt. Dépêche-toi, je n'ai pas que ça à faire.
#. column 36: Here with the delivery? Good, then let us be quick. One can never tell when the dragon horde will strike next, and I would like to have my stock secure when it does.
#. column 37: The craftsmanship is excellent. The knights I serve will be beyond pleased... Now, whether they can live long enough to appreciate it, is another matter. But such are the ways of war.
#. column 39: The most ill-stricken of the knights may not be fortunate enough to find me before my stock is depleted once more. You see, no matter how much I procure, the demand is always greater than the supply. Now, if there were some way to increase my stock...
#. column 40: Oh, I understand. There is more to life as an adventurer than seeing knights are properly equipped so that they might return to their families alive, rather than in several pieces.
#. column 41: Thank you for the extra effort, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>. Knowing that the work we do might save even a single life... It makes this all worthwhile.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:19:0:38"
msgid "The very lives of the men and women of this place ride on whether or not I can provide them with quality materiel in a timely manner. If you are incapable of fulfilling my request, then might I suggest finding someone who can?"
msgstr "От того, успею ли я вовремя снабдить здешних людей качественным снаряжением, зависит их жизнь. Если не справляешься с заказом, найди того, кто справится."

#. ja: いい仕事してくれるじゃないか。<br>もしよければ、追加で仕事を回したいんだが……<br>むろん、報酬はしっかり払うぞ？
#. de: Du hast feine Arbeit geleistet. Wärst du vielleicht an einer Erweiterung deines Auftrages interessiert? An der entsprechenden Vergütung soll es nicht scheitern.
#. fr: Tu travailles bien, dis donc. Si ça t'intéresse, j'ai encore du travail pour toi. Bien sûr, il y a une récompense à la clef<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Here with the delivery? Good, then let us be quick. One can never tell when the dragon horde will strike next, and I would like to have my stock secure when it does.
#. column 37: The craftsmanship is excellent. The knights I serve will be beyond pleased... Now, whether they can live long enough to appreciate it, is another matter. But such are the ways of war.
#. column 38: The very lives of the men and women of this place ride on whether or not I can provide them with quality materiel in a timely manner. If you are incapable of fulfilling my request, then might I suggest finding someone who can?
#. column 40: Oh, I understand. There is more to life as an adventurer than seeing knights are properly equipped so that they might return to their families alive, rather than in several pieces.
#. column 41: Thank you for the extra effort, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>. Knowing that the work we do might save even a single life... It makes this all worthwhile.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:19:0:39"
msgid "The most ill-stricken of the knights may not be fortunate enough to find me before my stock is depleted once more. You see, no matter how much I procure, the demand is always greater than the supply. Now, if there were some way to increase my stock..."
msgstr "Самые тяжелораненые рыцари могут не успеть найти меня, прежде чем запасы снова иссякнут. Сколько бы я ни закупал, спрос всё равно выше предложения. Вот бы как-нибудь увеличить запасы..."

#. ja: どうやらヒマではないらしいな。<br>……こちらの都合で頼んだのだ、<br>不足分は何とかしよう。では、ごくろうだったな。
#. de: Ich hätte erwarten müssen, dass <if $gn4>eine Frau<else>ein Mann</if> deines Schlages vielbeschäftigt ist. Nun denn, so sei es ...
#. fr: Si tu es occupé<if $gn4>e</if>... Pas grave, je demanderai à quelqu'un d'autre.
#. column 36: Here with the delivery? Good, then let us be quick. One can never tell when the dragon horde will strike next, and I would like to have my stock secure when it does.
#. column 37: The craftsmanship is excellent. The knights I serve will be beyond pleased... Now, whether they can live long enough to appreciate it, is another matter. But such are the ways of war.
#. column 38: The very lives of the men and women of this place ride on whether or not I can provide them with quality materiel in a timely manner. If you are incapable of fulfilling my request, then might I suggest finding someone who can?
#. column 39: The most ill-stricken of the knights may not be fortunate enough to find me before my stock is depleted once more. You see, no matter how much I procure, the demand is always greater than the supply. Now, if there were some way to increase my stock...
#. column 41: Thank you for the extra effort, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>. Knowing that the work we do might save even a single life... It makes this all worthwhile.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:19:0:40"
msgid "Oh, I understand. There is more to life as an adventurer than seeing knights are properly equipped so that they might return to their families alive, rather than in several pieces."
msgstr "Понимаю. В жизни искателя приключений есть дела поважнее, чем снабжать рыцарей, чтобы те вернулись к семьям живыми, а не по кускам."

#. ja: よくやってくれた、感謝する！<br>これだけの数があれば、こちらの懐も<br>少しは温かくなるというものだ。
#. de: Eine sehenswerte Leistung! Dir sei gedankt.
#. fr: Tu me rends un immense service<nbsp>! Avec tout ce que tu m'as apporté, ça devrait permettre à ma bourse de retrouver des couleurs.
#. column 36: Here with the delivery? Good, then let us be quick. One can never tell when the dragon horde will strike next, and I would like to have my stock secure when it does.
#. column 37: The craftsmanship is excellent. The knights I serve will be beyond pleased... Now, whether they can live long enough to appreciate it, is another matter. But such are the ways of war.
#. column 38: The very lives of the men and women of this place ride on whether or not I can provide them with quality materiel in a timely manner. If you are incapable of fulfilling my request, then might I suggest finding someone who can?
#. column 39: The most ill-stricken of the knights may not be fortunate enough to find me before my stock is depleted once more. You see, no matter how much I procure, the demand is always greater than the supply. Now, if there were some way to increase my stock...
#. column 40: Oh, I understand. There is more to life as an adventurer than seeing knights are properly equipped so that they might return to their families alive, rather than in several pieces.
#. macro: <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:19:0:41"
msgid "Thank you for the extra effort, <if $gn4>good lady<else>good sir</if>. Knowing that the work we do might save even a single life... It makes this all worthwhile."
msgstr "Спасибо за дополнительный труд, <if $gn4>миледи<else>сударь</if>. Мы делаем всё это ради того, чтобы спасти хотя бы одну жизнь... И это того стоит."

#. ja: 我々が依頼した仕事を<br>引き受けてくださった冒険者さんですね？<br>お待ちしておりました。
#. de: Du hast also unseren Auftrag angenommen? Wir haben bereits auf dich gewartet, <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if>.
#. fr: <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>Bonsoir<else>Bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>Bonjour<else>Bonsoir</if></if>, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>, je vous attendais.
#. column 37: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: You <i>do</i> remember what it is you have been asked to craft, do you not? Because I, uh, do not. I am certain the list is around here somewhere, but if I had time to look for it, I wouldn't be here talking with you now, would I? How is that for logic, eh?
#. column 39: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. Now, there's the matter of this <i>other</i> list─a list that is similar to the one given by me to the Adventurers' Guild, but with a few more items on it. Nothing fancy, mind you, just more of the same. If only there were someone standing directly before me with the skills necessary to complete the new order. Oh, but there is!
#. column 40: Well then... I suppose the blame is on me for not adding the additional items to the original list. I shall make a note to do so next time.
#. column 41: Allow me to fetch you a rag to wipe the grease from those elbows of yours! The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:20:0:36"
msgid "You must be the adventurer from that guild...what was it called again? Oh yes, the Adventurers' Guild! I must write that down somewhere. Ah, but to business. Did you have any trouble finding us out here? Are the items I requested in that nebulous bag of yours? Are you going to stop me? Because if you do not, I may keep talking until one of us collapses."
msgstr "Ты, должно быть, искатель приключений из той гильдии... Как же её? Ах да, гильдия искателей приключений! Надо бы записать. Но к делу. Трудно было нас найти? Заказанные вещи лежат в твоей загадочной сумке? Может, остановишь меня? А то я буду говорить, пока один из нас не свалится."

#. ja: 必要な品、すべてそろっていますね。<br>聖コイナク財団を代表して、お礼を申し上げます。<br>ご協力、ありがとうございました。
#. de: Alles wie gewünscht vorhanden. Im Namen der Sankt Coinach-Stiftung sei dir gedankt.
#. fr: Je vois que vous apportez tout ce dont j'avais besoin. Au nom de la Trouvaille de Saint-Coinach, permettez-moi de vous remercier.
#. column 36: You must be the adventurer from that guild...what was it called again? Oh yes, the Adventurers' Guild! I must write that down somewhere. Ah, but to business. Did you have any trouble finding us out here? Are the items I requested in that nebulous bag of yours? Are you going to stop me? Because if you do not, I may keep talking until one of us collapses.
#. column 38: You <i>do</i> remember what it is you have been asked to craft, do you not? Because I, uh, do not. I am certain the list is around here somewhere, but if I had time to look for it, I wouldn't be here talking with you now, would I? How is that for logic, eh?
#. column 39: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. Now, there's the matter of this <i>other</i> list─a list that is similar to the one given by me to the Adventurers' Guild, but with a few more items on it. Nothing fancy, mind you, just more of the same. If only there were someone standing directly before me with the skills necessary to complete the new order. Oh, but there is!
#. column 40: Well then... I suppose the blame is on me for not adding the additional items to the original list. I shall make a note to do so next time.
#. column 41: Allow me to fetch you a rag to wipe the grease from those elbows of yours! The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:20:0:37"
msgid "I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!"
msgstr "Кажется, это всё, что было в списке, оставленном мной в гильдии. От имени сынов святого Койнаха благодарю тебя, искатель приключений!"

#. ja: 依頼した品は、覚えていらっしゃいますか？<br>どれも、調査活動に必要な品ですから、<br>よろしく頼みますよ。
#. de: Hast du etwa deinen Auftrag vergessen? Beeile dich bitte, wir brauchen die angeforderten Güter dringend für unsere Forschungen.
#. fr: Vous souvenez-vous des articles dont j'ai fait la demande<nbsp>? Ils sont très importants pour nos recherches ici, vous savez.
#. column 36: You must be the adventurer from that guild...what was it called again? Oh yes, the Adventurers' Guild! I must write that down somewhere. Ah, but to business. Did you have any trouble finding us out here? Are the items I requested in that nebulous bag of yours? Are you going to stop me? Because if you do not, I may keep talking until one of us collapses.
#. column 37: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
#. column 39: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. Now, there's the matter of this <i>other</i> list─a list that is similar to the one given by me to the Adventurers' Guild, but with a few more items on it. Nothing fancy, mind you, just more of the same. If only there were someone standing directly before me with the skills necessary to complete the new order. Oh, but there is!
#. column 40: Well then... I suppose the blame is on me for not adding the additional items to the original list. I shall make a note to do so next time.
#. column 41: Allow me to fetch you a rag to wipe the grease from those elbows of yours! The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:20:0:38"
msgid "You <i>do</i> remember what it is you have been asked to craft, do you not? Because I, uh, do not. I am certain the list is around here somewhere, but if I had time to look for it, I wouldn't be here talking with you now, would I? How is that for logic, eh?"
msgstr "Ты ведь <i>помнишь</i>, что именно просили изготовить? Потому что я, э-э... не помню. Список где-то тут, но если бы у меня было время его искать, я бы сейчас не разговаривал с тобой. Ну как тебе такая логика?"

#. ja: 依頼した品、すべてそろっていますね。<br>ところで、時間がまだあるようでしたら、<br>追加の発注をかけたいのですが……いかがですか？
#. de: Wir würden übrigens gerne noch mehr bestellen, falls du die Zeit dafür finden könntest.
#. fr: Très bien, on dirait que tout y est. Au fait, si vous avez un peu de temps devant vous, puis-je vous demander un autre service<nbsp>?
#. column 36: You must be the adventurer from that guild...what was it called again? Oh yes, the Adventurers' Guild! I must write that down somewhere. Ah, but to business. Did you have any trouble finding us out here? Are the items I requested in that nebulous bag of yours? Are you going to stop me? Because if you do not, I may keep talking until one of us collapses.
#. column 37: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: You <i>do</i> remember what it is you have been asked to craft, do you not? Because I, uh, do not. I am certain the list is around here somewhere, but if I had time to look for it, I wouldn't be here talking with you now, would I? How is that for logic, eh?
#. column 40: Well then... I suppose the blame is on me for not adding the additional items to the original list. I shall make a note to do so next time.
#. column 41: Allow me to fetch you a rag to wipe the grease from those elbows of yours! The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:20:0:39"
msgid "I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. Now, there's the matter of this <i>other</i> list─a list that is similar to the one given by me to the Adventurers' Guild, but with a few more items on it. Nothing fancy, mind you, just more of the same. If only there were someone standing directly before me with the skills necessary to complete the new order. Oh, but there is!"
msgstr "Кажется, это всё из списка, который я оставил в гильдии. Но есть ещё один список — <i>другой</i>. Почти такой же, как тот, что я отдал гильдии искателей приключений, только в нём побольше товаров. Ничего особенного, просто ещё того же самого. Вот бы здесь оказался кто-нибудь, кто умеет выполнять такие заказы... А, так ведь ты уже здесь!"

#. ja: これは失礼致しました。<br>冒険者さんにも、事情というものがおありでしょう。<br>また機会があれば、お願い致します。
#. de: Das ist bedauerlich. Auf bald!
#. fr: Ah, pardonnez-moi. Vous devez être très occupé<if $gn4>e</if>, et je ne voudrais surtout pas vous déranger. Une autre fois, peut-être.
#. column 36: You must be the adventurer from that guild...what was it called again? Oh yes, the Adventurers' Guild! I must write that down somewhere. Ah, but to business. Did you have any trouble finding us out here? Are the items I requested in that nebulous bag of yours? Are you going to stop me? Because if you do not, I may keep talking until one of us collapses.
#. column 37: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: You <i>do</i> remember what it is you have been asked to craft, do you not? Because I, uh, do not. I am certain the list is around here somewhere, but if I had time to look for it, I wouldn't be here talking with you now, would I? How is that for logic, eh?
#. column 39: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. Now, there's the matter of this <i>other</i> list─a list that is similar to the one given by me to the Adventurers' Guild, but with a few more items on it. Nothing fancy, mind you, just more of the same. If only there were someone standing directly before me with the skills necessary to complete the new order. Oh, but there is!
#. column 41: Allow me to fetch you a rag to wipe the grease from those elbows of yours! The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:20:0:40"
msgid "Well then... I suppose the blame is on me for not adding the additional items to the original list. I shall make a note to do so next time."
msgstr "Что ж... Пожалуй, сам виноват, что не добавил всё это в первый список. В следующий раз не забуду."

#. ja: 素晴らしい働きぶりです。<br>聖コイナク財団を代表して、お礼を申し上げます。<br>ご協力、ありがとうございました。
#. de: Eine Meisterleistung! Im Namen der Sankt Coinach-Stiftung danke ich dir von ganzem Herzen.
#. fr: Ça alors, vous êtes l<if $gn4>a bienfaitrice<else>e bienfaiteur</if> de la Trouvaille de Saint-Coinach<nbsp>! Merci beaucoup.
#. column 36: You must be the adventurer from that guild...what was it called again? Oh yes, the Adventurers' Guild! I must write that down somewhere. Ah, but to business. Did you have any trouble finding us out here? Are the items I requested in that nebulous bag of yours? Are you going to stop me? Because if you do not, I may keep talking until one of us collapses.
#. column 37: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: You <i>do</i> remember what it is you have been asked to craft, do you not? Because I, uh, do not. I am certain the list is around here somewhere, but if I had time to look for it, I wouldn't be here talking with you now, would I? How is that for logic, eh?
#. column 39: I do believe that is everything on the list I left with the guild. Now, there's the matter of this <i>other</i> list─a list that is similar to the one given by me to the Adventurers' Guild, but with a few more items on it. Nothing fancy, mind you, just more of the same. If only there were someone standing directly before me with the skills necessary to complete the new order. Oh, but there is!
#. column 40: Well then... I suppose the blame is on me for not adding the additional items to the original list. I shall make a note to do so next time.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:20:0:41"
msgid "Allow me to fetch you a rag to wipe the grease from those elbows of yours! The Sons of Saint Coinach thank you, adventurer!"
msgstr "Позволь принести тряпку, чтобы ты вытер масло с локтей! От имени сынов святого Койнаха благодарю тебя, искатель приключений!"

#. ja: おう、お前さんが、俺の依頼を受けた漁師だな？<br>頼んでおいた品は捕れたかい？
#. de: Ha, du musst <if $gn4>die Fischerin<else>der Fischer</if> sein, auf <if $gn4>die<else>den</if> ich gewartet habe! Bitte enttäusche mich nicht.
#. fr: Tu es l<if $gn4>a pêcheuse<else>e pêcheur</if> que la guilde des aventuriers m'envoie<nbsp>? Fais donc voir ce que tu rapportes.
#. column 37: Yes! This will add the needed flavor to my next masterpiece! My taste buds thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: I'm used to that crooked Wawalago making me wait, but didn't expect the same from an adventurer. Are you sure you're using the right bait?
#. column 39: ...But will it be <i>enough</i>? I suppose it can't hurt to have <i>too</i> much of a good thing. So, what of it, adventurer? Cast your line one more time for ol' Unsynwilf?
#. column 40: Well then, I won't press you. Maybe next time, eh?
#. column 41: Hah hah! Tonight's stew will be the greatest culinary creation in the history of Limsa Lominsa─no, the history of man! And I have you to thank, adventurer!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:21:0:36"
msgid "Let's just skip the pleasantries, aye? You hand me the fish, I slip you a purse of coin. Everyone's happy."
msgstr "Давай без любезностей, а? Ты даёшь мне рыбу, я — кошель с монетами. Все довольны."

#. ja: おおう、コレコレ！<br>コイツで創作料理を作ってみようと思ってな。<br>ありがとよ、助かったぜ。
#. de: Genau darauf hab ich gewartet! Damit werde ich jetzt was Feines brutzeln. Danke dir!
#. fr: C'est exactement ce qu'il me faut<nbsp>! Avec ça, je vais préparer un plat original dont j'ai le secret. Merci à toi, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>.
#. column 36: Let's just skip the pleasantries, aye? You hand me the fish, I slip you a purse of coin. Everyone's happy.
#. column 38: I'm used to that crooked Wawalago making me wait, but didn't expect the same from an adventurer. Are you sure you're using the right bait?
#. column 39: ...But will it be <i>enough</i>? I suppose it can't hurt to have <i>too</i> much of a good thing. So, what of it, adventurer? Cast your line one more time for ol' Unsynwilf?
#. column 40: Well then, I won't press you. Maybe next time, eh?
#. column 41: Hah hah! Tonight's stew will be the greatest culinary creation in the history of Limsa Lominsa─no, the history of man! And I have you to thank, adventurer!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:21:0:37"
msgid "Yes! This will add the needed flavor to my next masterpiece! My taste buds thank you, adventurer!"
msgstr "Вот оно! С ним моё следующее блюдо станет ещё вкуснее! Мои вкусовые рецепторы благодарят тебя, искатель приключений!"

#. ja: おいおい、依頼した品はまだなのかい？<br>魚介類は鮮度が命、依頼だって同じだぜ！？
#. de: Was ist mit meiner Bestellung? Beißen sie heute nicht oder sind die Gewässer plötzlich ausgetrocknet?
#. fr: Alors, qu'est-ce que tu attends<nbsp>? La fraîcheur est tout pour les fruits de mer, et c'est pareil pour ma requête, compris<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Let's just skip the pleasantries, aye? You hand me the fish, I slip you a purse of coin. Everyone's happy.
#. column 37: Yes! This will add the needed flavor to my next masterpiece! My taste buds thank you, adventurer!
#. column 39: ...But will it be <i>enough</i>? I suppose it can't hurt to have <i>too</i> much of a good thing. So, what of it, adventurer? Cast your line one more time for ol' Unsynwilf?
#. column 40: Well then, I won't press you. Maybe next time, eh?
#. column 41: Hah hah! Tonight's stew will be the greatest culinary creation in the history of Limsa Lominsa─no, the history of man! And I have you to thank, adventurer!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:21:0:38"
msgid "I'm used to that crooked Wawalago making me wait, but didn't expect the same from an adventurer. Are you sure you're using the right bait?"
msgstr "Я привык, что этот проныра Вавалаго заставляет меня ждать, но от искателя приключений такого не ожидал. Ты точно на правильную наживку ловишь?"

#. ja: ついでと言っちゃ何だが、<br>お前さん、ちょいと追加注文を受けてくれんか？
#. de: Da du gerade hier bist ... hast du vielleicht Zeit für eine Nachbestellung?
#. fr: Tiens, pendant que je t'ai sous la main... Tu accepterais une petite requête sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>re<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Let's just skip the pleasantries, aye? You hand me the fish, I slip you a purse of coin. Everyone's happy.
#. column 37: Yes! This will add the needed flavor to my next masterpiece! My taste buds thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: I'm used to that crooked Wawalago making me wait, but didn't expect the same from an adventurer. Are you sure you're using the right bait?
#. column 40: Well then, I won't press you. Maybe next time, eh?
#. column 41: Hah hah! Tonight's stew will be the greatest culinary creation in the history of Limsa Lominsa─no, the history of man! And I have you to thank, adventurer!
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:21:0:39"
msgid "...But will it be <i>enough</i>? I suppose it can't hurt to have <i>too</i> much of a good thing. So, what of it, adventurer? Cast your line one more time for ol' Unsynwilf?"
msgstr "...Но хватит ли этого? Пожалуй, чего доброго не бывает <i>слишком</i> <i>много</i>. Ну что скажешь, искатель приключений? Забросишь удочку ещё разок для старого Унсинвильфа?"

#. ja: そうかい、そうかい。<br>お前さんにも、事情ってもんがあるだろうよ。<br>ま、気にすんな。
#. de: Kein Problem, war nur eine Frage.
#. fr: Tant pis. Tu dois avoir tes raisons je suppose... Je trouverai quelqu'un d'autre à qui m'adresser, ne t'en fais pas.
#. column 36: Let's just skip the pleasantries, aye? You hand me the fish, I slip you a purse of coin. Everyone's happy.
#. column 37: Yes! This will add the needed flavor to my next masterpiece! My taste buds thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: I'm used to that crooked Wawalago making me wait, but didn't expect the same from an adventurer. Are you sure you're using the right bait?
#. column 39: ...But will it be <i>enough</i>? I suppose it can't hurt to have <i>too</i> much of a good thing. So, what of it, adventurer? Cast your line one more time for ol' Unsynwilf?
#. column 41: Hah hah! Tonight's stew will be the greatest culinary creation in the history of Limsa Lominsa─no, the history of man! And I have you to thank, adventurer!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:21:0:40"
msgid "Well then, I won't press you. Maybe next time, eh?"
msgstr "Что ж, не стану настаивать. Может, в другой раз, а?"

#. ja: やってくれるじゃねぇか。<br>こんだけ食材があれば、新レシピの創作にも<br>力が入るってもんだぜ。あんがとよ！
#. de: Herzlichen Dank! Jetzt hab ich sogar genug, um ein paar neue Rezepte auszuprobieren!
#. fr: Voilà ce que j'appelle du travail bien fait<nbsp>! Avec tout ça, je vais pouvoir laisser libre court à mon imagination culinaire. Merci<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Let's just skip the pleasantries, aye? You hand me the fish, I slip you a purse of coin. Everyone's happy.
#. column 37: Yes! This will add the needed flavor to my next masterpiece! My taste buds thank you, adventurer!
#. column 38: I'm used to that crooked Wawalago making me wait, but didn't expect the same from an adventurer. Are you sure you're using the right bait?
#. column 39: ...But will it be <i>enough</i>? I suppose it can't hurt to have <i>too</i> much of a good thing. So, what of it, adventurer? Cast your line one more time for ol' Unsynwilf?
#. column 40: Well then, I won't press you. Maybe next time, eh?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:21:0:41"
msgid "Hah hah! Tonight's stew will be the greatest culinary creation in the history of Limsa Lominsa─no, the history of man! And I have you to thank, adventurer!"
msgstr "Ха-ха! Сегодняшняя похлёбка станет величайшим кулинарным творением в истории Лимсы Ломинсы… нет, в истории человечества! И всё благодаря тебе, искатель приключений!"

#. ja: あなたが冒険者ギルドから派遣された漁師さん？<br>お願いしておいた魚介類は、用意できたかしら？
#. de: <if $gn4>Die Fischerin<else>Der Fischer</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>den</if> mir die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde geschickt hat. Endlich! Hast du meine Bestellung mitgebracht?
#. fr: Salut, aventurrri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if><nbsp>! Alors, tu m'apportes ces délicieux petits poissons<nbsp>?
#. column 37: I'm not going to find any nasty surprises swimming amongst these, am I? One cannot be too careful, you know.
#. column 38: You are here, yet you have naught to deliver. I suppose you can avail yourself of my generosity and spend a few more moments about the water's edge, but just remember: I have my eye on you.
#. column 39: The order would seem to be fulfilled, but I would be turning my nose at a chance for good fortune if I were not to tug on the strand of fate that the Spinner has so conveniently strewn betwixt us. Might you be interested in extending our little contract?
#. column 40: Understood. I shall keep you no longer.
#. column 41: It appears my suspicions were unwarranted. It truly has been a pleasure working with you...this time. I make no guarantees for the next.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:22:0:36"
msgid "Hold it right there. You say you're the one sent to deliver the items I requested? Hmmm."
msgstr "Постой-ка. Ты говоришь, что это ты принёс заказанные мной товары? Хм-м…"

#. ja: うんうん、摘み食いなさらずに、<br>ちゃんと頼んでおいた品を持ってきてくださったのね？<br>さあ、約束していた報酬をお渡ししますよ。
#. de: Danke! Hoffentlich hast du nicht zu sehr daran rumgetatscht.
#. fr: Oh, tu l'as vrrraiment fait<nbsp>! À ta place, j'en aurais avalé la moitié en route, héhé. Tiens, voilà ta récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Hold it right there. You say you're the one sent to deliver the items I requested? Hmmm.
#. column 38: You are here, yet you have naught to deliver. I suppose you can avail yourself of my generosity and spend a few more moments about the water's edge, but just remember: I have my eye on you.
#. column 39: The order would seem to be fulfilled, but I would be turning my nose at a chance for good fortune if I were not to tug on the strand of fate that the Spinner has so conveniently strewn betwixt us. Might you be interested in extending our little contract?
#. column 40: Understood. I shall keep you no longer.
#. column 41: It appears my suspicions were unwarranted. It truly has been a pleasure working with you...this time. I make no guarantees for the next.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:22:0:37"
msgid "I'm not going to find any nasty surprises swimming amongst these, am I? One cannot be too careful, you know."
msgstr "Надеюсь, среди этого улова не найдётся никаких неприятных сюрпризов? Осторожность никогда не помешает, знаешь ли."

#. ja: これから漁に出るのですか？<br>捕れた魚介類がおいしそうだからって、<br>摘み食いなさらないでくださいね？
#. de: Wie bitte? Ist dir dein Fang etwa zurück ins Meer geflutscht?
#. fr: Quoi, tu vas te mettre à les pêcher maintenant<nbsp>? Bon, au moins comme ça ils seront de la première frrraîcheur...
#. column 36: Hold it right there. You say you're the one sent to deliver the items I requested? Hmmm.
#. column 37: I'm not going to find any nasty surprises swimming amongst these, am I? One cannot be too careful, you know.
#. column 39: The order would seem to be fulfilled, but I would be turning my nose at a chance for good fortune if I were not to tug on the strand of fate that the Spinner has so conveniently strewn betwixt us. Might you be interested in extending our little contract?
#. column 40: Understood. I shall keep you no longer.
#. column 41: It appears my suspicions were unwarranted. It truly has been a pleasure working with you...this time. I make no guarantees for the next.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:22:0:38"
msgid "You are here, yet you have naught to deliver. I suppose you can avail yourself of my generosity and spend a few more moments about the water's edge, but just remember: I have my eye on you."
msgstr "Ты пришёл, а принести нечего. Ну что ж, можешь воспользоваться моей добротой и ещё немного порыбачить у воды. Только помни: я за тобой слежу."

#. ja: 素晴らしいですわ！<br>この調子で、追加注文をお願いしたいくらい……<br>もちろん報酬は増額しますから、いかがかしら？
#. de: Auch wenn ich etwas Angst davor habe, dass du meine Bestellung zu sehr antatschst, hätte ich gerne noch mehr davon.
#. fr: C'est excellent<nbsp>! Vu comme tu t'en sorrrs bien, j'aurais presque envie de t'en demander encorrre plus... Qu'en dis-tu<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Hold it right there. You say you're the one sent to deliver the items I requested? Hmmm.
#. column 37: I'm not going to find any nasty surprises swimming amongst these, am I? One cannot be too careful, you know.
#. column 38: You are here, yet you have naught to deliver. I suppose you can avail yourself of my generosity and spend a few more moments about the water's edge, but just remember: I have my eye on you.
#. column 40: Understood. I shall keep you no longer.
#. column 41: It appears my suspicions were unwarranted. It truly has been a pleasure working with you...this time. I make no guarantees for the next.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:22:0:39"
msgid "The order would seem to be fulfilled, but I would be turning my nose at a chance for good fortune if I were not to tug on the strand of fate that the Spinner has so conveniently strewn betwixt us. Might you be interested in extending our little contract?"
msgstr "Похоже, заказ выполнен. Но было бы глупо упускать такой шанс, раз сама Наложница Судеб свела нас вместе. Не хочешь продолжить наше небольшое соглашение?"

#. ja: それは残念ですね。<br>とはいえ漁師さんにも都合があるのでしょう。<br>またの機会にお願いしますね。
#. de: Gut, dann geh dir erst mal die Hände waschen.
#. fr: Ah bon... Je suppose que tu dois t'en aller pêcher dans d'autres eaux. Tant pis, une prrrochaine fois<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Hold it right there. You say you're the one sent to deliver the items I requested? Hmmm.
#. column 37: I'm not going to find any nasty surprises swimming amongst these, am I? One cannot be too careful, you know.
#. column 38: You are here, yet you have naught to deliver. I suppose you can avail yourself of my generosity and spend a few more moments about the water's edge, but just remember: I have my eye on you.
#. column 39: The order would seem to be fulfilled, but I would be turning my nose at a chance for good fortune if I were not to tug on the strand of fate that the Spinner has so conveniently strewn betwixt us. Might you be interested in extending our little contract?
#. column 41: It appears my suspicions were unwarranted. It truly has been a pleasure working with you...this time. I make no guarantees for the next.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:22:0:40"
msgid "Understood. I shall keep you no longer."
msgstr "Понимаю. Не стану тебя задерживать."

#. ja: 本当に助かりましたわ！<br>お約束していた増額した報酬、<br>さっそくお渡ししますわね？
#. de: Gut gemacht, ich kann keine Mängel an dem Fang erkennen!
#. fr: Mille merrrcis<nbsp>! Voici la récompense promise, avec un petit supplément. À bientôt, aventurrri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if><nbsp>!
#. column 36: Hold it right there. You say you're the one sent to deliver the items I requested? Hmmm.
#. column 37: I'm not going to find any nasty surprises swimming amongst these, am I? One cannot be too careful, you know.
#. column 38: You are here, yet you have naught to deliver. I suppose you can avail yourself of my generosity and spend a few more moments about the water's edge, but just remember: I have my eye on you.
#. column 39: The order would seem to be fulfilled, but I would be turning my nose at a chance for good fortune if I were not to tug on the strand of fate that the Spinner has so conveniently strewn betwixt us. Might you be interested in extending our little contract?
#. column 40: Understood. I shall keep you no longer.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:22:0:41"
msgid "It appears my suspicions were unwarranted. It truly has been a pleasure working with you...this time. I make no guarantees for the next."
msgstr "Похоже, я зря подозревала тебя. Работать с тобой было сплошным удовольствием… на этот раз. За следующий ничего не обещаю."

#. ja: あなたが、依頼を受けてくれた漁師さんね？<br>うふふ、頼んだ品を届けてくれるのを、<br>楽しみに待っているわ！
#. de: Du bist also <if $gn4>die Fischerin<else>der Fischer</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>der</if> sich meiner Bestellung angenommen hat? Zeig mal, was du hast. Ich bin schon total gespannt!
#. fr: Que fait donc ce pêcheur que la guilde des aventuriers m'a envoyé... Ah, c'est vous<nbsp>? J'avais hâte de vous rencontrer<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged.
#. column 38: Ye cannot be bringin' the fish in dribs and drabs, <if $gn4>girl<else>son</if>. Make sure ye match the order afore ye come speak with me again. Half-filled deliveries ain't worth their weight in shattered shells.
#. column 39: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged. But I'd bet my weight in seashells that yer lookin' to pad them pockets with another layer o' coin now. Tell me I'm wrong.
#. column 40: Ah, about that bet... I don't need to tell a cultured <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> as yerself that was but a figure of speech, now, do I?
#. column 41: Ye came through! I never doubted ye would, mind ye.
#. macro: <if $gn4>lass<else>laddie</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:23:0:36"
msgid "Ye here to deliver me fish, <if $gn4>lass<else>laddie</if>?"
msgstr "Ты принёс мне рыбку, <if $gn4>красавица<else>дружок</if>?"

#. ja: わぁ！　本当に捕ってきてくれたのね！<br>ありがとう～～！！
#. de: Wow, toll! Vielen, vielen Dank!
#. fr: Vous avez vraiment été pêcher tout ça pour moi<nbsp>? Comme c'est gentil<nbsp>! Merci, merci<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Ye here to deliver me fish, <if $gn4>lass<else>laddie</if>?
#. column 38: Ye cannot be bringin' the fish in dribs and drabs, <if $gn4>girl<else>son</if>. Make sure ye match the order afore ye come speak with me again. Half-filled deliveries ain't worth their weight in shattered shells.
#. column 39: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged. But I'd bet my weight in seashells that yer lookin' to pad them pockets with another layer o' coin now. Tell me I'm wrong.
#. column 40: Ah, about that bet... I don't need to tell a cultured <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> as yerself that was but a figure of speech, now, do I?
#. column 41: Ye came through! I never doubted ye would, mind ye.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:23:0:37"
msgid "Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged."
msgstr "Так-так… Да, всё, что было в списке. Благодарю."

#. ja: うふふ、あなたが漁から帰ってくるのを<br>わくわくしながら、楽しみに待っているわ！
#. de: Ich hab Zeit, geh einfach fischen und komm wieder, wenn du so weit bist, ja?
#. fr: Vous n'avez pas encore mes poissons<nbsp>? Ça n'est pas grave, je vous attendrai ici le temps qu'il faudra, hihi.
#. column 36: Ye here to deliver me fish, <if $gn4>lass<else>laddie</if>?
#. column 37: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged.
#. column 39: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged. But I'd bet my weight in seashells that yer lookin' to pad them pockets with another layer o' coin now. Tell me I'm wrong.
#. column 40: Ah, about that bet... I don't need to tell a cultured <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> as yerself that was but a figure of speech, now, do I?
#. column 41: Ye came through! I never doubted ye would, mind ye.
#. macro: <if $gn4>girl<else>son</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:23:0:38"
msgid "Ye cannot be bringin' the fish in dribs and drabs, <if $gn4>girl<else>son</if>. Make sure ye match the order afore ye come speak with me again. Half-filled deliveries ain't worth their weight in shattered shells."
msgstr "Нельзя приносить рыбу по частям, <if $gn4>девочка<else>сынок</if>. В следующий раз проверь заказ, прежде чем приходить. От недоделанной поставки пользы — как от ракушек без жемчуга."

#. ja: うふふ、あなたって本当に頼りになるのね！<br>それでね、もしよかったら追加注文を<br>受けてほしいのだけれど……どうかしら？
#. de: Auf dich kann man sich verlassen. Hast du vielleicht Lust, mir noch mehr davon zu bringen?
#. fr: Vous alors, vous êtes quelqu'un sur qui on peut compter<nbsp>! J'aimerais vous en demander encore plus... C'est possible<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Ye here to deliver me fish, <if $gn4>lass<else>laddie</if>?
#. column 37: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged.
#. column 38: Ye cannot be bringin' the fish in dribs and drabs, <if $gn4>girl<else>son</if>. Make sure ye match the order afore ye come speak with me again. Half-filled deliveries ain't worth their weight in shattered shells.
#. column 40: Ah, about that bet... I don't need to tell a cultured <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> as yerself that was but a figure of speech, now, do I?
#. column 41: Ye came through! I never doubted ye would, mind ye.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:23:0:39"
msgid "Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged. But I'd bet my weight in seashells that yer lookin' to pad them pockets with another layer o' coin now. Tell me I'm wrong."
msgstr "Так-так… Да, всё, что было в списке. Благодарю. Но готова поспорить на целую гору ракушек, что ты не прочь набить карманы ещё монетками. Ну, я права?"

#. ja: そっかあ。<br>残念だけど、頂いた分でがまんするわ。
#. de: Ach so. Na, ich bin immer hier zu finden, falls du mich suchst.
#. fr: Oh, quel dommage... Mais ça n'est pas grave, je suis déjà tellement contente d'avoir pu faire votre con<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ce<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Ye here to deliver me fish, <if $gn4>lass<else>laddie</if>?
#. column 37: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged.
#. column 38: Ye cannot be bringin' the fish in dribs and drabs, <if $gn4>girl<else>son</if>. Make sure ye match the order afore ye come speak with me again. Half-filled deliveries ain't worth their weight in shattered shells.
#. column 39: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged. But I'd bet my weight in seashells that yer lookin' to pad them pockets with another layer o' coin now. Tell me I'm wrong.
#. column 41: Ye came through! I never doubted ye would, mind ye.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:23:0:40"
msgid "Ah, about that bet... I don't need to tell a cultured <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> as yerself that was but a figure of speech, now, do I?"
msgstr "Кстати, насчёт спора… Неужели мне нужно объяснять такой воспитанной <if $gn4>даме<else>господину</if>, что это была просто фигура речи?"

#. ja: わぁ！　本当に採ってきてくれたのね！<br>ありがとう～～！！<br>報酬もオマケしちゃうんだから！
#. de: Wow! Du musst einer der Besten deiner Zunft sein! Dafür bekommst du eine tolle Belohnung! Danke vielmals!
#. fr: Oh<nbsp>! Tout ça, vraiment<nbsp>? Je ne sais pas comment vous remercier... Tenez, ça vient du fond du cœur<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Ye here to deliver me fish, <if $gn4>lass<else>laddie</if>?
#. column 37: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged.
#. column 38: Ye cannot be bringin' the fish in dribs and drabs, <if $gn4>girl<else>son</if>. Make sure ye match the order afore ye come speak with me again. Half-filled deliveries ain't worth their weight in shattered shells.
#. column 39: Lessee now... Aye, ye brought everythin' on the list. Much obliged. But I'd bet my weight in seashells that yer lookin' to pad them pockets with another layer o' coin now. Tell me I'm wrong.
#. column 40: Ah, about that bet... I don't need to tell a cultured <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> as yerself that was but a figure of speech, now, do I?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:23:0:41"
msgid "Ye came through! I never doubted ye would, mind ye."
msgstr "Ты справился! Я ни капли в тебе не сомневалась, вот увидишь."

#. ja: 冒険者ギルドから派遣された漁師さんだよね？<br>ねぇねぇ、お願いした品は用意できたのかしら？
#. de: Hallo, du musst <if $gn4>die Fischerin<else>der Fischer</if> sein, auf <if $gn4>die<else>den</if> ich gewartet habe. Hast du alles dabei?
#. fr: Vous venez de la part de la guilde des aventuriers<nbsp>? Oh... C'est donc à ça que ressemble un<if $gn4>e</if> vérrritable pêcheu<if $gn4>se<else>r</if>...
#. column 37: Good. Very good. Very, very good. Everything seems to be in order. You have done me and my customers a great service, adventurer.
#. column 38: Ah, yet it seems <i>you</i> have yet to fulfill <i>your</i> end of the bargain. <i>You</i> are free to take as long as <i>you</i> like, though in the meantime, <i>I</i> shall hold on to this reward.
#. column 39: Before I thank you for today's catch, how about we discuss the possibility of extending our agreement. My stalls always do better when they are full, just as I am sure that <i>you</i> do better when your <i>pockets</i> are full.
#. column 40: Interesting. It is rare to find an adventurer unwilling to do...just about anything when there is coin to be had. I apologize for judging you otherwise.
#. column 41: Good. Very good, Very, very good. The order is, what you would say, “in order.” Thank you again for your extra time, adventurer.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:24:0:36"
msgid "Here to deliver the catch? How thoughtful of you! Though something tells me you are not doing this out of the kindness of your heart. Ah hah hah hah. You need worry not. I have your coin ready right here."
msgstr "Принесли улов? Как мило с вашей стороны! Хотя что-то подсказывает мне, что дело не в доброте душевной. Ах-ха-ха-ха! Не волнуйтесь, ваши монеты уже здесь."

#. ja: ありがとうございます～。<br>ほんと、助かっちゃいました。<br>これでダメ漁師って言われないで済みます～。
#. de: Sehr schön! Wie bestellt.
#. fr: Merci, je ne sais pas comment j'aurrrais fait, sans vous<nbsp>! Enfin si, je sais... J'aurais été la risée de tout le hameau.
#. column 36: Here to deliver the catch? How thoughtful of you! Though something tells me you are not doing this out of the kindness of your heart. Ah hah hah hah. You need worry not. I have your coin ready right here.
#. column 38: Ah, yet it seems <i>you</i> have yet to fulfill <i>your</i> end of the bargain. <i>You</i> are free to take as long as <i>you</i> like, though in the meantime, <i>I</i> shall hold on to this reward.
#. column 39: Before I thank you for today's catch, how about we discuss the possibility of extending our agreement. My stalls always do better when they are full, just as I am sure that <i>you</i> do better when your <i>pockets</i> are full.
#. column 40: Interesting. It is rare to find an adventurer unwilling to do...just about anything when there is coin to be had. I apologize for judging you otherwise.
#. column 41: Good. Very good, Very, very good. The order is, what you would say, “in order.” Thank you again for your extra time, adventurer.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:24:0:37"
msgid "Good. Very good. Very, very good. Everything seems to be in order. You have done me and my customers a great service, adventurer."
msgstr "Прекрасно. Очень хорошо. Чудесно. Всё в полном порядке. Вы оказали мне и моим покупателям большую услугу, искатель приключений."

#. ja: ねぇねぇ、お願いした品は用意できたのかしら？<br>なるべく早くお願いします～。
#. de: Äh, könntest du dich vielleicht ein bisschen beeilen?
#. fr: Dites, vous ne voudriez pas vous dépêcher un peu<nbsp>? C'est que ça va commencer à se voir, que je passe la journée à me tourrrner les pouces.
#. column 36: Here to deliver the catch? How thoughtful of you! Though something tells me you are not doing this out of the kindness of your heart. Ah hah hah hah. You need worry not. I have your coin ready right here.
#. column 37: Good. Very good. Very, very good. Everything seems to be in order. You have done me and my customers a great service, adventurer.
#. column 39: Before I thank you for today's catch, how about we discuss the possibility of extending our agreement. My stalls always do better when they are full, just as I am sure that <i>you</i> do better when your <i>pockets</i> are full.
#. column 40: Interesting. It is rare to find an adventurer unwilling to do...just about anything when there is coin to be had. I apologize for judging you otherwise.
#. column 41: Good. Very good, Very, very good. The order is, what you would say, “in order.” Thank you again for your extra time, adventurer.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:24:0:38"
msgid "Ah, yet it seems <i>you</i> have yet to fulfill <i>your</i> end of the bargain. <i>You</i> are free to take as long as <i>you</i> like, though in the meantime, <i>I</i> shall hold on to this reward."
msgstr "Ах, похоже, <i>вы</i> ещё не выполнили <i>свою</i> часть сделки. Можете не спешить, сколько <i>вам</i> угодно, но пока что <i>я</i> оставлю награду у <i>себя</i>."

#. ja: ねぇねぇ、追加でお願いしたいんですが、<br>大丈夫ですか？
#. de: Falls du Zeit hast, kannst du mir gerne noch mehr davon bringen ... Was meinst du?
#. fr: Hé, c'est que vous savez y fairrre<nbsp>! Ça vous embêterait de m'en apporter un peu plus<nbsp>? Ça ferait meilleur effet, vous voyez.
#. column 36: Here to deliver the catch? How thoughtful of you! Though something tells me you are not doing this out of the kindness of your heart. Ah hah hah hah. You need worry not. I have your coin ready right here.
#. column 37: Good. Very good. Very, very good. Everything seems to be in order. You have done me and my customers a great service, adventurer.
#. column 38: Ah, yet it seems <i>you</i> have yet to fulfill <i>your</i> end of the bargain. <i>You</i> are free to take as long as <i>you</i> like, though in the meantime, <i>I</i> shall hold on to this reward.
#. column 40: Interesting. It is rare to find an adventurer unwilling to do...just about anything when there is coin to be had. I apologize for judging you otherwise.
#. column 41: Good. Very good, Very, very good. The order is, what you would say, “in order.” Thank you again for your extra time, adventurer.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:24:0:39"
msgid "Before I thank you for today's catch, how about we discuss the possibility of extending our agreement. My stalls always do better when they are full, just as I am sure that <i>you</i> do better when your <i>pockets</i> are full."
msgstr "Прежде чем поблагодарить вас за сегодняшний улов, давайте обсудим, не продлить ли наше соглашение. Мои прилавки лучше торгуют, когда на них полно товара. Уверен, и <i>вы</i> будете в выигрыше, если <i>ваши карманы</i> набьются монетами."

#. ja: まあ、そう甘くはないですよね……<br>解ってました……。<br>冷たくされるのって、初めてじゃないんです～。
#. de: Das ist ganz allein deine Entscheidung. Wie du möchtest ...
#. fr: Bien sûr, les choses ne se passent pas toujourrrs comme on veut... Bah, j'ai l'habitude d'être méprisée, ça ne me fait plus rien<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Here to deliver the catch? How thoughtful of you! Though something tells me you are not doing this out of the kindness of your heart. Ah hah hah hah. You need worry not. I have your coin ready right here.
#. column 37: Good. Very good. Very, very good. Everything seems to be in order. You have done me and my customers a great service, adventurer.
#. column 38: Ah, yet it seems <i>you</i> have yet to fulfill <i>your</i> end of the bargain. <i>You</i> are free to take as long as <i>you</i> like, though in the meantime, <i>I</i> shall hold on to this reward.
#. column 39: Before I thank you for today's catch, how about we discuss the possibility of extending our agreement. My stalls always do better when they are full, just as I am sure that <i>you</i> do better when your <i>pockets</i> are full.
#. column 41: Good. Very good, Very, very good. The order is, what you would say, “in order.” Thank you again for your extra time, adventurer.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:24:0:40"
msgid "Interesting. It is rare to find an adventurer unwilling to do...just about anything when there is coin to be had. I apologize for judging you otherwise."
msgstr "Любопытно. Редко встретишь искателя приключений, который отказывается делать… почти что угодно за звонкую монету. Прошу прощения, что судил о вас иначе."

#. ja: わぁ、ありがとうございます～。<br>ほんと、助かっちゃいました！<br>報酬も弾んじゃいますよ～。
#. de: Das übertrifft meine kühnsten Erwartungen! Deine Belohnung hast du dir redlich verdient.
#. fr: Voilà ce que j'appelle une affaire rrrondement menée<nbsp>! Ça vaut bien une petite compensation améliorrrée, héhé.
#. column 36: Here to deliver the catch? How thoughtful of you! Though something tells me you are not doing this out of the kindness of your heart. Ah hah hah hah. You need worry not. I have your coin ready right here.
#. column 37: Good. Very good. Very, very good. Everything seems to be in order. You have done me and my customers a great service, adventurer.
#. column 38: Ah, yet it seems <i>you</i> have yet to fulfill <i>your</i> end of the bargain. <i>You</i> are free to take as long as <i>you</i> like, though in the meantime, <i>I</i> shall hold on to this reward.
#. column 39: Before I thank you for today's catch, how about we discuss the possibility of extending our agreement. My stalls always do better when they are full, just as I am sure that <i>you</i> do better when your <i>pockets</i> are full.
#. column 40: Interesting. It is rare to find an adventurer unwilling to do...just about anything when there is coin to be had. I apologize for judging you otherwise.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:24:0:41"
msgid "Good. Very good, Very, very good. The order is, what you would say, “in order.” Thank you again for your extra time, adventurer."
msgstr "Прекрасно. Очень хорошо. Просто замечательно. Заказ, как говорится, в полном порядке. Ещё раз благодарю за помощь, искатель приключений."

#. ja: 貴方が依頼を受注した漁師ですね？<br>注文していた品は、用意できていますか？
#. de: Willkommen an der Sonnenküste, <if $gn4>Fischerin<else>Fischer</if>! Hast du den Auftrag erledigt?
#. fr: Êtes-vous l'envoyé<if $gn4>e</if> de la guilde des aventuriers<nbsp>? Parrrfait, je vous attendais.
#. column 37: Thank the Twelve. The world continues to turn, and your service to Master Gegeruju shall be remembered.
#. column 38: Oh, gods, no! Were you not informed of the urgency!? Dive in the water and use your hands if you must, but make haste! Haste, I say! Master Gegeruju does not tolerate three things in this world: being made to wait, being made to wait, and being made to wait!
#. column 39: I have some good news, and some bad news. The bad news is, in my haste to find an adventurer who could obtain the items Master Gegeruju requested, I failed to remember one of his many mottos─why have one of anything when you can have a dozen? The good news is, there is more coin to be made if you are interested. Say you are interested!
#. column 40: Then I can only pray that Master is too busy cuddling with his latest courtesan to notice the lack of cuisine.
#. column 41: Oh, the relief! The last time I forgot to double an order of fish for the master, he had me stand in a corner with a ten-ponze bucket of offal on my head for five bells straight. And that was only because he was feeling merciful.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <if $gn4>dear lady<else>good fellow</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:25:0:36"
msgid "Where have you <i>been</i>, my <if $gn4>dear lady<else>good fellow</if>? Please tell me you have the items I ordered."
msgstr "Где же вы <i>пропадали</i>, <if $gn4>дорогая<else>добрый человек</if>? Скажите, что принесли заказанные товары."

#. ja: 確かに、受け取りました。<br>これでゲゲルジュ氏も満足するでしょう。<br>さあ、報酬を受け取ってください。
#. de: Gegeruju wird begeistert sein! Hier, deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Permettez-moi de vérrrifier... Excellent. Le seigneur Gegeruju sera ravi, à n'en point douter.
#. column 36: Where have you <i>been</i>, my <if $gn4>dear lady<else>good fellow</if>? Please tell me you have the items I ordered.
#. column 38: Oh, gods, no! Were you not informed of the urgency!? Dive in the water and use your hands if you must, but make haste! Haste, I say! Master Gegeruju does not tolerate three things in this world: being made to wait, being made to wait, and being made to wait!
#. column 39: I have some good news, and some bad news. The bad news is, in my haste to find an adventurer who could obtain the items Master Gegeruju requested, I failed to remember one of his many mottos─why have one of anything when you can have a dozen? The good news is, there is more coin to be made if you are interested. Say you are interested!
#. column 40: Then I can only pray that Master is too busy cuddling with his latest courtesan to notice the lack of cuisine.
#. column 41: Oh, the relief! The last time I forgot to double an order of fish for the master, he had me stand in a corner with a ten-ponze bucket of offal on my head for five bells straight. And that was only because he was feeling merciful.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:25:0:37"
msgid "Thank the Twelve. The world continues to turn, and your service to Master Gegeruju shall be remembered."
msgstr "Слава Двенадцати! Мир всё ещё вертится, а ваша помощь господину Гегеруджу не будет забыта."

#. ja: 注文していた品は、まだ用意できていないようですね。<br>今からでも、漁に出てはいかがですか？
#. de: Du hast noch nicht alles? Dann mal los zum Fischen!
#. fr: Ce n'est pas ce qui était prrrévu. Pourriez-vous m'apporter la marchandise, comme convenu<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Where have you <i>been</i>, my <if $gn4>dear lady<else>good fellow</if>? Please tell me you have the items I ordered.
#. column 37: Thank the Twelve. The world continues to turn, and your service to Master Gegeruju shall be remembered.
#. column 39: I have some good news, and some bad news. The bad news is, in my haste to find an adventurer who could obtain the items Master Gegeruju requested, I failed to remember one of his many mottos─why have one of anything when you can have a dozen? The good news is, there is more coin to be made if you are interested. Say you are interested!
#. column 40: Then I can only pray that Master is too busy cuddling with his latest courtesan to notice the lack of cuisine.
#. column 41: Oh, the relief! The last time I forgot to double an order of fish for the master, he had me stand in a corner with a ten-ponze bucket of offal on my head for five bells straight. And that was only because he was feeling merciful.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:25:0:38"
msgid "Oh, gods, no! Were you not informed of the urgency!? Dive in the water and use your hands if you must, but make haste! Haste, I say! Master Gegeruju does not tolerate three things in this world: being made to wait, being made to wait, and being made to wait!"
msgstr "О боги, нет! Разве вам не сказали, как это срочно?! Если придётся, ныряйте в воду и ловите рыбу руками, но поспешите! Быстрее, я сказал! Господин Гегеруджу терпеть не может всего трёх вещей: когда его заставляют ждать, когда его заставляют ждать и когда его заставляют ждать!"

#. ja: 貴方の確かな腕を見込んで、<br>さらに追加で注文したいのですが……<br>ご検討いただけますか？
#. de: Ich weiß, deine Zeit ist kostbar, aber könntest du mir vielleicht noch mehr davon bringen?
#. fr: Je vois que vous êtes une personne sérrrieuse. Accepteriez-vous une commande sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>re<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Where have you <i>been</i>, my <if $gn4>dear lady<else>good fellow</if>? Please tell me you have the items I ordered.
#. column 37: Thank the Twelve. The world continues to turn, and your service to Master Gegeruju shall be remembered.
#. column 38: Oh, gods, no! Were you not informed of the urgency!? Dive in the water and use your hands if you must, but make haste! Haste, I say! Master Gegeruju does not tolerate three things in this world: being made to wait, being made to wait, and being made to wait!
#. column 40: Then I can only pray that Master is too busy cuddling with his latest courtesan to notice the lack of cuisine.
#. column 41: Oh, the relief! The last time I forgot to double an order of fish for the master, he had me stand in a corner with a ten-ponze bucket of offal on my head for five bells straight. And that was only because he was feeling merciful.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:25:0:39"
msgid "I have some good news, and some bad news. The bad news is, in my haste to find an adventurer who could obtain the items Master Gegeruju requested, I failed to remember one of his many mottos─why have one of anything when you can have a dozen? The good news is, there is more coin to be made if you are interested. Say you are interested!"
msgstr "У меня для вас хорошие и плохие новости. Плохая в том, что, спеша найти искателя приключений, который добудет заказанные господином Гегеруджу товары, я забыл одно из его любимых изречений: зачем брать одну вещь, если можно взять дюжину? Хорошая новость — на этом можно заработать ещё монет. Если, конечно, вы согласны. Скажите, что согласны!"

#. ja: なるほど。<br>確かに注文していた数は受け取っていますから、<br>問題はありません。ありがとうございました。
#. de: Ich habe verstanden. Weiterhin viel Erfolg, <if $gn4>Fischerin<else>Fischer</if>!
#. fr: C'est tout à fait naturrrel. Vous avez déjà rempli vos engagements initiaux, et je vous en remercie.
#. column 36: Where have you <i>been</i>, my <if $gn4>dear lady<else>good fellow</if>? Please tell me you have the items I ordered.
#. column 37: Thank the Twelve. The world continues to turn, and your service to Master Gegeruju shall be remembered.
#. column 38: Oh, gods, no! Were you not informed of the urgency!? Dive in the water and use your hands if you must, but make haste! Haste, I say! Master Gegeruju does not tolerate three things in this world: being made to wait, being made to wait, and being made to wait!
#. column 39: I have some good news, and some bad news. The bad news is, in my haste to find an adventurer who could obtain the items Master Gegeruju requested, I failed to remember one of his many mottos─why have one of anything when you can have a dozen? The good news is, there is more coin to be made if you are interested. Say you are interested!
#. column 41: Oh, the relief! The last time I forgot to double an order of fish for the master, he had me stand in a corner with a ten-ponze bucket of offal on my head for five bells straight. And that was only because he was feeling merciful.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:25:0:40"
msgid "Then I can only pray that Master is too busy cuddling with his latest courtesan to notice the lack of cuisine."
msgstr "Тогда остаётся молиться, чтобы господин был слишком занят своей новой фавориткой и не заметил, что на столе не хватает еды."

#. ja: 柔軟な対応に感謝いたします。<br>それでは追加注文分を含めて、<br>報酬を支払いましょう。
#. de: Ich bin dir sehr dankbar. Deine Belohnung wird entsprechend angepasst werden.
#. fr: Je vous remercie d'avoir pu répondre à ma requête favorablement. Voici le paiement convenu, avec un supplément pour vos serrrvices.
#. column 36: Where have you <i>been</i>, my <if $gn4>dear lady<else>good fellow</if>? Please tell me you have the items I ordered.
#. column 37: Thank the Twelve. The world continues to turn, and your service to Master Gegeruju shall be remembered.
#. column 38: Oh, gods, no! Were you not informed of the urgency!? Dive in the water and use your hands if you must, but make haste! Haste, I say! Master Gegeruju does not tolerate three things in this world: being made to wait, being made to wait, and being made to wait!
#. column 39: I have some good news, and some bad news. The bad news is, in my haste to find an adventurer who could obtain the items Master Gegeruju requested, I failed to remember one of his many mottos─why have one of anything when you can have a dozen? The good news is, there is more coin to be made if you are interested. Say you are interested!
#. column 40: Then I can only pray that Master is too busy cuddling with his latest courtesan to notice the lack of cuisine.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:25:0:41"
msgid "Oh, the relief! The last time I forgot to double an order of fish for the master, he had me stand in a corner with a ten-ponze bucket of offal on my head for five bells straight. And that was only because he was feeling merciful."
msgstr "Фух, отлегло! В прошлый раз я забыл удвоить заказ рыбы для господина, и он заставил меня пять часов простоять в углу с ведром требухи на голове. И это ещё он был милостив!"

#. ja: 依頼を受けてくれてありがとう。<br>さっそくだけど、頼んでおいた品はあるかい？
#. de: Danke, dass du dich um den Auftrag gekümmert hast. Warst du erfolgreich?
#. fr: Ah, vous voilà. Trêve de bavardages, apportez-vous ce que j'ai demandé<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for with this fish, they will not know hunger.
#. column 38: I am but a lone skyfisher, and the Sea of Clouds can oft prove a harsh mistress. It is why I turn to the Adventurers' Guild to help me see my contracts with the valley families are met and that they do not starve. If the adventurer sent by the guild cannot complete <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> end of the agreement, then I may be forced to look elsewhere.
#. column 39: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for they will not know hunger this evening. Tomorrow, however, is another day... Unless, that is, I can somehow procure more skyfish.
#. column 40: That is alright. With the number of dragon attacks increasing by the day, there is no guarantee these families will even live to see tomorrow.
#. column 41: I thank you, and Coerthas thanks you...though it may not readily seem like it.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:26:0:36"
msgid "First, allow me to thank you for agreeing to this contract. The people of Coerthas can no longer turn away the aid of outsiders if they are to survive this everlasting winter the Calamity has brought."
msgstr "Прежде всего позвольте поблагодарить вас за согласие взяться за этот заказ. Чтобы пережить бесконечную зиму, которую принесло Бедствие, жителям Кёртаса больше нельзя отказываться от помощи чужаков."

#. ja: 助かったよ、ありがとう。<br>冒険者ギルドに頼んで正解だったよ。<br>約束の報酬を受け取ってくれ。
#. de: Prachtvoll! Die Aben<shy>teurer<shy>gilde kann stolz auf dich sein! Hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Je vous remercie. C'est bien de voir qu'il est possible de faire confiance à la guilde des aventuriers. Tenez, voici la récompense dont nous avions convenu.
#. column 36: First, allow me to thank you for agreeing to this contract. The people of Coerthas can no longer turn away the aid of outsiders if they are to survive this everlasting winter the Calamity has brought.
#. column 38: I am but a lone skyfisher, and the Sea of Clouds can oft prove a harsh mistress. It is why I turn to the Adventurers' Guild to help me see my contracts with the valley families are met and that they do not starve. If the adventurer sent by the guild cannot complete <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> end of the agreement, then I may be forced to look elsewhere.
#. column 39: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for they will not know hunger this evening. Tomorrow, however, is another day... Unless, that is, I can somehow procure more skyfish.
#. column 40: That is alright. With the number of dragon attacks increasing by the day, there is no guarantee these families will even live to see tomorrow.
#. column 41: I thank you, and Coerthas thanks you...though it may not readily seem like it.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:26:0:37"
msgid "Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for with this fish, they will not know hunger."
msgstr "Благодаря вашему усердию несколько семей не останутся голодными. С этой рыбой им будет что поесть."

#. ja: ところで、頼んでおいた品はあるかい？<br>もしよかったら、早めに用意してもらえると<br>助かるんだが……。
#. de: Was soll das heißen? Bitte beeile dich, ich drauche die Bestellung wirklich dringend!
#. fr: Alors, avez-vous apporté ce que j'ai commandé<nbsp>? Non<nbsp>? Bon, j'aimerais que vous vous dépêchiez un peu...
#. column 36: First, allow me to thank you for agreeing to this contract. The people of Coerthas can no longer turn away the aid of outsiders if they are to survive this everlasting winter the Calamity has brought.
#. column 37: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for with this fish, they will not know hunger.
#. column 39: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for they will not know hunger this evening. Tomorrow, however, is another day... Unless, that is, I can somehow procure more skyfish.
#. column 40: That is alright. With the number of dragon attacks increasing by the day, there is no guarantee these families will even live to see tomorrow.
#. column 41: I thank you, and Coerthas thanks you...though it may not readily seem like it.
#. macro: <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:26:0:38"
msgid "I am but a lone skyfisher, and the Sea of Clouds can oft prove a harsh mistress. It is why I turn to the Adventurers' Guild to help me see my contracts with the valley families are met and that they do not starve. If the adventurer sent by the guild cannot complete <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> end of the agreement, then I may be forced to look elsewhere."
msgstr "Я один промышляю небесной рыбалкой, а Море Облаков порой бывает суровой хозяйкой. Потому я и обращаюсь в Гильдию искателей приключений: она помогает мне выполнять договоры с семьями из долины, чтобы те не голодали. Если присланный гильдией искатель приключений не выполнит <if $gn4>свою<else>свою</if> часть сделки, мне, возможно, придётся искать кого-то ещё."

#. ja: 助かったよ、ありがとう。<br>ところで、追加注文をしたいんだが、<br>受けてはもらえるだろうか？
#. de: Du hast doch sicher noch ein Weilchen Zeit, um noch mehr davon zu besorgen, oder?
#. fr: Merci à vous, aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. Si cela ne vous embête pas, j'aimerais vous en demander un peu plus...
#. column 36: First, allow me to thank you for agreeing to this contract. The people of Coerthas can no longer turn away the aid of outsiders if they are to survive this everlasting winter the Calamity has brought.
#. column 37: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for with this fish, they will not know hunger.
#. column 38: I am but a lone skyfisher, and the Sea of Clouds can oft prove a harsh mistress. It is why I turn to the Adventurers' Guild to help me see my contracts with the valley families are met and that they do not starve. If the adventurer sent by the guild cannot complete <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> end of the agreement, then I may be forced to look elsewhere.
#. column 40: That is alright. With the number of dragon attacks increasing by the day, there is no guarantee these families will even live to see tomorrow.
#. column 41: I thank you, and Coerthas thanks you...though it may not readily seem like it.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:26:0:39"
msgid "Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for they will not know hunger this evening. Tomorrow, however, is another day... Unless, that is, I can somehow procure more skyfish."
msgstr "Благодаря вашему усердию несколько семей сегодня вечером не останутся голодными. Но завтра — новый день… если только мне не удастся раздобыть ещё небесной рыбы."

#. ja: そうか、残念だが仕方がない。<br>いや、気にしないでくれ、こちらで何とかするさ。
#. de: Wie dir beliebt. Mich kannst du jederzeit hier finden.
#. fr: Ah, vraiment<nbsp>? Dans ce cas, je vais essayer de trouver une autre solution. Merci encore.
#. column 36: First, allow me to thank you for agreeing to this contract. The people of Coerthas can no longer turn away the aid of outsiders if they are to survive this everlasting winter the Calamity has brought.
#. column 37: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for with this fish, they will not know hunger.
#. column 38: I am but a lone skyfisher, and the Sea of Clouds can oft prove a harsh mistress. It is why I turn to the Adventurers' Guild to help me see my contracts with the valley families are met and that they do not starve. If the adventurer sent by the guild cannot complete <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> end of the agreement, then I may be forced to look elsewhere.
#. column 39: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for they will not know hunger this evening. Tomorrow, however, is another day... Unless, that is, I can somehow procure more skyfish.
#. column 41: I thank you, and Coerthas thanks you...though it may not readily seem like it.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:26:0:40"
msgid "That is alright. With the number of dragon attacks increasing by the day, there is no guarantee these families will even live to see tomorrow."
msgstr "Ничего страшного. С каждым днём нападения драконов учащаются, и никто не знает, доживут ли эти семьи до завтра."

#. ja: 追加注文にまで応えてもらえるなんて、<br>なんてお礼を言っていいものやら。<br>ひとまず報酬という形で、応えさせてくれ。
#. de: Die Götter sollen dich beschützen! Danke für die Lieferung, hier ist deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Vous êtes décidément une personne sur qui on peut compter. Je ne manquerai pas de le faire savoir à la guilde des aventuriers.
#. column 36: First, allow me to thank you for agreeing to this contract. The people of Coerthas can no longer turn away the aid of outsiders if they are to survive this everlasting winter the Calamity has brought.
#. column 37: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for with this fish, they will not know hunger.
#. column 38: I am but a lone skyfisher, and the Sea of Clouds can oft prove a harsh mistress. It is why I turn to the Adventurers' Guild to help me see my contracts with the valley families are met and that they do not starve. If the adventurer sent by the guild cannot complete <if $gn4>her<else>his</if> end of the agreement, then I may be forced to look elsewhere.
#. column 39: Your diligence has seen the lives of several families saved, for they will not know hunger this evening. Tomorrow, however, is another day... Unless, that is, I can somehow procure more skyfish.
#. column 40: That is alright. With the number of dragon attacks increasing by the day, there is no guarantee these families will even live to see tomorrow.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:26:0:41"
msgid "I thank you, and Coerthas thanks you...though it may not readily seem like it."
msgstr "Благодарю вас. И весь Кёртас благодарен… хоть это и не всегда заметно."

#. ja: 依頼を受けてくれた冒険者だね？<br>極寒のホワイトブリムまで、よく来てくれた。<br>ところで、依頼した品は用意できたかい？
#. de: Das sieht man gerne, <if $gn4>eine Abenteurerin<else>ein Abenteurer</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>der</if> der Kälte trotzt. Hast du meine Bestellung dabei?
#. fr: Bien le <if ($gn11 < 12)><if ($gn11 < 4)>bonsoir<else>bonjour</if><else><if ($gn11 < 17)>bonjour<else>bonsoir</if></if>, ch<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if> aventuri<if $gn4>ère<else>er</if>. Je vous remercie de vous être déplacé<if $gn4>e</if> jusqu'ici. Que m'apportez-vous de beau<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Say what you will about the weather, the frigid air up here does wonders for preserving the freshness of dead flesh. I could leave this order of yours in a barrel outside and the fish would still taste as if they were caught yesterday.
#. column 38: I care not how long it takes for you to fulfill my order. Just know that I have many others in my employ, and every delivery <i>they</i> make is another sack of coin in <i>their</i> hands when it could have been in yours.
#. column 39: Now that I have seen true you are a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> for your word, might I suggest we increase the contract? The guild need not know. I am saved the hassle, and you can have their exorbitant finder's fee.
#. column 40: Color me unsurprised. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't want a reason to stay a moment longer in this damnable cold.
#. column 41: And here you are, the finder's fee included, just as promised.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:27:0:36"
msgid "The cold of this godsforsaken place has not discouraged you from fulfilling my order, has it?"
msgstr "Неужели холод в этом проклятом богами месте не помешал вам выполнить мой заказ?"

#. ja: これを待っていたんだ。<br>君たちのような漁師がいるからこそ、<br>私たちの商売も成り立つというものだよ。
#. de: Wunderbar. Ohne <if $gn4>Fischerinnen<else>Fischer</if> wie dich wäre unsere Profession schon am Ende.
#. fr: Oui, c'est ce que j'attendais<nbsp>! Heu<shy>reu<shy>se<shy>ment qu'il y a des pêcheurs comme vous pour que les gens comme moi puissent faire du commerce. Je vous remercie.
#. column 36: The cold of this godsforsaken place has not discouraged you from fulfilling my order, has it?
#. column 38: I care not how long it takes for you to fulfill my order. Just know that I have many others in my employ, and every delivery <i>they</i> make is another sack of coin in <i>their</i> hands when it could have been in yours.
#. column 39: Now that I have seen true you are a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> for your word, might I suggest we increase the contract? The guild need not know. I am saved the hassle, and you can have their exorbitant finder's fee.
#. column 40: Color me unsurprised. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't want a reason to stay a moment longer in this damnable cold.
#. column 41: And here you are, the finder's fee included, just as promised.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:27:0:37"
msgid "Say what you will about the weather, the frigid air up here does wonders for preserving the freshness of dead flesh. I could leave this order of yours in a barrel outside and the fish would still taste as if they were caught yesterday."
msgstr "Погода погодой, а здешний мороз отлично сохраняет свежесть мёртвой рыбы. Оставь я ваш заказ в бочке на улице — рыба всё равно была бы на вкус будто её поймали вчера."

#. ja: どうやら、依頼した品は、<br>まだ用意できていないようだね。<br>寒いとは思うが、一働きお願いするよ。
#. de: Hmm, da war ich wohl etwas zu voreilig. Die Kälte macht dir also doch zu schaffen. Gib dein Bestes, ich werde hier auf dich warten.
#. fr: Il semblerait que vous n'ayez pas pu préparer les mar<shy>chan<shy>di<shy>ses pour l'instant. J'imagine que vous devez être gelé<if $gn4>e</if>, mais je vous demande encore un petit effort.
#. column 36: The cold of this godsforsaken place has not discouraged you from fulfilling my order, has it?
#. column 37: Say what you will about the weather, the frigid air up here does wonders for preserving the freshness of dead flesh. I could leave this order of yours in a barrel outside and the fish would still taste as if they were caught yesterday.
#. column 39: Now that I have seen true you are a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> for your word, might I suggest we increase the contract? The guild need not know. I am saved the hassle, and you can have their exorbitant finder's fee.
#. column 40: Color me unsurprised. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't want a reason to stay a moment longer in this damnable cold.
#. column 41: And here you are, the finder's fee included, just as promised.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:27:0:38"
msgid "I care not how long it takes for you to fulfill my order. Just know that I have many others in my employ, and every delivery <i>they</i> make is another sack of coin in <i>their</i> hands when it could have been in yours."
msgstr "Мне всё равно, сколько времени займёт выполнение заказа. Только учтите: у меня полно других работников, и с каждой их поставкой ещё один мешок монет достаётся <i>им</i>, а мог бы достаться <i>вам</i>."

#. ja: 君の実直な働きぶりに敬意を示そう。<br>だが、もう少し甘えさせてもらえないだろうか？<br>追加の注文を受けてもらいたいのだよ。
#. de: Deinem Fleiß gebührt Hochachtung! Bist du bereit, noch eine weitere Bestellung zu erledigen?
#. fr: J'aime les gens pleins de bonne volonté comme vous. Puis-je abuser de votre patience et vous demander quelques unités sup<shy>plé<shy>men<shy>tai<shy>res<nbsp>?
#. column 36: The cold of this godsforsaken place has not discouraged you from fulfilling my order, has it?
#. column 37: Say what you will about the weather, the frigid air up here does wonders for preserving the freshness of dead flesh. I could leave this order of yours in a barrel outside and the fish would still taste as if they were caught yesterday.
#. column 38: I care not how long it takes for you to fulfill my order. Just know that I have many others in my employ, and every delivery <i>they</i> make is another sack of coin in <i>their</i> hands when it could have been in yours.
#. column 40: Color me unsurprised. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't want a reason to stay a moment longer in this damnable cold.
#. column 41: And here you are, the finder's fee included, just as promised.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:27:0:39"
msgid "Now that I have seen true you are a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> for your word, might I suggest we increase the contract? The guild need not know. I am saved the hassle, and you can have their exorbitant finder's fee."
msgstr "Теперь я вижу: вы <if $gn4>женщина<else>мужчина</if>, которая держит слово. Может, увеличим заказ? Гильдии знать необязательно. Мне не придётся хлопотать, а вы получите их непомерную плату за посредничество."

#. ja: ふむ、それでは致し方あるまい。<br>別の手で仕入れることにしよう。
#. de: Die Kälte verwirrt deine Gedanken. Das passiert hier so manchem.
#. fr: Très bien, je ne veux en aucun cas vous mettre la pression. Je m'adresserai à quelqu'un d'autre, voilà tout.
#. column 36: The cold of this godsforsaken place has not discouraged you from fulfilling my order, has it?
#. column 37: Say what you will about the weather, the frigid air up here does wonders for preserving the freshness of dead flesh. I could leave this order of yours in a barrel outside and the fish would still taste as if they were caught yesterday.
#. column 38: I care not how long it takes for you to fulfill my order. Just know that I have many others in my employ, and every delivery <i>they</i> make is another sack of coin in <i>their</i> hands when it could have been in yours.
#. column 39: Now that I have seen true you are a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> for your word, might I suggest we increase the contract? The guild need not know. I am saved the hassle, and you can have their exorbitant finder's fee.
#. column 41: And here you are, the finder's fee included, just as promised.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:27:0:40"
msgid "Color me unsurprised. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't want a reason to stay a moment longer in this damnable cold."
msgstr "Не удивлён. Будь я на вашем месте, тоже не стал бы задерживаться ни на миг в этом проклятом холоде."

#. ja: 君の真摯な働きぶりに敬意を示そう。<br>むろん気持ちだけではなく、報酬も上乗せしてね。
#. de: Es sei dir gedankt. Aber von Dank allein kann niemand leben, deshalb gibt es noch eine Belohnung obendrauf.
#. fr: J'admire votre abnégation. C'est un plaisir pour moi de travailler avec vous. Tenez, prenez ceci, vous l'avez amplement mérité.
#. column 36: The cold of this godsforsaken place has not discouraged you from fulfilling my order, has it?
#. column 37: Say what you will about the weather, the frigid air up here does wonders for preserving the freshness of dead flesh. I could leave this order of yours in a barrel outside and the fish would still taste as if they were caught yesterday.
#. column 38: I care not how long it takes for you to fulfill my order. Just know that I have many others in my employ, and every delivery <i>they</i> make is another sack of coin in <i>their</i> hands when it could have been in yours.
#. column 39: Now that I have seen true you are a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> for your word, might I suggest we increase the contract? The guild need not know. I am saved the hassle, and you can have their exorbitant finder's fee.
#. column 40: Color me unsurprised. If I were in your shoes, I wouldn't want a reason to stay a moment longer in this damnable cold.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:27:0:41"
msgid "And here you are, the finder's fee included, just as promised."
msgstr "А вот и вы — с платой за посредничество, как и договаривались."

#. ja: 冒険者ギルドの漁師さんだね？<br>依頼した品の納品だと嬉しいんだが……。
#. de: Du musst <if $gn4>die Fischerin<else>der Fischer</if> sein, auf <if $gn4>die<else>den</if> ich gewartet habe. Hast du den Auftrag ausgeführt?
#. fr: Salutations, mon ami<if $gn4>e</if>. Alors, la pêche a été bonne<nbsp>?
#. column 37: Ah, yes. Fish. Always fish, isn't it. I suppose I only have myself to blame, being the one writing up the orders and all.
#. column 38: My colleagues cannot be expected to make the discovery of a lifetime if forced to constantly battle hunger pangs. Find us those fish, friend, so that we may fill our bellies and fuel our minds.
#. column 39: My powers of deduction tell me you are quite adept with that rod of yours. Could I convince you to pull it out and take it in hand once more to service the Sons of Saint Coinach?
#. column 40: Might it have been how I worded the request?
#. column 41: Rarely am I wrong, but that does not make it feel any less good when I am right, and oh, how I was right to ask you to increase the order. Well done, adventurer. I have your reward right here.
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:28:0:36"
msgid "Even men of science must eat, but must we be made to forage for that sustenance ourselves? I think not. That is what <i>you</i> are for. Oh, uh... Not that the tasks you undertake are...uh, in any way...er, menial... Er...so...uh, what have you brought us today?"
msgstr "Даже учёным нужно есть. Но неужели нам самим приходится добывать пропитание? Вот уж нет. Для этого <i>вы</i> и нужны. Ой… Я не хотел сказать, что ваша работа… э-э… какая-то… низкая… В общем… что вы сегодня принесли?"

#. ja: うん、確かに受け取ったよ。<br>君みたいな漁師さんが、この仕事を引き受けてくれて、<br>本当に助かったよ。ありがとう！
#. de: Genau, wie ich es mir gewünscht habe. Vielen Dank. Mit dir hat deine Gilde einen Volltreffer gelandet.
#. fr: Eh bien oui, on dirait que tout y est. Quelle chance que la guilde des aventuriers m'ait envoyé quelqu'un comme vous<nbsp>! Je suis satisfait.
#. column 36: Even men of science must eat, but must we be made to forage for that sustenance ourselves? I think not. That is what <i>you</i> are for. Oh, uh... Not that the tasks you undertake are...uh, in any way...er, menial... Er...so...uh, what have you brought us today?
#. column 38: My colleagues cannot be expected to make the discovery of a lifetime if forced to constantly battle hunger pangs. Find us those fish, friend, so that we may fill our bellies and fuel our minds.
#. column 39: My powers of deduction tell me you are quite adept with that rod of yours. Could I convince you to pull it out and take it in hand once more to service the Sons of Saint Coinach?
#. column 40: Might it have been how I worded the request?
#. column 41: Rarely am I wrong, but that does not make it feel any less good when I am right, and oh, how I was right to ask you to increase the order. Well done, adventurer. I have your reward right here.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:28:0:37"
msgid "Ah, yes. Fish. Always fish, isn't it. I suppose I only have myself to blame, being the one writing up the orders and all."
msgstr "Ах да, рыба. Вечно эта рыба, да? Наверное, винить мне стоит только себя: это ведь я составляю заказы."

#. ja: あれ、依頼した品はどこだい？<br>てっきり、納品に来たのかと思ったんだが……。
#. de: Hast du etwa die ganze Zeit auf der faulen Haut gelegen? Beeil dich bitte.
#. fr: Hein<nbsp>? Où sont les poissons que j'ai commandés<nbsp>? Moi qui pensais que tout cela serait rapidement réglé...
#. column 36: Even men of science must eat, but must we be made to forage for that sustenance ourselves? I think not. That is what <i>you</i> are for. Oh, uh... Not that the tasks you undertake are...uh, in any way...er, menial... Er...so...uh, what have you brought us today?
#. column 37: Ah, yes. Fish. Always fish, isn't it. I suppose I only have myself to blame, being the one writing up the orders and all.
#. column 39: My powers of deduction tell me you are quite adept with that rod of yours. Could I convince you to pull it out and take it in hand once more to service the Sons of Saint Coinach?
#. column 40: Might it have been how I worded the request?
#. column 41: Rarely am I wrong, but that does not make it feel any less good when I am right, and oh, how I was right to ask you to increase the order. Well done, adventurer. I have your reward right here.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:28:0:38"
msgid "My colleagues cannot be expected to make the discovery of a lifetime if forced to constantly battle hunger pangs. Find us those fish, friend, so that we may fill our bellies and fuel our minds."
msgstr "Нельзя же ждать, что мои коллеги совершат великое открытие, если им постоянно приходится бороться с голодом. Достаньте нам рыбы, друг, чтобы мы набили животы и подпитали разум."

#. ja: 君って、漁師としてはかなりの腕前だよね？<br>その腕を見込んで、追加注文したいんだが……。
#. de: Mit Leuten wie dir macht man gerne Geschäfte. Willst du mir noch mehr davon bringen?
#. fr: Ce n'est pas tous les jours que j'ai la chance d'avoir un<if $gn4>e</if> pêcheu<if $gn4>se<else>r</if> comme vous à mon service. Puis-je vous demander un dernier effort<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Even men of science must eat, but must we be made to forage for that sustenance ourselves? I think not. That is what <i>you</i> are for. Oh, uh... Not that the tasks you undertake are...uh, in any way...er, menial... Er...so...uh, what have you brought us today?
#. column 37: Ah, yes. Fish. Always fish, isn't it. I suppose I only have myself to blame, being the one writing up the orders and all.
#. column 38: My colleagues cannot be expected to make the discovery of a lifetime if forced to constantly battle hunger pangs. Find us those fish, friend, so that we may fill our bellies and fuel our minds.
#. column 40: Might it have been how I worded the request?
#. column 41: Rarely am I wrong, but that does not make it feel any less good when I am right, and oh, how I was right to ask you to increase the order. Well done, adventurer. I have your reward right here.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:28:0:39"
msgid "My powers of deduction tell me you are quite adept with that rod of yours. Could I convince you to pull it out and take it in hand once more to service the Sons of Saint Coinach?"
msgstr "Моя дедукция подсказывает, что вы отлично управляетесь с удочкой. Не уговорить ли вас снова взять её в руки и послужить Сынам Святого Коинеха?"

#. ja: ……君がそう言うのであれば、<br>別ルートでの仕入れを考えるとしよう。
#. de: Gut, es gibt auch noch andere, die ich fragen kann.
#. fr: Évidemment... Vous devez être quelqu'un de très demandé, ce que je comprends. Ça sera pour une prochaine fois<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Even men of science must eat, but must we be made to forage for that sustenance ourselves? I think not. That is what <i>you</i> are for. Oh, uh... Not that the tasks you undertake are...uh, in any way...er, menial... Er...so...uh, what have you brought us today?
#. column 37: Ah, yes. Fish. Always fish, isn't it. I suppose I only have myself to blame, being the one writing up the orders and all.
#. column 38: My colleagues cannot be expected to make the discovery of a lifetime if forced to constantly battle hunger pangs. Find us those fish, friend, so that we may fill our bellies and fuel our minds.
#. column 39: My powers of deduction tell me you are quite adept with that rod of yours. Could I convince you to pull it out and take it in hand once more to service the Sons of Saint Coinach?
#. column 41: Rarely am I wrong, but that does not make it feel any less good when I am right, and oh, how I was right to ask you to increase the order. Well done, adventurer. I have your reward right here.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:28:0:40"
msgid "Might it have been how I worded the request?"
msgstr "Может, я просто не так сформулировал просьбу?"

#. ja: 君を頼ったのは正しかったようだ。<br>これだけの数があれば十分。<br>報酬も色を付けておこう。
#. de: Du bist <if $gn4>eine Lebensretterin<else>ein Lebensretter</if>. Vielen Dank. Ich hoffe, deine Belohnung stellt dich zufrieden.
#. fr: Que dire... Si seulement tout le monde travaillait aussi bien que vous<nbsp>! C'est un plaisir de vous payer, et de rajouter un bonus par-dessus le marché<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Even men of science must eat, but must we be made to forage for that sustenance ourselves? I think not. That is what <i>you</i> are for. Oh, uh... Not that the tasks you undertake are...uh, in any way...er, menial... Er...so...uh, what have you brought us today?
#. column 37: Ah, yes. Fish. Always fish, isn't it. I suppose I only have myself to blame, being the one writing up the orders and all.
#. column 38: My colleagues cannot be expected to make the discovery of a lifetime if forced to constantly battle hunger pangs. Find us those fish, friend, so that we may fill our bellies and fuel our minds.
#. column 39: My powers of deduction tell me you are quite adept with that rod of yours. Could I convince you to pull it out and take it in hand once more to service the Sons of Saint Coinach?
#. column 40: Might it have been how I worded the request?
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:28:0:41"
msgid "Rarely am I wrong, but that does not make it feel any less good when I am right, and oh, how I was right to ask you to increase the order. Well done, adventurer. I have your reward right here."
msgstr "Я редко ошибаюсь, но от этого не меньше приятно оказаться правым. И как же я был прав, попросив вас увеличить заказ! Отличная работа, искатель приключений. Вот ваша награда."

#. ja: あなたが依頼を受けてくれた職人か。<br>製作の方を、急いでくれたまえよ。
#. de: Du bist <if $gn4>die Handwerkerin<else>der Handwerker</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>der</if> den Auftrag übernommen hat? Dann bitte ich doch sehr um eine zügige Bearbeitung!
#. fr: C'est vous qui avez accepté notre demande<nbsp>? Je vous prie de vous dépêcher.
#. column 37: Impressive. You have proven yourself of great worth to the Holy See. I shall ready your recompense.
#. column 38: The lord commander did also mention that your ilk worked at your own pace. \<sigh>
#. column 39: You unbelievers never cease to amaze. How ones so unattuned to the word of the Fury can create things that can only be described as divine...I shall never understand. Yet, I would be a fool not to ask for more of your remarkable creations.
#. column 40: Hm... I seem to have spoken too soon.
#. column 41: Why, these are even better than I imagined. I shall inform the lord commander at once...ah, after I count out your payment, of course!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:29:0:36"
msgid "Many are wary of turning to outsiders and unbelievers for supplies, but the lord commander insists that the skill of lower Eorzea's craftsmen and women is unparalleled. I trust you will not disappoint?"
msgstr "Многие опасаются обращаться за припасами к чужакам и неверующим, но верховный командующий уверяет, что ремесленники Нижней Эорзеи непревзойдённы. Надеюсь, вы не подведёте?"

#. ja: 実に見事な品だ……。<br>まさに依頼にあった通りの物といえよう！
#. de: Hervorragende Arbeit. Genau so habe ich es mir vorgestellt. Vielen Dank!
#. fr: Oh, mais quel admirable travail<nbsp>! C'est exactement ce qu'il nous fallait comme qualité.
#. column 36: Many are wary of turning to outsiders and unbelievers for supplies, but the lord commander insists that the skill of lower Eorzea's craftsmen and women is unparalleled. I trust you will not disappoint?
#. column 38: The lord commander did also mention that your ilk worked at your own pace. \<sigh>
#. column 39: You unbelievers never cease to amaze. How ones so unattuned to the word of the Fury can create things that can only be described as divine...I shall never understand. Yet, I would be a fool not to ask for more of your remarkable creations.
#. column 40: Hm... I seem to have spoken too soon.
#. column 41: Why, these are even better than I imagined. I shall inform the lord commander at once...ah, after I count out your payment, of course!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:29:0:37"
msgid "Impressive. You have proven yourself of great worth to the Holy See. I shall ready your recompense."
msgstr "Впечатляет. Вы доказали, что Святому Престолу от вас немалая польза. Приготовлю вашу награду."

#. ja: どうやら依頼した品を持ってはいないようだな……。<br>製作の方を、急いでくれたまえよ。
#. de: Bitte erledige den Auftrag so schnell wie möglich. Wir haben ihn ja über die Freibriefe ausgeschrieben, gerade weil wir so dringend Hilfe benötigen.
#. fr: J'ai bien peur que vous n'ayez pas sur vous ce que nous vous avons demandé... Dépêchez, je vous prie<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Many are wary of turning to outsiders and unbelievers for supplies, but the lord commander insists that the skill of lower Eorzea's craftsmen and women is unparalleled. I trust you will not disappoint?
#. column 37: Impressive. You have proven yourself of great worth to the Holy See. I shall ready your recompense.
#. column 39: You unbelievers never cease to amaze. How ones so unattuned to the word of the Fury can create things that can only be described as divine...I shall never understand. Yet, I would be a fool not to ask for more of your remarkable creations.
#. column 40: Hm... I seem to have spoken too soon.
#. column 41: Why, these are even better than I imagined. I shall inform the lord commander at once...ah, after I count out your payment, of course!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:29:0:38"
msgid "The lord commander did also mention that your ilk worked at your own pace. \\<sigh>"
msgstr "Верховный командующий также упоминал, что такие, как вы, работают в своём темпе. \\<вздох>"

#. ja: 実に見事な品だ……。<br>その腕を見込んで、追加の仕事を頼んでもいいだろうか？<br>当然、報酬も上乗せさせてもらおう。
#. de: Hervorragende Arbeit. Genau so habe ich es mir vorgestellt. Kann ich dich vielleicht darum bitten, mir noch mehr davon zu bringen? Natürlich erhältst du einen Ausgleich dafür!
#. fr: C'est vraiment du bon travail, avec le niveau de qualité requis. Accepteriez-vous de faire un autre travail pour nous dans la foulée<nbsp>? Bien sûr, votre récompense sera à la hauteur de vos efforts.
#. column 36: Many are wary of turning to outsiders and unbelievers for supplies, but the lord commander insists that the skill of lower Eorzea's craftsmen and women is unparalleled. I trust you will not disappoint?
#. column 37: Impressive. You have proven yourself of great worth to the Holy See. I shall ready your recompense.
#. column 38: The lord commander did also mention that your ilk worked at your own pace. \<sigh>
#. column 40: Hm... I seem to have spoken too soon.
#. column 41: Why, these are even better than I imagined. I shall inform the lord commander at once...ah, after I count out your payment, of course!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:29:0:39"
msgid "You unbelievers never cease to amaze. How ones so unattuned to the word of the Fury can create things that can only be described as divine...I shall never understand. Yet, I would be a fool not to ask for more of your remarkable creations."
msgstr "Вы, неверующие, не перестаёте меня удивлять. Как можно, не внимая слову Фурии, создавать вещи, которые иначе как божественными не назовёшь… Этого мне никогда не понять. Но было бы глупо не попросить вас сделать ещё несколько таких замечательных изделий."

#. ja: ふむ、忙しいというのなら仕方がない。<br>またの機会に協力を頼むとしよう。
#. de: Verstehe. Als <if $gn4>Abenteurerin<else>Abenteurer</if> hast du natürlich genug um die Ohren. Falls du deine Meinung änderst, findest du mich hier!
#. fr: Écoutez, si vous n'avez pas le temps, nous ne pouvons pas vous y obliger. J'espère toutefois que vous nous ferez le plaisir de retravailler pour nous.
#. column 36: Many are wary of turning to outsiders and unbelievers for supplies, but the lord commander insists that the skill of lower Eorzea's craftsmen and women is unparalleled. I trust you will not disappoint?
#. column 37: Impressive. You have proven yourself of great worth to the Holy See. I shall ready your recompense.
#. column 38: The lord commander did also mention that your ilk worked at your own pace. \<sigh>
#. column 39: You unbelievers never cease to amaze. How ones so unattuned to the word of the Fury can create things that can only be described as divine...I shall never understand. Yet, I would be a fool not to ask for more of your remarkable creations.
#. column 41: Why, these are even better than I imagined. I shall inform the lord commander at once...ah, after I count out your payment, of course!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:29:0:40"
msgid "Hm... I seem to have spoken too soon."
msgstr "Хм… Кажется, я поторопился с выводами."

#. ja: これで十分な数がそろった！<br>助かった、わたしからも礼をさせてもらおう！
#. de: Ich danke dir vielmals für deine Hilfe! Deine Belohnung habe ich natürlich nicht vergessen.
#. fr: Oui, je crois bien que le compte y est<nbsp>! Merci énormément. Voici votre dû<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Many are wary of turning to outsiders and unbelievers for supplies, but the lord commander insists that the skill of lower Eorzea's craftsmen and women is unparalleled. I trust you will not disappoint?
#. column 37: Impressive. You have proven yourself of great worth to the Holy See. I shall ready your recompense.
#. column 38: The lord commander did also mention that your ilk worked at your own pace. \<sigh>
#. column 39: You unbelievers never cease to amaze. How ones so unattuned to the word of the Fury can create things that can only be described as divine...I shall never understand. Yet, I would be a fool not to ask for more of your remarkable creations.
#. column 40: Hm... I seem to have spoken too soon.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:29:0:41"
msgid "Why, these are even better than I imagined. I shall inform the lord commander at once...ah, after I count out your payment, of course!"
msgstr "Да они даже лучше, чем я ожидал! Надо немедленно доложить верховному командующему… А, сначала, конечно, выдать вам плату!"

#. ja: 依頼を受けてくださった、漁師の方ですね？<br>それでは、さっそく品物をいただけますでしょうか。
#. de: Du musst <if $gn4>die Fischerin<else>der Fischer</if> sein, <if $gn4>die<else>der</if> den Auftrag übernommen hat, ja? Hast du ihn schon ausgeführt?
#. fr: C'est vous qui avez accepté notre demande, n'est-ce pas<nbsp>? Avez-vous apporté ce que nous voulons<nbsp>?
#. column 37: These will make quite the meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Let me prepare your reward.
#. column 38: Well, then why are you not out fishing? There are hungry mouths that long to be fed!
#. column 39: Beautiful! These will make an amazing meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Unless...you were to bring me more. There appears to be some coin left over from the first order that I'm certain Sister Amianne will not be missing. What say you? Fancy another cast?
#. column 40: Ah, well... Thankfully my lack of good fortune is offset by the city<hyphen>state's abundance of able fishers.
#. column 41: Oh, how I have longed for something other than beet soup, and now, thanks to your kindness and the Minister of Coin's negligence, I shall have it─beet soup with fish!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:30:0:36"
msgid "I never met a fish I did not like...just a great deal many I couldn't catch...which is why I hired you! Have you brought me what I asked?"
msgstr "Я ещё не встречал рыбы, которая мне не нравилась… Хотя поймать удавалось далеко не всякую. Вот потому-то я вас и нанял! Принесли, что я просил?"

#. ja: 確かに依頼していた品ですね。<br>実直な働きには、報酬をもってお応えしましょう。
#. de: Hervorragend! Vielen Dank! Du machst der Fischergilde alle Ehre.
#. fr: Oui, c'est exactement ce qu'il nous faut<nbsp>! Une chance qu'il y ait des pêcheurs de votre envergure par ici. Je vais récompenser vos efforts à leur juste valeur.
#. column 36: I never met a fish I did not like...just a great deal many I couldn't catch...which is why I hired you! Have you brought me what I asked?
#. column 38: Well, then why are you not out fishing? There are hungry mouths that long to be fed!
#. column 39: Beautiful! These will make an amazing meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Unless...you were to bring me more. There appears to be some coin left over from the first order that I'm certain Sister Amianne will not be missing. What say you? Fancy another cast?
#. column 40: Ah, well... Thankfully my lack of good fortune is offset by the city<hyphen>state's abundance of able fishers.
#. column 41: Oh, how I have longed for something other than beet soup, and now, thanks to your kindness and the Minister of Coin's negligence, I shall have it─beet soup with fish!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:30:0:37"
msgid "These will make quite the meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Let me prepare your reward."
msgstr "Из этого выйдет отличный обед! Жаль, что есть его буду не я. Позвольте приготовить вашу награду."

#. ja: おや、依頼した品物をお持ちでないようですが？
#. de: Immer noch nicht? Langsam würde ich mir doch wünschen, dass du dich an den Auftrag machst ...
#. fr: J'ai comme qui dirait l'impression que vous avez oublié le plus important... notre commande<nbsp>!
#. column 36: I never met a fish I did not like...just a great deal many I couldn't catch...which is why I hired you! Have you brought me what I asked?
#. column 37: These will make quite the meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Let me prepare your reward.
#. column 39: Beautiful! These will make an amazing meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Unless...you were to bring me more. There appears to be some coin left over from the first order that I'm certain Sister Amianne will not be missing. What say you? Fancy another cast?
#. column 40: Ah, well... Thankfully my lack of good fortune is offset by the city<hyphen>state's abundance of able fishers.
#. column 41: Oh, how I have longed for something other than beet soup, and now, thanks to your kindness and the Minister of Coin's negligence, I shall have it─beet soup with fish!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:30:0:38"
msgid "Well, then why are you not out fishing? There are hungry mouths that long to be fed!"
msgstr "Тогда почему вы ещё не на рыбалке? Столько голодных ртов ждут еды!"

#. ja: なかなかの腕利きのようですね。<br>もしよろしければ、追加の依頼をしたいのですが……。
#. de: Wie sieht es aus? Kannst du mir vielleicht noch mehr davon besorgen?
#. fr: Écoutez, ce que vous m'apportez me satisfait pleinement, mais j'aimerais vous demander un petit supplément, si vous le voulez bien...
#. column 36: I never met a fish I did not like...just a great deal many I couldn't catch...which is why I hired you! Have you brought me what I asked?
#. column 37: These will make quite the meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Let me prepare your reward.
#. column 38: Well, then why are you not out fishing? There are hungry mouths that long to be fed!
#. column 40: Ah, well... Thankfully my lack of good fortune is offset by the city<hyphen>state's abundance of able fishers.
#. column 41: Oh, how I have longed for something other than beet soup, and now, thanks to your kindness and the Minister of Coin's negligence, I shall have it─beet soup with fish!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:30:0:39"
msgid "Beautiful! These will make an amazing meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Unless...you were to bring me more. There appears to be some coin left over from the first order that I'm certain Sister Amianne will not be missing. What say you? Fancy another cast?"
msgstr "Прекрасно! Из них получится чудесный обед. Жаль только, что не мне его есть. Хотя… если вы принесёте ещё, то, пожалуй, и мне достанется. После первого заказа осталось немного монет, сестра Амианна вряд ли заметит пропажу. Ну что скажете? Забросите удочку ещё раз?"

#. ja: 残念ですが、仕方がありません。<br>別の漁師を探してみることにしますね。
#. de: Nein? Verstehe. Dann suche ich mir eben <if $gn4>eine andere Fischerin<else>einen anderen Fischer</if>.
#. fr: Vous ne pouvez pas<nbsp>? Eh bien, ce n'est pas grave. Je trouverai sûrement quelqu'un d'autre, qui acceptera à votre place...
#. column 36: I never met a fish I did not like...just a great deal many I couldn't catch...which is why I hired you! Have you brought me what I asked?
#. column 37: These will make quite the meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Let me prepare your reward.
#. column 38: Well, then why are you not out fishing? There are hungry mouths that long to be fed!
#. column 39: Beautiful! These will make an amazing meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Unless...you were to bring me more. There appears to be some coin left over from the first order that I'm certain Sister Amianne will not be missing. What say you? Fancy another cast?
#. column 41: Oh, how I have longed for something other than beet soup, and now, thanks to your kindness and the Minister of Coin's negligence, I shall have it─beet soup with fish!
#. macro: <hyphen> — a hyphen that does not break the line (may be added or dropped)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:30:0:40"
msgid "Ah, well... Thankfully my lack of good fortune is offset by the city<hyphen>state's abundance of able fishers."
msgstr "Ну что ж… К счастью, нехватку удачи с лихвой восполняют умелые рыбаки города-государства."

#. ja: ありがとうございます。<br>素晴らしい仕事ぶりでした。<br>約束通り、報酬も上乗せさせていただきますね。
#. de: Vielen Dank! Das sollte erst einmal reichen. Und hier natürlich deine Belohnung!
#. fr: Merci infiniment<nbsp>! Vous avez fait un excellent travail<nbsp>! Tenez, voici la récompense promise.
#. column 36: I never met a fish I did not like...just a great deal many I couldn't catch...which is why I hired you! Have you brought me what I asked?
#. column 37: These will make quite the meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Let me prepare your reward.
#. column 38: Well, then why are you not out fishing? There are hungry mouths that long to be fed!
#. column 39: Beautiful! These will make an amazing meal! A pity it will not be me dining on them. Unless...you were to bring me more. There appears to be some coin left over from the first order that I'm certain Sister Amianne will not be missing. What say you? Fancy another cast?
#. column 40: Ah, well... Thankfully my lack of good fortune is offset by the city<hyphen>state's abundance of able fishers.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:30:0:41"
msgid "Oh, how I have longed for something other than beet soup, and now, thanks to your kindness and the Minister of Coin's negligence, I shall have it─beet soup with fish!"
msgstr "Ах, как же я мечтал о чём-нибудь кроме свекольного супа! И вот, благодаря вашей доброте и рассеянности министра финансов, наконец-то получу его… свекольный суп с рыбой!"

#. ja: 依頼した品が完成したら、持って来ておくれ。<br>お客さんも、きっとお待ちかねだからね。
#. de: Alles, was du wissen musst, steht in dem Freibrief, einschließlich der geforderten Menge und Qualität. Wenn du deine Arbeit vollrichtet hast, liefere die Waren bei mir ab und ich lasse sie zum Kunden liefern.
#. fr: Quand vous aurez récupéré les produits pour les mandats, n'hésitez pas à me les apporter. Je suis certaine que nos clients sont impatients de recevoir leur commande.
#. column 37: You have outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. The client will be most pleased.
#. column 38: I understand that myriad adventures hither and thither across the realm can keep a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> from <i>lesser</i> duties such as these, but I ask that you remember many of your clients' livelihoods depend on the timely completion of their requests.
#. column 39: You've outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! In fact, I believe it is reasonable to venture that this delivery will please the client greatly─which brings me to my next proposal. In such cases, I have been instructed to offer the opportunity to create more...for an additional compensation, of course. Would such a task be of interest to you?
#. column 40: Of course. There are others who would gladly accept the petition.
#. column 41: On behalf of the client, I thank you. Compensation for the additional work has been added to your payment.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:31:0:36"
msgid "Everything you need to know about the request is indicated on the slip of parchment provided with the leve plate, including quantity and quality. When you have completed your work, you may deliver it to me, and I shall see it makes it into the hands of the client."
msgstr "Всё необходимое указано на записке, приложенной к доске с жетоном заказа: и количество, и качество. Когда закончите работу, отнесите её мне, а я прослежу, чтобы заказ попал к клиенту."

#. ja: さすがは自信があるだけあるね。<br>この品なら、お客さんも満足してくれるだろうさ。
#. de: Du hast dich wirklich selbst übertroffen, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Der Kunde wird sicher begeistert sein.
#. fr: C'est une belle livraison que vous me faites là<nbsp>! Continuez comme ça et les clients ne seront jamais déçus.
#. column 36: Everything you need to know about the request is indicated on the slip of parchment provided with the leve plate, including quantity and quality. When you have completed your work, you may deliver it to me, and I shall see it makes it into the hands of the client.
#. column 38: I understand that myriad adventures hither and thither across the realm can keep a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> from <i>lesser</i> duties such as these, but I ask that you remember many of your clients' livelihoods depend on the timely completion of their requests.
#. column 39: You've outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! In fact, I believe it is reasonable to venture that this delivery will please the client greatly─which brings me to my next proposal. In such cases, I have been instructed to offer the opportunity to create more...for an additional compensation, of course. Would such a task be of interest to you?
#. column 40: Of course. There are others who would gladly accept the petition.
#. column 41: On behalf of the client, I thank you. Compensation for the additional work has been added to your payment.
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:31:0:37"
msgid "You have outdone yourself, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. The client will be most pleased."
msgstr "Вы превзошли себя, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Клиент будет очень доволен."

#. ja: おや、依頼した品がないみたいだが……<br>さては作ったはいいが、持ってくるのを忘れたね？
#. de: Ich verstehe ja, dass da draußen noch andere Abenteuer auf <if $gn4>eine Frau<else>einen Mann</if> wie dich warten. Aber meine Kunden sind dringend auf die gewünschten Waren angewiesen. Für manche geht es sogar um ihre Existenz, vergiss das nicht.
#. fr: Hum... Vous n'avez visiblement aucune commande de prête. Je ne doute pas du fait que vous avez été très occupé<if $gn4>e</if>, mais il ne faut pas pour autant délaisser nos clients...
#. column 36: Everything you need to know about the request is indicated on the slip of parchment provided with the leve plate, including quantity and quality. When you have completed your work, you may deliver it to me, and I shall see it makes it into the hands of the client.
#. column 37: You have outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. The client will be most pleased.
#. column 39: You've outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! In fact, I believe it is reasonable to venture that this delivery will please the client greatly─which brings me to my next proposal. In such cases, I have been instructed to offer the opportunity to create more...for an additional compensation, of course. Would such a task be of interest to you?
#. column 40: Of course. There are others who would gladly accept the petition.
#. column 41: On behalf of the client, I thank you. Compensation for the additional work has been added to your payment.
#. macro: <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> — shows the first branch when the condition holds, otherwise the branch after <else>; condition = global number 4 (1 when the player character is female, 0 when male) (condition: may be reworded, restructured, added, or dropped)
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:31:0:38"
msgid "I understand that myriad adventures hither and thither across the realm can keep a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> from <i>lesser</i> duties such as these, but I ask that you remember many of your clients' livelihoods depend on the timely completion of their requests."
msgstr "Я понимаю, что бесчисленные приключения по всему свету могут отвлекать <if $gn4>женщину<else>мужчину</if> от <i>мелких</i> поручений вроде этого. Но помните: от своевременного выполнения заказов порой зависит благополучие клиентов."

#. ja: この品なら、お客さんも満足してくれるだろうさ。<br>ところで、追加の仕事があるんだが……やってくかい？<br>もちろん報酬の方も、ドンと追加させてもらうよ。
#. de: Du hast dich selbst übertroffen, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! Ich bin mir sicher, dass der Kunde sehr zufrieden sein wird. <i>Sehr</i> zufrieden. Stücke von dieser Qualität kann ich immer verkaufen. Würdest du noch mehr davon machen? Gegen ein entsprechendes Entgelt, versteht sich.
#. fr: Voilà qui va faire plaisir à la personne qui attendait sa commande. D'ailleurs, elle nous en a passé une autre<nbsp>! Si ça vous intéresse, le mandat est pour vous. Il y aura évidemment une autre récompense à la clef<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Everything you need to know about the request is indicated on the slip of parchment provided with the leve plate, including quantity and quality. When you have completed your work, you may deliver it to me, and I shall see it makes it into the hands of the client.
#. column 37: You have outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. The client will be most pleased.
#. column 38: I understand that myriad adventures hither and thither across the realm can keep a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> from <i>lesser</i> duties such as these, but I ask that you remember many of your clients' livelihoods depend on the timely completion of their requests.
#. column 40: Of course. There are others who would gladly accept the petition.
#. column 41: On behalf of the client, I thank you. Compensation for the additional work has been added to your payment.
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:31:0:39"
msgid "You've outdone yourself, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>! In fact, I believe it is reasonable to venture that this delivery will please the client greatly─which brings me to my next proposal. In such cases, I have been instructed to offer the opportunity to create more...for an additional compensation, of course. Would such a task be of interest to you?"
msgstr "Вы превзошли себя, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>! Уверен, клиент будет в восторге от этой поставки. И вот что я хотел предложить: в таких случаях мне велено предложить вам изготовить ещё. Разумеется, за дополнительную плату. Интересуетесь?"

#. ja: 無理を言って悪かったね。<br>また時間があるときにでも、手伝っておくれ。
#. de: Ich verstehe. Du hast schon genug geleistet.
#. fr: Désolée, je vois que vous n'êtes pas intéressé<if $gn4>e</if>. Peut-être une autre fois, quand vous aurez plus de temps<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Everything you need to know about the request is indicated on the slip of parchment provided with the leve plate, including quantity and quality. When you have completed your work, you may deliver it to me, and I shall see it makes it into the hands of the client.
#. column 37: You have outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. The client will be most pleased.
#. column 38: I understand that myriad adventures hither and thither across the realm can keep a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> from <i>lesser</i> duties such as these, but I ask that you remember many of your clients' livelihoods depend on the timely completion of their requests.
#. column 39: You've outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! In fact, I believe it is reasonable to venture that this delivery will please the client greatly─which brings me to my next proposal. In such cases, I have been instructed to offer the opportunity to create more...for an additional compensation, of course. Would such a task be of interest to you?
#. column 41: On behalf of the client, I thank you. Compensation for the additional work has been added to your payment.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:31:0:40"
msgid "Of course. There are others who would gladly accept the petition."
msgstr "Разумеется. Есть и другие, кто с радостью возьмётся за это поручение."

#. ja: ありがとう、これだけあればバッチリさ。<br>約束通り、報酬にも色をつけておくからね。
#. de: Ich danke dir, auch im Namen meines Kunden. Du hast dir die zusätzliche Vergütung redlich verdient.
#. fr: Parfait<nbsp>! Pour vous remercier, une compensation a été ajoutée à votre récompense...
#. column 36: Everything you need to know about the request is indicated on the slip of parchment provided with the leve plate, including quantity and quality. When you have completed your work, you may deliver it to me, and I shall see it makes it into the hands of the client.
#. column 37: You have outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. The client will be most pleased.
#. column 38: I understand that myriad adventures hither and thither across the realm can keep a <if $gn4>woman<else>man</if> from <i>lesser</i> duties such as these, but I ask that you remember many of your clients' livelihoods depend on the timely completion of their requests.
#. column 39: You've outdone yourself, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>! In fact, I believe it is reasonable to venture that this delivery will please the client greatly─which brings me to my next proposal. In such cases, I have been instructed to offer the opportunity to create more...for an additional compensation, of course. Would such a task be of interest to you?
#. column 40: Of course. There are others who would gladly accept the petition.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:31:0:41"
msgid "On behalf of the client, I thank you. Compensation for the additional work has been added to your payment."
msgstr "От имени клиента благодарю вас. Дополнительная работа оплачена."

#. ja: リーヴを引き受けてくれた、漁師さんですよね？<br>依頼品を獲ってきたなら、受け取りますよ！
#. de: Sag, bist du <if $gn4>die Fischerin<else>der Fischer</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>der</if> bei den Erlassen helf'n will? Das lob ich mir! Wenn es mehr von deinem Schlag gäb', wär die Welt nicht halb so verrucht. Also, wenn du dein'n Fang gemacht hast, dann komm hier vorbei und wir besprech'n den Rest.
#. fr: C'est vous <if $gn4>la pêcheuse<else>le pêcheur</if> qui a accepté de remplir certains mandats, non<nbsp>? Si vous avez des prises à livrer, c'est à moi qu'il faut les amener<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Aye, everything seems in order. I reckon you'll be wantin' that recompense was promised, like. Fear not, for I have it right here.
#. column 38: The salt air may have pickled me brain a mite, but me eyes, they 'aven't fooled me yet. Come back when you've what was asked of you.
#. column 39: Aye, seems both Navigator and Matron did smile upon you this fine day. There be more 'an enough 'ere to set us straight, but if you're lookin' to make a few extra coins, might be I's lookin' for a few more fish...
#. column 40: Never you mind, then. Another'll be along to bite. Heh heh.
#. column 41: Never seen a more able fisher than you, friend. I fancy you had these in your nets in less time than it takes to fillet a flounder. And no, I don't just say that to all me clients. Swear it on Thal's left ball!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:32:0:36"
msgid "You must be the fisher what agreed to help with the levequest! 'Tis kind souls like yourself what keep this realm from fallin' into chaos. Once you've bagged the catch, bring 'er to me and I'll see 'er where she needs to be."
msgstr "Ты, должно быть, рыбак, согласившийся помочь с поручением! Такие добрые души, как ты, не дают миру погрязнуть в хаосе. Наловишь рыбы — приноси её мне, а уж я позабочусь, чтобы она попала куда надо."

#. ja: うんうん、依頼品は全部そろっているようです。<br>お疲れ様でした、報酬をお渡ししますね！
#. de: Jau, sieht alles gut aus. Und hier ist auch die versproch'ne Belohnung. Soll ja keiner umsonst arbeit'n.
#. fr: Bien, bien, bien... Tout y est<nbsp>! Vous avez bien mérité votre récompense.
#. column 36: You must be the fisher what agreed to help with the levequest! 'Tis kind souls like yourself what keep this realm from fallin' into chaos. Once you've bagged the catch, bring 'er to me and I'll see 'er where she needs to be.
#. column 38: The salt air may have pickled me brain a mite, but me eyes, they 'aven't fooled me yet. Come back when you've what was asked of you.
#. column 39: Aye, seems both Navigator and Matron did smile upon you this fine day. There be more 'an enough 'ere to set us straight, but if you're lookin' to make a few extra coins, might be I's lookin' for a few more fish...
#. column 40: Never you mind, then. Another'll be along to bite. Heh heh.
#. column 41: Never seen a more able fisher than you, friend. I fancy you had these in your nets in less time than it takes to fillet a flounder. And no, I don't just say that to all me clients. Swear it on Thal's left ball!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:32:0:37"
msgid "Aye, everything seems in order. I reckon you'll be wantin' that recompense was promised, like. Fear not, for I have it right here."
msgstr "Ага, всё вроде на месте. Наверное, ждёшь обещанную плату. Не бойся, она уже здесь."

#. ja: うんうん、依頼品は全部そろって……ないじゃないですか！<br>もう、頼みますよ、本当に……。
#. de: Was ist? Kein Glück gehabt? Macht ja nichts, kann ja nicht immer alles glatt lauf'n. Komm wieder, wenn du dein'n Fang gemacht hast.
#. fr: Bien, bien, bien... La commande... n'est absolument pas prête<nbsp>! Courage, c'est juste un petit effort à fournir<nbsp>!
#. column 36: You must be the fisher what agreed to help with the levequest! 'Tis kind souls like yourself what keep this realm from fallin' into chaos. Once you've bagged the catch, bring 'er to me and I'll see 'er where she needs to be.
#. column 37: Aye, everything seems in order. I reckon you'll be wantin' that recompense was promised, like. Fear not, for I have it right here.
#. column 39: Aye, seems both Navigator and Matron did smile upon you this fine day. There be more 'an enough 'ere to set us straight, but if you're lookin' to make a few extra coins, might be I's lookin' for a few more fish...
#. column 40: Never you mind, then. Another'll be along to bite. Heh heh.
#. column 41: Never seen a more able fisher than you, friend. I fancy you had these in your nets in less time than it takes to fillet a flounder. And no, I don't just say that to all me clients. Swear it on Thal's left ball!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:32:0:38"
msgid "The salt air may have pickled me brain a mite, but me eyes, they 'aven't fooled me yet. Come back when you've what was asked of you."
msgstr "Морской воздух, может, и засолил мне мозги, но глаза меня ещё не подводили. Возвращайся, когда принесёшь всё, что просили."

#. ja: うんうん、依頼品は全部そろっているようです。<br>ところで追加の依頼とかって、興味あったりしますか？
#. de: Jau, Llymlaen und Nophica mein'n es gut mit dir. Du hast mehr als genug gefang'n. Wenn du willst, nehm ich dir den Rest auch noch ab. Gegen bare Münze, versteht sich.
#. fr: Bien, bien, bien... Tout a l'air en ordre. Maintenant que vous avez effectué cette commande, seriez-vous intéressé<if $gn4>e</if> par un autre mandat<nbsp>?
#. column 36: You must be the fisher what agreed to help with the levequest! 'Tis kind souls like yourself what keep this realm from fallin' into chaos. Once you've bagged the catch, bring 'er to me and I'll see 'er where she needs to be.
#. column 37: Aye, everything seems in order. I reckon you'll be wantin' that recompense was promised, like. Fear not, for I have it right here.
#. column 38: The salt air may have pickled me brain a mite, but me eyes, they 'aven't fooled me yet. Come back when you've what was asked of you.
#. column 40: Never you mind, then. Another'll be along to bite. Heh heh.
#. column 41: Never seen a more able fisher than you, friend. I fancy you had these in your nets in less time than it takes to fillet a flounder. And no, I don't just say that to all me clients. Swear it on Thal's left ball!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:32:0:39"
msgid "Aye, seems both Navigator and Matron did smile upon you this fine day. There be more 'an enough 'ere to set us straight, but if you're lookin' to make a few extra coins, might be I's lookin' for a few more fish..."
msgstr "Вижу, сегодня и Навигатор, и Матрона тебе благоволят. Рыбы здесь с избытком. А если хочешь подзаработать, мне бы ещё немного…"

#. ja: あらら、残念です……。<br>仕方ないので、あとでこっそり、私が釣ってきましょう。
#. de: Dann eben nicht. 'S ist ja deine Entscheidung.
#. fr: Quel dommage<nbsp>! Mais bon, tant pis... Pour être tout à fait honnête, j'étais justement en train de me dire que je pourrais très bien remplir ce mandat moi-même. Il faudrait juste que je trouve cinq minutes pour sortir ma canne et m'en occuper<nbsp>!
#. column 36: You must be the fisher what agreed to help with the levequest! 'Tis kind souls like yourself what keep this realm from fallin' into chaos. Once you've bagged the catch, bring 'er to me and I'll see 'er where she needs to be.
#. column 37: Aye, everything seems in order. I reckon you'll be wantin' that recompense was promised, like. Fear not, for I have it right here.
#. column 38: The salt air may have pickled me brain a mite, but me eyes, they 'aven't fooled me yet. Come back when you've what was asked of you.
#. column 39: Aye, seems both Navigator and Matron did smile upon you this fine day. There be more 'an enough 'ere to set us straight, but if you're lookin' to make a few extra coins, might be I's lookin' for a few more fish...
#. column 41: Never seen a more able fisher than you, friend. I fancy you had these in your nets in less time than it takes to fillet a flounder. And no, I don't just say that to all me clients. Swear it on Thal's left ball!
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:32:0:40"
msgid "Never you mind, then. Another'll be along to bite. Heh heh."
msgstr "Ну ладно, не беда. Клюнет кто-нибудь другой. Хе-хе."

#. ja: ご協力に感謝します！<br>おかげで無事に、必要な数がそろいました。<br>追加ぶんを含めて、多めに報酬をお渡ししますね！
#. de: Du kannst was, soviel ist klar. Und schnell bist du auch. Vielleicht bist du <if $gn4>die beste Fischerin<else>der beste Fischer</if>, <if $gn4>die<else>den</if> ich je geseh'n habe. Doch, ich schwör's! \<spuck> Leck auf, schwimm durch!
#. fr: Merci à vous<nbsp>! Je suis épatée par votre travail. Vous faites toujours de belles prises comme ça<nbsp>? Bref, voilà votre récompense, avec un petit plus en compensation<nbsp>!
#. column 36: You must be the fisher what agreed to help with the levequest! 'Tis kind souls like yourself what keep this realm from fallin' into chaos. Once you've bagged the catch, bring 'er to me and I'll see 'er where she needs to be.
#. column 37: Aye, everything seems in order. I reckon you'll be wantin' that recompense was promised, like. Fear not, for I have it right here.
#. column 38: The salt air may have pickled me brain a mite, but me eyes, they 'aven't fooled me yet. Come back when you've what was asked of you.
#. column 39: Aye, seems both Navigator and Matron did smile upon you this fine day. There be more 'an enough 'ere to set us straight, but if you're lookin' to make a few extra coins, might be I's lookin' for a few more fish...
#. column 40: Never you mind, then. Another'll be along to bite. Heh heh.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:32:0:41"
msgid "Never seen a more able fisher than you, friend. I fancy you had these in your nets in less time than it takes to fillet a flounder. And no, I don't just say that to all me clients. Swear it on Thal's left ball!"
msgstr "Не встречал рыбака способнее тебя, друг. Похоже, ты выловил это быстрее, чем успевают разделать камбалу. И нет, я так каждому клиенту не говорю. Клянусь левым яйцом Тала!"

#. ja: 指定された品は完成したかい？<br>製作が終わったら、ここに持ってきておくれ！
#. de: Hast du deine Arbeit erledigt? Ich nehme alles entgegen, was du für die Manufaktur herstellst.
#. fr: Vous avez rempli la commande pour le mandat que vous avez accepté<nbsp>? Si c'est le cas, je vous prie de l'apporter ici<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Yes, this appears to fit the bill. No issues as far as I can see.
#. column 38: Ah, weren't you supposed to bring me something? Don't tell me you've forgotten...?
#. column 39: Well done, well done. Though...if it's no imposition, could you bring us more? You would be duly compensated, of course.
#. column 40: I quite understand. We would be more than happy to abide by the original terms of the arrangement.
#. column 41: Thank you so very much! Please accept this additional payment with my compliments.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:33:0:36"
msgid "Have you completed the commission yet? I will be here, ready and waiting until you have."
msgstr "Заказ уже готов? Я буду здесь и стану ждать, пока вы его не принесёте."

#. ja: うん、依頼どおりの仕事ぶりだね。<br>これなら、何の問題もないよ。
#. de: Gut, alles wie bestellt. Die Gemeinschaft dankt.
#. fr: Oui, c'est bien ce qui était stipulé dans le mandat. Vous avez bien mérité votre récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed the commission yet? I will be here, ready and waiting until you have.
#. column 38: Ah, weren't you supposed to bring me something? Don't tell me you've forgotten...?
#. column 39: Well done, well done. Though...if it's no imposition, could you bring us more? You would be duly compensated, of course.
#. column 40: I quite understand. We would be more than happy to abide by the original terms of the arrangement.
#. column 41: Thank you so very much! Please accept this additional payment with my compliments.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:33:0:37"
msgid "Yes, this appears to fit the bill. No issues as far as I can see."
msgstr "Да, похоже, всё как заказывали. Проблем не вижу."

#. ja: ええっと、依頼した品はどこだい？<br>もしかして、どこかに忘れてきたとか……？
#. de: Äh, und wo ist dein Meisterwerk? Du hast es doch nicht irgendwo liegen gelassen?
#. fr: Euh... Où est l'article qui vous a été demandé<nbsp>? Ne me dites pas que vous l'avez oublié, quand même<nbsp>!<nbsp>...
#. column 36: Have you completed the commission yet? I will be here, ready and waiting until you have.
#. column 37: Yes, this appears to fit the bill. No issues as far as I can see.
#. column 39: Well done, well done. Though...if it's no imposition, could you bring us more? You would be duly compensated, of course.
#. column 40: I quite understand. We would be more than happy to abide by the original terms of the arrangement.
#. column 41: Thank you so very much! Please accept this additional payment with my compliments.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:33:0:38"
msgid "Ah, weren't you supposed to bring me something? Don't tell me you've forgotten...?"
msgstr "А разве вы не должны были что-то принести? Не говорите, что забыли…"

#. ja: うん、依頼どおりの仕事ぶりだね。<br>ところで、追加を頼みたいって言ったら……どうする？<br>もちろん報酬も、割増させてもらうよ。
#. de: Gute Arbeit. Hör mal, was würdest du sagen, wenn ich dir noch mehr abnehmen möchte? Ich würde natürlich auch dafür bezahlen.
#. fr: Oui, c'est bien ce qui était stipulé dans le mandat. Mais dites, ça vous embêterait de faire quelque chose en plus<nbsp>? Bien sûr, votre récompense sera majorée<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed the commission yet? I will be here, ready and waiting until you have.
#. column 37: Yes, this appears to fit the bill. No issues as far as I can see.
#. column 38: Ah, weren't you supposed to bring me something? Don't tell me you've forgotten...?
#. column 40: I quite understand. We would be more than happy to abide by the original terms of the arrangement.
#. column 41: Thank you so very much! Please accept this additional payment with my compliments.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:33:0:39"
msgid "Well done, well done. Though...if it's no imposition, could you bring us more? You would be duly compensated, of course."
msgstr "Отличная работа, отличная. Но… если вас не затруднит, не могли бы вы принести ещё? Разумеется, мы доплатим."

#. ja: そうかい、それならいいんだ。<br>最初に頼んだ仕事は、こなしてくれたんだからね！
#. de: Na gut, vielleicht ein anderes Mal. Dann bleibt es also bei unserer Absprache.
#. fr: Non<nbsp>? Ce n'est pas grave, puisque vous avez fait ce qu'on vous avait demandé initialement.
#. column 36: Have you completed the commission yet? I will be here, ready and waiting until you have.
#. column 37: Yes, this appears to fit the bill. No issues as far as I can see.
#. column 38: Ah, weren't you supposed to bring me something? Don't tell me you've forgotten...?
#. column 39: Well done, well done. Though...if it's no imposition, could you bring us more? You would be duly compensated, of course.
#. column 41: Thank you so very much! Please accept this additional payment with my compliments.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:33:0:40"
msgid "I quite understand. We would be more than happy to abide by the original terms of the arrangement."
msgstr "Понимаю. Тогда оставим всё как договаривались изначально."

#. ja: いい仕事っぷりだね！<br>さあ、約束通りに割りました報酬を受け取っておくれ！
#. de: Wirklich gute Arbeit. Auf dich ist Verlass. Hier ist deine Belohnung, wie versprochen.
#. fr: Oui, c'est parfait comme ça<nbsp>! Tenez, comme promis, voici votre récompense avec un petit supplément<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have you completed the commission yet? I will be here, ready and waiting until you have.
#. column 37: Yes, this appears to fit the bill. No issues as far as I can see.
#. column 38: Ah, weren't you supposed to bring me something? Don't tell me you've forgotten...?
#. column 39: Well done, well done. Though...if it's no imposition, could you bring us more? You would be duly compensated, of course.
#. column 40: I quite understand. We would be more than happy to abide by the original terms of the arrangement.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:33:0:41"
msgid "Thank you so very much! Please accept this additional payment with my compliments."
msgstr "Большое спасибо! Пожалуйста, примите эту доплату от меня."

#. ja: リーヴを引き受けてくださった漁師さんですね？<br>もう漁が済んだようでしたら、納品を受け付けますよ？
#. de: \<schnüff> \<schnüff> Du bist <if $gn4>Fischerin<else>Fischer</if>, nicht wahr? Wenn du einen Fang abgeben möchtest, bist du bei mir an der richtigen Stelle.
#. fr: C'est bien vous <if $gn4>la pêcheuse<else>le pêcheur</if> qui aviez accepté le mandat<nbsp>? Avez-vous attrrrapé ce qu'on vous avait demandé<nbsp>? Si oui, veuillez me remettre ça, s'il vous plaît<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Everything appears to be in order. Let me just prepare your payment...
#. column 38: Huh, this doesn't seem right. Are you sure you haven't forgotten something somewhere? No?
#. column 39: Thank you kindly. But before you go─mind tossing us a little extra? You'll be paid extra too for the trouble, mind.
#. column 40: Too busy, eh? Fair enough. Wasn't my intention to press.
#. column 41: Everything we asked for and then some. You're a peach. As promised, here's your bonus.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:34:0:36"
msgid "You're the fisher I was told to expect? Right, then. If you've got the goods, then let's have them."
msgstr "Вы тот рыбак, которого я ждал? Отлично. Если всё принесли, давайте сюда."

#. ja: 確かに、受け取りました。<br>それでは報酬をお支払いいたしましょう。
#. de: Das sieht doch lecker aus. Ich schick's direkt an die Küche. Aber zuerst gebe ich dir noch deine Belohnung.
#. fr: Oui, c'est bien ça<nbsp>! Tenez, voici la rrrécompense<nbsp>!
#. column 36: You're the fisher I was told to expect? Right, then. If you've got the goods, then let's have them.
#. column 38: Huh, this doesn't seem right. Are you sure you haven't forgotten something somewhere? No?
#. column 39: Thank you kindly. But before you go─mind tossing us a little extra? You'll be paid extra too for the trouble, mind.
#. column 40: Too busy, eh? Fair enough. Wasn't my intention to press.
#. column 41: Everything we asked for and then some. You're a peach. As promised, here's your bonus.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:34:0:37"
msgid "Everything appears to be in order. Let me just prepare your payment..."
msgstr "Всё вроде в порядке. Сейчас приготовлю вашу плату…"

#. ja: おや、足りないようですが……<br>漁場に置き去り、なんてことはないですよね？
#. de: Tja, kann es sein, dass du etwas an deinem Angelplatz liegen gelassen hast? Hier fehlt noch was.
#. fr: Attendez, mais ça ne suffit pas... Vous n'aurrriez pas oublié quelque chose sur le lieu de pêche<nbsp>?
#. column 36: You're the fisher I was told to expect? Right, then. If you've got the goods, then let's have them.
#. column 37: Everything appears to be in order. Let me just prepare your payment...
#. column 39: Thank you kindly. But before you go─mind tossing us a little extra? You'll be paid extra too for the trouble, mind.
#. column 40: Too busy, eh? Fair enough. Wasn't my intention to press.
#. column 41: Everything we asked for and then some. You're a peach. As promised, here's your bonus.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:34:0:38"
msgid "Huh, this doesn't seem right. Are you sure you haven't forgotten something somewhere? No?"
msgstr "Хм, что-то не так. Вы уверены, что ничего нигде не забыли? Нет?"

#. ja: 確かに、受け取りました。<br>ちなみに追加の依頼には、対応できたりしますか？<br>報酬を追加しますので、ご検討ください。
#. de: Vielen Dank. Eigentlich ... bräuchten wir noch mehr davon. Was sagst du? Ich würde natürlich etwas drauflegen.
#. fr: Oui, c'est bien ça<nbsp>! Mais dites, vous pensez que vous pourriez accepter une commande supplémentairrre<nbsp>? Bien sûr, la récompense serait conséquente<nbsp>!
#. column 36: You're the fisher I was told to expect? Right, then. If you've got the goods, then let's have them.
#. column 37: Everything appears to be in order. Let me just prepare your payment...
#. column 38: Huh, this doesn't seem right. Are you sure you haven't forgotten something somewhere? No?
#. column 40: Too busy, eh? Fair enough. Wasn't my intention to press.
#. column 41: Everything we asked for and then some. You're a peach. As promised, here's your bonus.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:34:0:39"
msgid "Thank you kindly. But before you go─mind tossing us a little extra? You'll be paid extra too for the trouble, mind."
msgstr "Спасибо. Но прежде чем уйдёте… не принесёте ли ещё немного? За хлопоты, конечно, доплатим."

#. ja: おや、忙しいのですか……？<br>とはいえ、無理にお願いすることもできませんね。
#. de: Du hast wohl auch noch andere Dinge zu erledigen, was? Einverstanden, vielleicht ein anderes Mal.
#. fr: Je vois... J'imagine que vous avez d'autrrres engagements à tenir. Je ne vais pas insister alors.
#. column 36: You're the fisher I was told to expect? Right, then. If you've got the goods, then let's have them.
#. column 37: Everything appears to be in order. Let me just prepare your payment...
#. column 38: Huh, this doesn't seem right. Are you sure you haven't forgotten something somewhere? No?
#. column 39: Thank you kindly. But before you go─mind tossing us a little extra? You'll be paid extra too for the trouble, mind.
#. column 41: Everything we asked for and then some. You're a peach. As promised, here's your bonus.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:34:0:40"
msgid "Too busy, eh? Fair enough. Wasn't my intention to press."
msgstr "Заняты, да? Понимаю. Я не хотел настаивать."

#. ja: ありがとうございます。<br>追加依頼も含めて、ばっちりです。<br>報酬にも色を付けさせていただきますよ！
#. de: Das wäre dann alles, einschließlich der Nachbestellung. Hier, wie abgemacht habe ich die Belohnung erhöht.
#. fr: Parrrfait<nbsp>! Tenez, voici la récompense augmentée, comme je vous l'avais dit<nbsp>! Merci pour votre travail<nbsp>!
#. column 36: You're the fisher I was told to expect? Right, then. If you've got the goods, then let's have them.
#. column 37: Everything appears to be in order. Let me just prepare your payment...
#. column 38: Huh, this doesn't seem right. Are you sure you haven't forgotten something somewhere? No?
#. column 39: Thank you kindly. But before you go─mind tossing us a little extra? You'll be paid extra too for the trouble, mind.
#. column 40: Too busy, eh? Fair enough. Wasn't my intention to press.
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:34:0:41"
msgid "Everything we asked for and then some. You're a peach. As promised, here's your bonus."
msgstr "Всё, что мы просили, да ещё и сверх того. Вы просто прелесть. Вот обещанная надбавка."

#. ja: 依頼した品は出来上がったのか？<br>完成したら、この窓口に持ってきてくれ。
#. de: Hast du mitgebracht, wofür du beauftragt wurdest?<br>Falls ja, kannst du es hier abgeben.
#. fr: Passez au guichet dès que vous aurez ce que l'on vous a commandé.
#. column 37: Aye, this will do nicely. Here is your payment, as agreed.
#. column 38: If you've nothing for me, might I suggest getting back to work? Our clients are growing impatient.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:35:0:36"
msgid "Have a delivery for me, do you? Well, let's have it, then."
msgstr "У вас для меня заказ? Ну-ка, показывайте."

#. ja: 見事なもんだ。<br>依頼通りの品だと確認したぜ！
#. de: Das sieht großartig aus.<br>Genau, was für die Lieferung gefordert wurde!
#. fr: Parfait<nbsp>! Exactement ce qui nous a été commandé<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Have a delivery for me, do you? Well, let's have it, then.
#. column 38: If you've nothing for me, might I suggest getting back to work? Our clients are growing impatient.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:35:0:37"
msgid "Aye, this will do nicely. Here is your payment, as agreed."
msgstr "Да, сойдёт. Вот ваша плата, как и договаривались."

#. ja: おいおい、作った品を忘れてきたのか？<br>依頼した品が見当たらないようだが……。
#. de: He, willst du mich veräppeln? Du musst schon was liefern, wenn du die Belohnung abgreifen willst.
#. fr: Notre commande ne se trouve pas dans vos affaires<nbsp>? Me dites pas que vous avez oublié de la mettre dans votre baluchon avant de venir...
#. column 36: Have a delivery for me, do you? Well, let's have it, then.
#. column 37: Aye, this will do nicely. Here is your payment, as agreed.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:35:0:38"
msgid "If you've nothing for me, might I suggest getting back to work? Our clients are growing impatient."
msgstr "Если вам нечего мне показать, советую вернуться к работе. Клиенты уже теряют терпение."

#. ja: 仕事を引き受けてくれて、ありがとね！<br>漁が終わったら、忘れずに納品しておくれよ！
#. de: Du bist <if $gn4>Fischerin<else>Fischer</if>, nicht wahr? Wusste ich's doch! Man sieht es dir gleich an. Vergiss nicht deinen Fang bei mir abzugeben, wenn du was Gutes geangelt hast!
#. fr: Merci pour votre aide<nbsp>! N'oubliez pas de nous livrer la commande quand vous reviendrez de votre pêche. Ce serait dommage qu'elle pourrisse dans votre sac<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Well, well! Seems you're every bit the fisher they said you were. All right, then. Here's your reward.
#. column 38: If you're expectin' compensation, I'm afraid you'll need to bring in the agreed upon fish.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:36:0:36"
msgid "I was told a master angler'd be makin' a delivery of fish soon. I take it that's you?"
msgstr "Мне сказали, что скоро рыбак-мастер принесёт улов. Это вы?"

#. ja: バッチリだね！<br>頼れる漁師には、相応の支払いをしなくっちゃ！<br>さあ、受け取っておくれ！
#. de: Was für ein Prachtexemplar!<br>Sehr gut. Hier, deine Belohnung. Sollst ja nicht umsonst arbeiten.
#. fr: Belle prise<nbsp>! Tenez, les pros de la pêche comme vous méritent une belle récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 36: I was told a master angler'd be makin' a delivery of fish soon. I take it that's you?
#. column 38: If you're expectin' compensation, I'm afraid you'll need to bring in the agreed upon fish.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:36:0:37"
msgid "Well, well! Seems you're every bit the fisher they said you were. All right, then. Here's your reward."
msgstr "Ну надо же! Вы и правда такой рыбак, как о вас говорили. Вот ваша награда."

#. ja: ええっと、頼んでおいたものはどこだい？<br>もう一度、確認してみておくれよ。
#. de: Äh, hast du nicht irgendwas vergessen? Gewöhnlich mit Schuppen und Kiemen versehen und so?<br>Ohne Fleiß kein Preis!
#. fr: Euh... Croyez-le ou pas, votre prise s'est fait la malle... À moins que vous l'ayez oubliée<nbsp>?
#. column 36: I was told a master angler'd be makin' a delivery of fish soon. I take it that's you?
#. column 37: Well, well! Seems you're every bit the fisher they said you were. All right, then. Here's your reward.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:36:0:38"
msgid "If you're expectin' compensation, I'm afraid you'll need to bring in the agreed upon fish."
msgstr "Если ждёте плату, придётся сначала принести обещанную рыбу."

#. ja: お願いしていた品は完成しましたか？<br>作り終わったら、こちらへお持ちくださいね。
#. de: Möchtest du eine Bestellung abliefern? Ich nehme alles entgegen, was fertig ist.
#. fr: Si vous avez rempli la commande pour le mandat que vous avez accepté, n'oubliez pas de me l'apporter<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Wonderful work. The client will be thrilled, I'm sure.
#. column 38: Lost it in your bag, you say? Worry not─I will be here whenever you're ready.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:37:0:36"
msgid "I can accept any crafted commissions you may have."
msgstr "Я приму любые изделия, которые вы изготовили по заказу."

#. ja: まあ、見事な出来栄えですね。<br>依頼の品、たしかに受領いたしました。
#. de: Ja, das sieht nach ordentlicher Arbeit aus. Damit ist dein Auftrag abgeschlossen.
#. fr: C'est en tous points conforme aux conditions du mandat. Vous avez bien mérité votre récompense<nbsp>!
#. column 36: I can accept any crafted commissions you may have.
#. column 38: Lost it in your bag, you say? Worry not─I will be here whenever you're ready.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:37:0:37"
msgid "Wonderful work. The client will be thrilled, I'm sure."
msgstr "Чудесная работа. Клиент будет в восторге, я уверен."

#. ja: 依頼の品が見当たらないようですが……。<br>お荷物を検めてみてください。
#. de: Hm, das scheint nicht das Richtige zu sein. Hast du dich etwa vertan? Bitte sieh doch noch einmal nach.
#. fr: Apparemment, vous n'avez aucun article correspondant... Je vous laisse le soin de mettre de l'ordre dans vos affaires.
#. column 36: I can accept any crafted commissions you may have.
#. column 37: Wonderful work. The client will be thrilled, I'm sure.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:37:0:38"
msgid "Lost it in your bag, you say? Worry not─I will be here whenever you're ready."
msgstr "Потеряли в сумке? Не волнуйтесь, я буду здесь, когда будете готовы."

#. ja: やあ、漁師さん！<br>リーヴの納品だったら、ここで承るよ！
#. de: Na, willst du etwas abliefern? Immer her damit!
#. fr: Vous devez être <if $gn4>la pêcheuse<else>le pêcheur</if> qui avait accepté le mandat<nbsp>? Remettez-moi donc votre prise, si vous l'avez apportée<nbsp>!
#. column 37: Perfect! Just what we were hopin' for. Take this, with our compliments.
#. column 38: Forgot your fish? Now that's embarrassin'... Better luck next time, eh?
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:38:0:36"
msgid "Hallo, friend! Have any fish for me?"
msgstr "Здорово, друг! Есть для меня рыбка?"

#. ja: 頼んでいたもので間違いないようだね！<br>お仕事おつかれさま、報酬をどうぞ！
#. de: Ja, das sieht doch genau richtig aus! Hier, nimm das als kleine Anerkennung.
#. fr: C'est ef<shy>fec<shy>ti<shy>ve<shy>ment une très belle prise<nbsp>! Vous méritez une récompense à sa hauteur<nbsp>!
#. column 36: Hallo, friend! Have any fish for me?
#. column 38: Forgot your fish? Now that's embarrassin'... Better luck next time, eh?
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:38:0:37"
msgid "Perfect! Just what we were hopin' for. Take this, with our compliments."
msgstr "Отлично! Именно то, что нужно. Вот, возьмите — с наилучшими пожеланиями."

#. ja: あれ、頼んでいたものがないようだけど……。<br>うっかり忘れてきちゃったのかな？
#. de: Sag bloß, du warst in Gedanken ganz woanders und hast vergessen, warum du hergekommen bist!
#. fr: Hum... Rien ne correspond dans votre besace... Vous n'avez pas relâché votre prise par mégarde<nbsp>?
#. column 36: Hallo, friend! Have any fish for me?
#. column 37: Perfect! Just what we were hopin' for. Take this, with our compliments.
#. column 39: 0
#. column 40: 0
#. column 41: 0
msgctxt "CraftLeveTalk:38:0:38"
msgid "Forgot your fish? Now that's embarrassin'... Better luck next time, eh?"
msgstr "Забыли рыбу? Ну и неловко… В следующий раз повезёт, а?"
